      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Search Jobs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Search  Postings (134) Hide Search Options View all open Postings below, or enter search criteria to narrow your search. Keywords Posted Within Any time period Last Day Last Week Last Month Position Type No Selection NFE CSA Faculty Temp Position Title Institution No Selection Black Hills State University Board of Regents Dakota State University Northern State University SD School f/t Blind & VI SD Services f/t Deaf South Dakota Mines South Dakota State University The University of South Dakota Posting Number City No Selection Unspecified Aberdeen Alexandria Armour Belle Fourche Beresford Bison Britton Brookings Buffalo Burke Canton Chamberlain Clark Clear Lake Crow Creek Custer Dakota Valley De Smet Dupree Eagle Butte Elk Point Ellsworth Base Faulkton Flandreau Forestburg Fort Pierre Gettysburg Gregory Hayti Highmore Hot Springs Howard Huron Ipswich Kadoka Kennebec Lake Andes Lead Leola Lemmon Madison Martin Mc Intosh Milbank Miller Mission Mitchell Mound City Murdo Olivet Onida Parker Philip Pierre Pine Ridge Plankinton Porcupine Rapid City Redfield Salem Selby Sioux Falls Sisseton Spearfish Sturgis Tea Timber Lake Tyndall Vermillion Watertown Webster Wessington Springs White River Winner Woonsocket Yankton Previous 1 2 3 4 5 Next View Results (134\n    ) Job Title Posting Number Department Position Type Job Close Date Assistant Coach-Softball NFE03191P USD-Intercollegiate Athletics NFE The University of South Dakota Assistant Softball Coach – Pitching is responsible for assisting the head coach in all aspects of managing a NCAA Division I softball program including but not limited to: recruitment, development and everyday training of all members of a pitching staff; assisting with training and development in other areas of team/players on and off the field; liaison for academ... View Details Bookmark Training and Development Coordinator NFE03192P USD-Human Resources NFE The University of South Dakota is seeking a Training and Development Coordinator to help build and deliver a comprehensive employee training and development program that supports faculty, staff, supervisors, managers, and institutional leaders. This is an exciting opportunity to join a forward-thinking Human Resources team and play a key role in advancing employee growth, leadership development... View Details Bookmark Alumni Relations Officer NFE03105P DSU-Institutional Advancement NFE Dakota State University is seeking an enthusiastic and creative Alumni Relations Officer to join our team. This is an excellent role for a professional who is ready to make an impact by supporting alumni engagement and strengthening lifelong relationships between graduates and DSU. Responsibilities:Develop, plan, and implement engaging alumni events and programs that connect former students wit... View Details Bookmark Facilities Services Supervisor I CSA02821P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications a full-time Facilities Services Supervisor I. This position will work an 8 hour shift Monday through Friday with some weekends as needed to help with preparation/clean-up for events on campus. The hours will be 4:00am-12:30pmResponsibilities Include:General cleaning of an academic building.Floor care mainly vacuuming and mopping but could include ... View Details Bookmark Facility Worker CSA02820P DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt CSA Dakota State University is seeking applications for a full-time facility worker. Primary responsibilities include custodial care and minor maintenance at the Community Center.The position will be scheduled Monday through Friday from 10pm to 6:30am. Responsibilities:Floor care will be daily vacuuming, scrubbing and mopping, occasional carpet shampooing and floor waxing.Clean and sanitize restroo... View Details Bookmark Program Assistant II (4-H Educator) Meade County CSA02819P SDSU-4-H Programs CSA 09/30/2026 Do you want to inspire and empower the next generation of South Dakota leaders? At South Dakota State University (SDSU) 4-H Programs, we are dedicated to providing youth with supportive adults, hands-on learning experiences, and opportunities to reach their full potential. We’re seeking a collaborative, people-focused professional who is passionate about mentoring, guiding, and helping others g... View Details Bookmark Financial Program Assistant CSA02818P SDSU-Facilities & Services-Customer Service Ctr CSA 09/18/2026 South Dakota State University’s Facilities & Services Department is seeking a Financial Program Assistant to support essential financial and operational services across campus. This multifaceted role combines accounts payable, purchasing, mail services, and warehouse support, making it an excellent opportunity for an organized and detail-oriented professional looking to make a campus-wide i... View Details Bookmark Custodial Services Supervisor I CSA02609P SDSU-University Housing CSA 09/17/2026 South Dakota State University (SDSU) Student Life Building Services is looking for a motivated individual to join our team as a Custodial Services Supervisor within University Housing and Residential Life.This position is located in Brookings.Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.Job Responsibilities:This position plans, coordinates and directs th... View Details Bookmark Accountant CSA02817P USD-Accounting Services CSA USD is seeking an energetic, creative problem solver, and strategic thinker to fill an open Accountant position. The individual hired must be able to interpret, analyze, and determine accuracy of financial data in the maintenance of controlling funds. Individual must be able to provide exceptional customer service and interpret USD and State of SD policies and procedures.Specific tasks will inc... View Details Bookmark Vice President for Research and Economic Development NFE03147P SDSU-Division of Research & Econ Dvlp NFE South Dakota State University (SDState) invites applications and nominations to serve as its next Vice President for Research and Economic Development (VPRED). The university seeks a visionary, dynamic, and strategic leader to lead our research strategy, fostering innovation, economic development, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Reporting directly to the President and serving on the univer... View Details Bookmark Assistant Athletic Trainer NFE03190P SDSU-Intercollegiate Athletics NFE South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an Assistant Athletic Trainer to join our team. This role supports the coordination of athletic training services, ensuring the health and well-being of our student-athletes. From injury prevention and evaluation to rehabilitation and return-to-play management, this position plays a vital role in keeping athletes performing at their best. We’re... View Details Bookmark Facility Worker CSA02755P SDSMT-Facilities Management CSA LOCATION: Facilities ManagementStarting Hourly Rate: $17.10 + per hour, depending upon education and experience, GCPOSITION PURPOSE: Performs a variety of cleaning and maintenance procedures to ensure sanitary conditions are met. Duties will include maintaining hard surface floors, including sweeping, mopping, and refinishing; maintaining carpets, including vacuuming and shampooing; cleaning an... View Details Bookmark Outreach & Event Coordinator CSA02785P SDSMT-Marketing & Communications CSA LOCATION: Marketing & CommunicationsSTARTING HOURLY RATE: $21.41-$23.99 hourly, depending upon education and experience, GGPosition Summary:Support South Dakota Mines’ public image and K-12 education pipeline by planning and executing public relations and K-12-focused events, and by developing community and K-12 outreach efforts that connect prospective students with Mines resources.Duties ... View Details Bookmark Licensed Provider QE8537 NFE03189P USD-Center for Disabilities NFE This position may provide training, technical assistance, and clinical services to professionals and families in establishing evidence-based interventions for individuals with developmental disabilities. The position may be responsible for the coordination, information dissemination, and implementation of professional development training opportunities and may also coordinate other training eve... View Details Bookmark Speech-Language Pathologist F01943P USD-Communication Sciences & Disorders Faculty The University of South Dakota invites applications for a full-time, ten or eleven-month Speech-Language Pathologist position based in Sioux Falls within the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders.Qualifications:Master’s degree in speech-language pathology.Ability to provide clinical education and supervision.Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as an SLP.Possession of or eligi... View Details Bookmark HR Program Assistant II CSA02816P SDSU-Human Resources CSA 09/23/2026 South Dakota State University (SDState) is actively seeking a highly dedicated, people-centered Human Resource professional to join our team! Be a part of a dynamic team and provide exceptional customer service to the campus community. We are hiring for four HR Program Assistant II positions.  This position is located in Brookings, South Dakota.  Must be authorized to work in the U.S.  Sponsors... View Details Bookmark Information Specialist CSA02815P SDSU- Animal Science CSA 09/18/2026 South Dakota State University (SDState) is currently seeking an Information Specialist to join our Animal Science department. This position will play a critical role in the department’s three primary missions which are learning, discovery, and engagement. If you have a strong attention to detail and excellent writing, editing and proofreading skills then this position may be for you!Tomorrow’s ... View Details Bookmark Instructor of Communication Studies F01942P NSU-Arts & Sciences Faculty Position Summary: The Department of English, Communication, and Global Languages at Northern State University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Instructor of Communication Studies. This instructor-rank position offers the opportunity to shape the foundational communication and first-year experience of NSU students through engaged teaching and active involvement in departmen... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of History F01941P NSU-History Faculty Position Summary: The Department of History and Social Sciences at Northern State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of History. This position offers the opportunity to teach and mentor students in Early American History through the Civil War era while contributing to the department’s research culture and to university life more broadly. The antici... View Details Bookmark Carpenter - Senior Building Maintenance Worker CSA02814P SDSU-Facilities & Services-Bldg Maint CSA South Dakota State University is seeking a skilled and highly motivated Carpenter – Senior Building Maintenance Worker to join our Facilities and Services team. This position is ideal for an individual who takes pride in quality craftsmanship, enjoys hands-on work, and is committed to maintaining and improving the university’s facilities. This position is located in Brookings, South Dakota.Faci... View Details Bookmark Program Assistant I CSA02771P SDSU-Undergraduate Nursing CSA 09/22/2026 Join the college of Nursing as a Program Assistant I and become an essential member of our Undergraduate Nursing team. We’re seeking a detail oriented and service focused professional who enjoys supporting students, faculty, and staff while helping ensure the smooth operation of our academic programs. This position is located in Rapid City, South Dakota.The College of Nursing has a long history... View Details Bookmark Custodial Services Supervisor I CSA02813P USD-Custodial Services CSA The Custodial Services department within USD Facilities Management is seeking a Custodial Supervisor I. This position is responsible for supervising and coordinating the activities of approximately 30 custodial personnel to maintain and provide quality custodial services for our campus facilities in Vermillion, SD. This person will be responsible for the presentation and cleanliness of our acad... View Details Bookmark Assistant Coach, Triathlon NFE03188P BHSU-Intercolleg Athletics NFE Black Hills State University is seeking applicants for an Assistant Triathlon Coach in the Athletics department.DUTIES:• Manage the day-to-day practice and skill development of student athletes, practice planning, and recruitment of student athletes. They will also oversee the strength and performance of the team.• Assist with management and administration of Triathlon Team• Assist the head coa... View Details Bookmark StoreKeeper CSA02812P SDSU-Facilities & Services-Customer Service Ctr CSA 09/08/2026 South Dakota State University (SDSU) is searching for a Storekeeper who will be responsible for processing all incoming and outgoing U.S. and campus mail, as well as delivering mail, packages, and warehouse materials across campus. Manages all shipping and receiving activities for items entering and leaving the central warehouse. Supports mail-related accounts payable functions and assists with... View Details Bookmark Building Maintenance Specialist CSA02811P SDSU-Facilities & Services-Energy Systems CSA The Facilities & Services department of South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an experienced boiler operator to be a part of the team in the heating plant. Responsibilities include operating and maintaining the campus heating plant to ensure reliable heat and hot water delivery to approximately 80% of SDSU campus. Ensures boilers run at optimal efficiency with minimal environme... View Details Bookmark Family & Community Health Educator CSA02810P SDSU-Food & Families Programs-Ext CSA 09/21/2026 South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking multiple Family & Community Health Educators. These positions improve the health and well-being of South Dakotans by delivering evidence-based health education programs, supporting behavior change, and connecting individuals with resources that promote healthy lifestyles and chronic disease self-management. This position is grant funded, co... View Details Bookmark Admissions Counselor NFE03187P USD-Admissions NFE The University of South Dakota Office of Admissions is seeking an energetic, goal-oriented, self-motivated individual for the position of Admissions Counselor. Responsibilities include, territory management, marketing and recruitment activities on and off campus, assist in financial aid as necessary, database management, counseling prospective students and families, contributing to overall enro... View Details Bookmark Facility Worker CSA02809P SDSU-Facilities & Services-Custodial Svc CSA 09/14/2026 SDSU Facilities & Services is in search of motivated and dependable individuals to join our cleaning team as Facility Workers. No prior professional cleaning experience is needed. You bring your willingness to learn, and we will equip you with all the training and tools to complete the job. This position is located in Brookings, South Dakota. Must be authorized to work in the U.S.  Sponsors... View Details Bookmark CBE Research Scientist IV NFE03174P SDSMT-Karen M. Swindler Chemical and Biological Engineering 1 NFE The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at South Dakota Mines is seeking applications for a Research Scientist IV, benefited position at 100% effort. This position will be responsible for designing and executing experimental research, advising student researchers, disseminating research findings through peer-reviewed publications and scientific conference present... View Details Bookmark Senior Building Maintenance Worker CSA02808P SDSMT-Facilities Management CSA LOCATION: FacilitiesSTARTING HOURLY RATE: Minimum of $18.45+ per hour, depending upon education and experience, GEPOSITION PURPOSE: Responsible for paint and wall repair in remodeling and renovation projects including painting walls, ceilings, metal doors and frames.. General maintenance duties include basic plumbing work on drains, faucets, etc. installing light bulbs and shelves; moving furni... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 Next The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
