      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Job Alert Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Job Alerts Indicate which categories you are interested in, and select Subscribe to\n      begin receiving notifications when new Postings\n      are open to applications. Email * First Name * Last Name * Select All Clear All Academic Affairs Admissions/Registrar Agriculture Athletics Buildings/Custodial/Facilities/Grounds Maintenance Business/Economics Communications/Marketing/Public Relations Development/Fundraising/Alumni Affairs Education/Teaching/Advising Engineering Enrollment Services Event and Conference Services Executive Administrative Assistant/Senior Secretary/Secretary Extension Faculty: Agriculture/Food/Animal/Plant Science Faculty: Arts/Humanities/Social Services Faculty: Business Faculty: Communications Faculty: Computer Game Design Faculty: Computer Science Faculty: Cyber Sciences Faculty: Education/Human Sciences Faculty: Engineering Faculty: Health Information Management Faculty: Information Systems Faculty: Mathematics Faculty: Natural Sciences Faculty: Physics Finance/Accounting/Budget Financial Aid Fitness/Health/Wellness Healthcare Professions Hospitality Human Resources/Payroll International/Cultural Engagement Internships K-12 Faculty/Teachers K-12 Outreach Laboratory Legal Library Mail Services Management/Administration Media/Design Medicine Natural Sciences Nursing Office & Administrative Support Performing Arts/Fine Arts Pharmacy Print Services Public Safety Research Scientist/ Post-Doc Researcher Research/Grants Skilled Trades (Plumbing, HVAC, Electrical) Social Sciences Student Affairs Student Life (Residence Life, Student Success Center, Student Activities, Counseling, Career, Disability Services, and Professional Development, Bookstore) Technology/Information Technology/Data Processing Temporary Positions Title IX Tutoring Veterans Services The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
