    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "South Dakota Board Of Regents: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:yourfuture.sdbor.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs South Dakota Board Of Regents: All Jobs 2026-07-09T16:01:52-05:00 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48935 2026-07-09T16:01:51-05:00 2026-07-09T16:01:52-05:00 Foster Care Licensing and Placement Specialist <div>The Center for the Prevention of Child Maltreatment (CPCM) at the University of South Dakota is seeking a highly organized and mission-driven Foster Care Licensing and Placement Specialist to help children in need find safe, supportive foster care homes.<br><br>In this full-time role, you will work closely with the Department of Social Services and a distributed CPCM team to facilitate placement requests and match children with foster families who meet their needs. You’ll use your problem-solving skills, quick judgment, and strong communication to facilitate timely placements, while maintaining detailed documentation and ensuring compliance with all state requirements. This position is perfect for someone who thrives in fast-paced work environments and finds meaning in supporting vulnerable children and families. You will also help recruit, license, and retain foster care families in South Dakota.<br><br>As a Foster Care Licensing and Placement Specialist you will:</div><ul><li>Coordinate timely and effective foster care placements, ensuring that each child is matched with a home that considers sibling bonds, cultural context, proximity, and special needs.</li><li>Maintain clear, ongoing communication and strong collaborative relationships with DSS Child Protective Services, DSS Office of Licensing &amp; Accreditation, foster families, and fellow CPCM team members.</li><li>Assist with recruitment, support, licensure, and retention of foster and potential adoptive families.</li><li>Accurately track, document, and report licensure and placement-related data, meeting DSS and OLA compliance requirements.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Undergraduate degree in social work, psychology, sociology, public administration, or other human service-related fields&nbsp;</li><li>1-3 years of related experience</li><li>Strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills</li><li>Experience with social services, family support systems, and office processes and databases</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>This role requires:</strong></div><ul><li>Sustained mental focus, rapid response, and excellent organizational skills.</li><li>Excellent in-person, virtual, and written communication skills</li><li>Ability to travel frequently in-state and work some evening and weekend hours</li><li>Ability to work in both an office setting and in a variety of home settings</li><li>Empathy, adaptability, and a commitment to timely, accurate data management.</li><li>Flexibility to adjust quickly to shifting tasks and priorities.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Join CPCM’s collaborative, purpose-driven team and help ensure every child is matched with a home where they can be safe, supported, and thriving. CPCM fosters a work culture grounded in collaboration, continuous learning and improvement, and community impact. Hybrid work options are available.</div><div><br>This position offers state health insurance and benefits, which includes a retirement plan with 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and 11 paid holidays.<br><br>Candidates must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br>Apply today and make a meaningful impact in the lives of children and families across South Dakota.</div> USD-Ctr Prevention of Child Maltreatment https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49523 2026-08-25T13:28:41-05:00 2026-08-25T13:28:42-05:00 MBM Pillar 3 Director <div>The University of South Dakota Sanford School of Medicine is seeking a dedicated individual to be the Pillar 3 Director. This position coordinates curriculum and guides students in their academic programs. Pillar 3 occupies the final sixteen months of medical school when students complete required clerkships (sub-internship, emergency medicine, surgery sub-specialties, rural family medicine), electives, and interview for residencies. These clerkships may be located at Rapid City, Sioux Falls, or Yankton, as well as at out-of-state or international locations.<br><br><strong>POSITION SUMMARY:</strong><br><br></div><div>The Pillar 3 Director coordinates curriculum and guides students in their academic programs.<br><br></div><div><strong>1. Develop, implement and maintain high-quality curricula in Pillar 3 to expand clinical learning opportunities, and to provide training in important and emerging areas, e.g., preparation for residency, Quality/Safety. (40%)</strong></div><ul><li>Develop and implement new curriculum in Pillar 3 to expand opportunities for students</li><li>Mentor faculty in required Pillar 3 courses, e.g. sub-internships and in the development of electives</li><li>Bring new course proposals to the Medical Education Committee</li><li>Explore options to offer distinction opportunities including micro credentialing and certificates</li><li>Lead development of the Medical Accelerated Program in partnership with the residencies</li></ul><div><strong>2. Collaborate with the associate deans of medical education and medical student affairs and registration officer on Pillar 3 curricular programs. (30%)</strong></div><ul><li>Collaborate in the implementation and maintenance of online Pillar 3 scheduling</li><li>Develop and enforce policies for away electives</li><li>Participate in sessions for Pillar 2 students on Pillar 3 course selection and preparation for residency application</li><li>Run clinical competency committee meetings and track students on monitored academic status</li></ul><div><strong>3. Collaborate with the Office of Medical Education to assure programs meet accreditation requirements. (15%)</strong></div><ul><li>Work with director of evaluation and assessment to monitor course requirements, evaluation data, timeliness of grades, and duty hours violations</li><li>Provide regular reports to the Medical Education Committee and Clerkship Directors Committee</li><li>Serve on the Medical Education Committee Integration Subcommittee</li><li>Provide documentation when requested as part of continuous quality improvement for accreditation</li></ul><div><strong>4. Collaborate with clinical departments and clerkship directors in coordinating required clerkships and electives. (10%)</strong></div><ul><li>Develop, implement, and oversee the processes of collecting student grades and reporting grades to the registrar in a timely manner</li><li>Attend the clinical department assistants monthly meeting</li><li>Attend the clerkship directors monthly meeting</li></ul><div><strong>5. Coordinate the Transition to Residency [TTR] course. (5%)</strong></div><div><br><strong>Curriculum Development:</strong></div><ul><li>Attend relevant conferences and symposia relevant to curriculum development in transition to residency</li><li>Support specialty-specific curricular opportunities for students throughout the week</li><li>Work with Parry Center to coordinate ‘Night on Call’ simulation experiences for students during Pillar 3</li><li>Review Program Director feedback on students’ residency preparedness to identify important themes to touch on during course</li></ul><div><strong>Precepting:</strong></div><ul><li>Precept small group and large group sessions the week of the course</li><li>Coordinate daily paging simulation experience and debriefs</li></ul><div><strong>Evaluation and Assessment:</strong></div><ul><li>Identify mechanisms for giving students feedback on their readiness for residency</li><li>Determine how students are assessed and assigning grades for the course</li><li>Review student feedback on the TTR course and make changes as appropriate</li></ul><div><strong>Communication/Coordination:</strong></div><ul><li>Work with Pillar 3 assistant to recruit and schedule faculty for lecture and small group sessions (Morning Report, Journal Club)</li><li>Develop relevant clinical skills sessions</li><li>Coordinate sessions with faculty specialists in the area of Financial Wellness</li></ul><div><br></div><h1><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h1><ul><li>MD/DO with current SD Licensure or ability to obtain one and appropriate certification for field of specialty.</li><li>Leadership experience in a medical school or similar environment.</li><li>Experience in student services in an academic environment is preferable.</li></ul><div><br>This position reports to Dr. Amy Prunuske, PhD, Associate Dean of Medical Student Education.</div> SSOM - Medical Education https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49278 2026-08-04T13:43:53-05:00 2026-08-04T13:43:54-05:00 Pre-School Teacher <div><strong>USD Head Start is seeking a passionate and dedicated Center Teacher to join our preschool team in Vermillion, SD.</strong><br>In this role, you’ll guide a classroom of 16 children ages 3–5, helping them build the social, emotional, and early academic skills that set the foundation for lifelong learning.</div><div><strong><br>What You’ll Do</strong></div><ul><li>Lead a preschool classroom of 16 children</li><li>Create a nurturing, developmentally appropriate learning environment</li><li>Support each child’s growth through engaging activities and individualized attention</li><li>Build strong relationships with families and collaborate with a supportive team</li></ul><div><strong><br>Position Details</strong></div><ul><li>Full‑time, 40 hours per week</li><li>9.5‑month schedule (August 15 – May 31)</li><li>Located in Tea, South Dakota</li><li>Eligible for the full State of South Dakota benefits package</li></ul><div><strong><br>Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>BA in Early Childhood Education, Education with Early Childhood Endorsement,Special Education with Early Childhood specialization</li><li>Experience working with young children</li></ul><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong></div><div>This position includes the comprehensive State of South Dakota benefits package:</div><ul><li>Health insurance</li><li>Paid annual and sick leave</li><li>Paid holidays</li><li>Matching contributions to the South Dakota Retirement System (SDRS)</li></ul> USD-Head Start https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49651 2026-09-03T12:25:07-05:00 2026-09-03T12:25:08-05:00 Vice President for Research and Economic Development <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) invites applications and nominations to serve as its next Vice President for Research and Economic Development (VPRED). The university seeks a visionary, dynamic, and strategic leader to lead our research strategy, fostering innovation, economic development, and interdisciplinary collaboration.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Reporting directly to the President and serving on the university's executive leadership team, the VPRED serves as the Chief Research Officer. The VPRED oversees all sponsored programs, research integrity, regulatory compliance, technology transfer, and economic development partnerships.<br><br>This is an exciting opportunity to continue to build on the current momentum, leading SDState's efforts to expand its research enterprise while driving the economic vitality of South Dakota and the region. SDState seeks an innovative leader with vision and strong leadership skills, who establishes collaborative relationships, fosters an environment in which faculty and stakeholders are engaged partners and communicates consistently and effectively.&nbsp;<br><br>The position’s anticipated start date is January 4, 2027.<br><br></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Develop and implement strategies to increase external funding, research, and creative activities across all disciplines;</li><li>Develop and execute the university research strategic plan and agenda to include setting and implementing the vision for research and creative activities, aiming for growth in research expenditures (e.g., aiming to attain R1 status and high-level research funding);</li><li>Provide effective engagement with federal legislative and administrative entities by representing SDSU in relationship building with South Dakota’s Congressional delegation and leading SDSU engagement with federal agencies;</li><li>Identify and promote research competitiveness by supporting faculty in securing external funding and managing internal funding opportunities;</li><li>Support faculty in securing grants and contracts through the Office of Sponsored Programs, as well as through collaboration with the University Research Council;</li><li>Establish partnerships and engage with state, regional and national partners, including industry leaders, businesses, state and federal government officials, and national policymakers to strengthen economic development and research funding;</li><li>Lead and facilitate university relationship development with the private sector, both at organizational level and at the expertise level;</li><li>Manage the full life cycle of intellectual property (IP), from invention disclosure to patenting, licensing, and collaboration with the Office of General Counsel;</li><li>Lead and assure university intellectual property identification, protection and management; and</li><li>Oversee the Division of Research and Economic Development, including recruiting, supervising, coaching and evaluating personnel;</li><li>Lead research compliance and safety by ensuring adherence to policies regarding research integrity, including IRB, IACUC, and export controls; and</li><li>Manage research space and ensure compliance with safety and research integrity regulations.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>About the University</strong></div><div>As the state's largest land-grant institution, SDState has experienced transformational research growth with research expenditures growing 47% to a record $94 million, and doctoral enrollment expanding significantly to position SDState closer to Research 1 (R1) classification.</div><div><br></div><div>South Dakota State University is the state’s largest, most comprehensive higher education institution. As South Dakota’s Morrill Act land-grant university, SDState had a fall 2025 enrollment of 12,139, with students coming from 48 states and 78 countries. Students can choose from 90 majors, 35 specializations, 107 minors, 39 master’s degree programs, 17 Ph.D. programs and 2 professional doctorates. The university also offers courses at various off-campus sites as well as undergraduate and graduate programs online through the Office of Continuing and Distance Education. The university is governed by the South Dakota Board of Regents, which also has oversight of South Dakota’s five additional universities within a unified system.<br><br></div><div>From its roots as a land-grant university, committed to the creation of knowledge and educating all, established in Brookings, South Dakota in 1881, South Dakota State University today is a vibrant institution. SDState is South Dakota’s first High Research Activity institution as classified by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. It competes in Division I athletics and is a member of the Big 12 conference for wrestling, the Missouri Valley Football Conference, and the Summit League for all other sports.<br><br></div><div>With exceptional alumni, community, and Foundation support for student scholarships and all aspects of university life, SDState is the center of life in Brookings, a friendly and economically healthy community of nearly 24,000. Brookings has outstanding schools, strong local economic research and development efforts, lovely parks, museums and well-attended cultural activities. The university fosters close working relationships with local school districts, and there is a kindergarten on campus. Located one hour’s drive north of Sioux Falls, the state’s largest city, SDState and Brookings offer a very high quality of life in an engaged, active campus community. It is also notable that the state of South Dakota has no personal income tax. Learn more about Brookings by visiting <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IT8OnH5eIgQ\"><strong>here</strong></a>.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Benefits</strong></div><div>South Dakota State University offers a wide range of excellent benefits including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.<br><br></div><div><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Earned terminal degree and evidence of scholarly, professional, or creative achievement sufficient to qualify for tenure as a full professor at South Dakota State University;</li><li>A minimum of 5 years of progressive, executive-level leadership experience managing a complex research enterprise within higher education, government, or industry;</li><li>Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>A record of successful leadership with a knowledge of, appreciation for and commitment to the philosophy and programs of a land-grant institution;</li><li>Ability to develop and implement a bold vision for the future of research and economic development;</li><li>A nimble strategist with a proven record of envisioning, developing and sustaining innovative programs that foster excellence and increased research across the fabric of the university;</li><li>An effective collaborator and consensus builder who can communicate with multiple constituencies and enable partnerships with other colleges and universities, government agencies, stakeholders, and corporations;</li><li>Capacity to identify, recruit and retain a strong staff;</li><li>Demonstrated experience overseeing large, complex budgets, fiscal matters, strategic planning and personnel management; and</li><li>Collaborative communicator with excellent interpersonal skills and the proven ability to advocate effectively with university leadership, industry, federal agencies, and other key partners.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Application Process</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.</div><div><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Division of Research & Econ Dvlp https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49606 2026-08-31T15:42:58-05:00 2026-08-31T15:42:59-05:00 Building Maintenance Specialist <div>The Facilities &amp; Services department of South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an experienced boiler operator to be a part of the team in the heating plant. Responsibilities include operating and maintaining the campus heating plant to ensure reliable heat and hot water delivery to approximately 80% of SDSU campus. Ensures boilers run at optimal efficiency with minimal environmental impact through continuous monitoring, adjustment, and adherence to best practices in plant operations.<br><br></div><div>The <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/facilities-services/energy-systems-sustainability\"><strong>Energy Systems Division of Facilities and Services</strong></a> manages the production and distribution of the heating and cooling for campus. Our staff of engineers and technicians continually assess new technologies and energy options to assure SDState utilizes the most efficient and reliable systems both environmentally and fiscally.<br><br></div><div>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, SD</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>· Operate high pressure (150PSIG) gas and oil-fired boilers and associated equipment in the Heating Plant<br><br></div><div>· Perform full range of maintenance activities and repairs on Central Heating Plant equipment.</div><div>· Maintenance and repair of hydronic heating and cooling systems across campus.<br><br></div><div>· Maintain heating, ventilation, air conditioning systems (HVAC)<br><br></div><div>· Perform planned preventative maintenance on building equipment</div><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:&nbsp;</div><div>· Boiler operations<br><br></div><div>· Methods, tools and equipment associated with boiler operations<br><br></div><div>· Knowledge of hydronics and HVAC for both small and large commercial or institutional sized equipment&nbsp;</div><div><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:</div><div>· Ability to maintain records<br><br></div><div>· Calculate boiler combustion efficiency</div><div><br>· Mechanical ability</div><div><br>· Ability to work shifts through winter</div><div><br>· Ability to lift 50lbs<br><br></div><div>· Ability to occasionally be on call<br><br></div><div><strong>Required License:<br></strong><br></div><div>· Valid Driver’s License</div><div><br>· Obtain EPA 608 certification within 6 months of employment</div><div><strong><br>Application Procedures:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Energy Systems https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48303 2026-05-27T08:48:14-05:00 2026-05-27T08:48:15-05:00 Health Sciences Faculty--QE8767 <div>The University of South Dakota Department of Public Health and Health Sciences, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for an instructor or lecturer position. This faculty position offers an exceptional opportunity to work with a dedicated team of faculty and staff to prepare graduates for a wide variety of health careers. This is a continuing faculty role structured on a 9-month contract. The faculty member will be responsible for classroom instruction and online instruction in the following undergraduate education content areas: interprofessional health teams, health career exploration, and the influences of culture, policy, and literacy on health.<br><br>Applicants must hold a graduate degree and have undergraduate and/or graduate preparation in health, education, or human services, or a combination of relevant academic preparation and professional experience; an MPH is preferred.<br><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> USD-Health Sciences Major https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49438 2026-08-19T08:45:20-05:00 2026-08-19T08:45:21-05:00 Manager, Business Office <div>The Manager, Business Office oversees student billing, receivables, loan processing, deposits, payment plans, collections, and customer service operations for the University of South Dakota. The position ensures compliance with Federal, State, BOR, and institutional policies; manages system processes and communication workflows; supervises Business Office staff; and serves as a primary point of contact for campus departments and external partners. The role maintains operational accuracy, efficiency, and customer‑focused service across all Business Office function.</div> USD-Business Office https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49113 2026-07-23T09:35:21-05:00 2026-07-23T09:35:22-05:00 Program Assistant I <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering<br><br></div><div><strong>STARTING HOURLY RATE: </strong>Minimum rate of $21.41 hourly, depending upon education and experience, GG<br><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE:</strong> The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) at South Dakota Mines is seeking applicants for Program Assistant I. This position will provide professional and efficient administrative/office support to the Chemical and Biological Engineering department head, faculty, staff, and students. Additionally, this position will provide research proposals and grant award management support for accounting, bookkeeping, and budgeting. A wide variety of office support, research grant support, and department outreach duties must be done with minimal supervision or assistance.<br><br></div><div>Specific duties will include managing the department office; assisting the department head and staff as needed; processing purchase requisitions, travel arrangements and reimbursements; processing student employment requests; creating and maintaining databases; accounting support for faculty research grants; budget forecasting; scheduling and coordinating meetings; answering the phone and greeting visitors; maintaining the department web page; and copying, filing and processing mail.<br><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>English grammar, spelling, and punctuation</li><li>basic bookkeeping and mathematical/budgeting/accounting skills</li><li>modern office equipment practices and procedures</li><li>computer software applications, including Microsoft Office</li></ul><div>Skills and Ability to:</div><ul><li>communicate professionally in a clear and concise manner</li><li>interact supportively with students, faculty, staff and visitors</li><li>manage and summarize data from a variety of sources</li><li>work independently, be detail-oriented, stay organized, prioritize and handle multiple tasks while meeting deadlines</li><li>set up/type/edit copy in a variety of formats</li><li>work with staff in other campus offices</li><li>use computer and learn new software</li><li>operate printers/scanners, copy machine, and other office equipment</li></ul><div><br></div><div>A bachelor’s degree is preferred, but an associate’s degree with relevant experience will be considered.<br><br></div><div>The CBE Department has a tradition of excellence in process-oriented education in chemical engineering, producing quality graduates who are sought by industry and top graduate programs. CBE resides in a remodeled $25MM Chemical and Biological Engineering and Chemistry (CBEC) building, which offers state-of-the-art teaching and research laboratories, including a 3,000 sq. ft. pilot-scale unit operations laboratory. The department offers BS, MS, and PhD degrees, and it is currently home to about 160 students. CBE has a strong research enterprise with annual grant expenditures exceeding $3.0 MM. For more information regarding the Karen M. Swindler CBE Department, visit http://www.sdsmt.edu/CBE.<strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>TO APPLY:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin July 17, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Karen M. Swindler Chemical and Biological Engineering https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48991 2026-07-14T11:30:55-05:00 2026-07-14T11:30:56-05:00 Assistant Professor of Accounting <div>&nbsp;Northern State University’s School of Business is accepting applications for a tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Accounting<br><br><strong>&nbsp;* Qualifications:</strong> Northern State University’s School of Business invites applications for a full-time faculty position in accounting, beginning January 2027, if possible, otherwise August 2027. Candidates holding a Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Accounting will be considered for a tenure-track appointment, while applicants with a master’s degree in accounting will be considered for non tenure-track positions. The ideal candidate will possess an active Certified Public Accountant (CPA) license and professional experience in taxation. <br><br>*<strong> Responsibilities:</strong> The successful candidate will be able to teach a variety of graduate and undergraduate accounting courses in both face-to-face and online settings; serve as an academic advisor and mentor; engage in scholarly activity; and provide service to the university and community.&nbsp;</div> NSU-Accounting https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49547 2026-08-27T08:48:54-05:00 2026-08-27T08:48:55-05:00 Program and Tribal Relations Coordinator <div>South Dakota State University is currently seeking a Program and Tribal Relations Coordinator. In this position you will help support student success and be a collaborative team player. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>Develop and coordinate programming that supports student success, belonging, and engagement, with a focus on strengthening relationships with Tribal Nations and advancing institutional support for Indigenous students, staff, and faculty.</div><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><strong><br>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in English, Education, American Indian and Indigenous Studies, Social Sciences to include Psychology, or Sociology, History, Training and Development, Curriculum Design or a related field completed by start date</li><li>Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Experiential knowledge of tribal language, culture, and lifeways</li><li>Experience working with tribal communities</li><li>Demonstrated experience in program management or program evaluation</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Academic Affairs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49297 2026-08-05T15:35:21-05:00 2026-08-05T15:35:21-05:00 Grounds Crew Specialist <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Facilities and Risk Management</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Starting Hourly Rate: </strong>Minimum of $18.45 per hour, depending upon education and experience, GE<br><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE:</strong> Will serve as a specialist in grounds care and maintenance. Duties include safely operating various types of grounds equipment; care of landscape and grounds, including snow removal, garbage pick-up, mowing, watering, cultivating, spraying, fertilizing, trimming, planting flowers, trees, shrubs and grass; maintenance of athletic facilities and parking lot, including moving equipment and furniture, maintaining artificial turf, and garbage pickup at events; maintenance, programming, and repair of manual and electronic irrigation systems; supervision of student, regular, and temporary employees; and other duties as assigned.</div><div><br><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>use of grounds equipment;</li><li>gardening and grounds maintenance practices, including artificial turf and athletic field maintenance (not required but preferred);</li><li>safe use of fertilizers, insecticides and herbicides;</li><li>safe disposal of hazardous wastes;</li><li>sprinkler and irrigation systems;</li><li>types and varieties of trees and plants.</li></ul><div>Ability to:</div><ul><li>communicate information clearly and concisely, exercising tact, patience, discretion and professional demeanor;</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner with students, faculty, staff and visitors;</li><li>operate motorized vehicles, hand and power tools, and related equipment;</li><li>work independently, prioritize assigned work, establish timetables, and meet deadlines;</li><li>read, comprehend, and follow instructions;</li><li>work outdoors, lift and carry heavy items in excess of 50 lbs., perform physical labor, bend, squat, and work in all types of extreme temperatures or weather conditions;</li><li>recognize and diagnose plant diseases, identify insect destruction and perform the necessary corrective action;</li><li>organize and delegate assignments;</li><li>provide outstanding customer service.</li></ul><div><br><strong>COMMENTS:</strong> A valid driver’s license is required. Will be required to work nights, weekends and holidays as needed for snow removal. Normal hours are early morning start with an 8-hr shift.</div><div><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin July 30, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a resume and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Facilities Management https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49656 2026-09-03T18:07:11-05:00 2026-09-03T18:07:12-05:00 Custodial Services Supervisor I <div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) Student Life Building Services is looking for a motivated individual to join our team as a Custodial Services Supervisor within University Housing and Residential Life.<br><br></div><div>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings.</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:<br></strong>This position plans, coordinates and directs the daily activities of facility workers to maintain cleanliness and hygiene standards across campus facilities. This includes, but is not limited to, assigning tasks, inspecting work, training new employees, and ensuring compliance in operational standards. This role requires strong leadership, communication and problem-solving skills to manage a team, respond to customer requests and contribute to overall efficiency and effectiveness of Student Life Building Services.</div><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:<br></em></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em></div><ul><li>Inventory tracking methods</li><li>Commercial custodial work techniques</li><li>Proper use of chemicals and equipment</li><li>Effective supervisory methods</li><li>Microsoft Office programs</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to:</em></div><ul><li>Clean floors, bathrooms, showers, carpets and walls</li><li>Establish and maintain effective supervisory relationships</li><li>Plan and schedule work to meet competing deadlines</li><li>Supervise, train, monitor and evaluate work of facility workers</li><li>Operate and repair cleaning equipment</li><li>Complete special assignments</li><li>Work independently</li><li>Lift and carry up to 65 pounds</li><li>Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing</li><li>Maintain records</li><li>Interact effectively and professionally with contractors, coworkers, and customers.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Required License: </em></strong>Valid driver’s license is required.</div><div><strong><em><br>Comments:</em></strong> This position requires occasional weekends/holidays.<br><br></div><div><strong>Application Procedures:<br></strong>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-University Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49610 2026-08-31T16:19:49-05:00 2026-08-31T16:19:50-05:00 Assistant Coach, Triathlon <div>Black Hills State University is seeking applicants for an Assistant Triathlon Coach in the Athletics department.<br><br>DUTIES:<br>• Manage the day-to-day practice and skill development of student athletes, practice planning, and recruitment of student athletes. They will also oversee the strength and performance of the team.<br>• Assist with management and administration of Triathlon Team<br>• Assist the head coach with fundraising and growing the program regionally as well as nationally.<br>• Ideal candidates will have excellent communication skills (both oral and written), work well with a team, assist across all areas of athletics and collaborate with campus and community partners.</div><div><br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:<br>• Bachelor’s degree<br>• 1-3 years’ experience</div><div><br>COMMENTS:<br>This is a part-time (19 hrs/week), 10-month appointment. Anticipated start date is as soon as possible. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br>TO APPLY:<br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7CKristin.Carmichael%40bhsu.edu%7C279a2e1023664b742a1708dc54275e3b%7C9bfcf28b3a114fd7a8138f519cdb0db2%7C0%7C0%7C638477775263784390%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=26V7Qkn4aNTCfF4rQ0681BGLLdK2XtWAxPD%2B295aDXc%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Candidates will need to attach a cover letter, resume and the names/contact information of at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of September 6, 2026 at 11pm (MDT). For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may be directed towards Katie Christy at Katie.Christy@bhsu.edu.<br><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Intercolleg Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48358 2026-06-01T09:15:54-05:00 2026-06-01T09:15:55-05:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>The Physics Department at South Dakota Mines invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher position to work on the germanium-based science and technology advancement research. This is a full-time, benefited position. In collaborating with USD and other universities in South Dakota, the successful applicant will play a major role in R&amp;Ds including laboratory testing and characterization of germanium detectors, develop advanced Monte Carlo models and AI-driven analysis tools to optimize detector response, and to promote precision medical imaging and low energy dark matter searches and neutrino experiments.<br><br>Located in Rapid City, next to the scenic Black Hills of South Dakota, South Dakota Mines is the leading science and engineering university in the region. The campus is an hour’s drive from the Sanford Underground Research Facility (SURF), historic home of the noble-prize-winning Ray Davis experiment on solar neutrino oscillations, and home of the LZ, MAJORANA Demonstrator, and CASPAR experiments, and the DUNE/LBNF far detector. The university has made a focus of underground physics experiments to increase our understanding of particle/astroparticle physics and nuclear astrophysics. Physics faculty at South Dakota Mines are conducting internationally recognized research in particle/astroparticle physics, dark matter search, neutrino physics, nuclear astrophysics, as well as condensed matter and materials science.<br><br>The preferred starting date of this position is July 1, 2026. The position would remain open for new applications until filled. <br><br><strong>Qualifications:<br></strong>Candidates should hold a PhD in experimental nuclear or particle physics. Experience with gamma-ray spectroscopy, germanium detectors and applications, GEANT4 simulations, as well as proficiency in C++ programming, is highly preferred.<br><br></div><div><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin June 1, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Physics 1 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49445 2026-08-19T10:17:07-05:00 2026-08-19T10:17:08-05:00 Associate Vice President for Human Resources <div>Northern State University invites applications for the position of <strong>Associate Vice President for Human Resources</strong>, an exceptional opportunity for an experienced human resources professional to serve as the University's chief HR officer. <br><br>Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Administration and the Board of Regents Chief HR Officer, the Associate Vice President for Human Resources provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all human resource functions while fostering a culture of excellence, engagement, and service across campus. In addition, this position serves as a valued member of the SD Board of Regents HR Leadership team. This position also provides comprehensive human resources and payroll services to the South Dakota School for the Blind and Visually Impaired, making it a unique opportunity to support two outstanding public institutions dedicated to education and student success. <br><br>The Associate Vice President for Human Resources serves as a trusted advisor to executive leadership, managers, faculty, and staff on all aspects of human resources. This position is responsible for developing and implementing strategic HR initiatives that support the University's mission and strategic plan while ensuring compliance with federal, state, and South Dakota Board of Regents policies. The successful candidate will lead initiatives in recruitment and retention, employee relations, performance management, compensation and classification, benefits administration, compliance, organizational development, payroll oversight, and HR information systems.<br><br> <strong>Primary Responsibilities<br></strong>• Provide strategic leadership for all Human Resources operations.<br>• Advise leadership on workforce planning, organizational development, and employee relations.<br>• Lead recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and retention initiatives for faculty, staff, and administrators.<br>• Oversee employee relations, workplace investigations, performance management, and corrective action processes.<br>• Ensure compliance with employment laws and Board of Regents policies, including FLSA, FMLA, ADA, ACA, Title VII, Title IX, and EEO requirements. <br>• Manage HR information systems, workforce reporting, and personnel records. <br>Oversee payroll operations within a complex system governing Board of Regents campuses. <br>• Support organizational effectiveness through strategic planning and data-informed decision-making. <br><br><strong>Required Qualifications</strong> <br>• Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Management, Leadership, or a closely related field. <br>• Significant progressively responsible professional experience in human resources, including management and leadership responsibilities.<br> • Demonstrated knowledge of employee relations, employment law, compensation, benefits, recruitment, organizational development, and HR information systems.<br> • Exceptional communication, interpersonal, analytical, and problem-solving skills.<br> • Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and build collaborative relationships across the organization. <br><br><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong><br>• Master's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Leadership, or a related field.<br> • PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, or SHRM-SCP professional certification.<br>• Experience working in higher education or another complex public-sector organization.</div> NSU-Finance & Administration https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49123 2026-07-23T13:04:21-05:00 2026-07-23T13:04:22-05:00 Department Head - Biology & Microbiology <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) seeks an innovative and collaborative leader to serve as Department Head of the Department of Biology and Microbiology within the College of Natural Sciences. This is a 12-month, full-time, tenure-track, benefits-eligible appointment with the academic rank of either Associate or Full Professor. This leadership position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\">Brookings, SD</a>, serves as the executive officer of the department and reports directly to the Dean of the College of Natural Sciences.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>This Department of Biology and Microbiology offers a variety of undergraduate degree programs including Human Biology, Microbiology, and Biotechnology. Together these majors train over 500 undergraduates for admission to professional programs in healthcare domains, graduate school, careers in industry, and a variety of other career paths. The Department is a key driver of South Dakota State University’s <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/office-president/pathway-premier-2030/r1-our-way\"><strong>R1 Our Way</strong></a> mission to expand federally funded research and has active research and graduate programs focused on mammalian physiology and cell biology, microbial biology, plant physiology and molecular biology, and bioprocessing biotechnology. Department members lead or contribute to large research programs including multiple federally-funded research centers and engage in STEM outreach and workforce development. South Dakota State University promotes access to and opportunities for all to receive the benefit of and participate in education, research, and service and is especially interested in candidates that can contribute to this land-grant mission of access.</div><div><br></div><div>&nbsp;Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>The Department of Biology and Microbiology seeks an innovative and collaborative leader with the vision, communication skills, and administrative capacity to guide the department. The successful candidate should be committed to establishing collaborative relationships, fostering an environment in which faculty and stakeholders are engaged partners, and communicating consistently and effectively. The Department Head is responsible for leading the development and maintenance of strong academic programs, supporting student recruitment and success across undergraduate and graduate programs, and ensuring that curricula remain rigorous, current, and responsive to workforce needs. The Department Head also provides leadership for the department’s research enterprise by supporting faculty grant development, managing research infrastructure and operations, mentoring early-career faculty, promoting collaboration, and cultivating a culture of high-quality, externally funded research.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><br>&nbsp;BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong><br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Ph.D. in Biology, Microbiology Biotechnology or closely related field by application date.</li><li>Meets the standards for tenure and rank within the department. Standards documents are available upon request to the search committee chair.</li><li>Evidence of effective leadership and administrative skills including management of academic and research programs, managing complex budgets, fiscal matters, and/or personnel within an academic setting.&nbsp;</li><li>Effective interpersonal relations, consensus building, professionalism, and motivational skills&nbsp;</li><li>Effective verbal and written communication skills</li><li>Understanding of the land-grant mission.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><br><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Experience in academic administration, including the development, evaluation and oversight of undergraduate academic programs, curricula and/or instructional operations.</li><li>Ability to support and advance research program success, strategic planning, and departmental initiatives.</li><li>Familiarity with student success best practices</li><li>Familiarity with recruitment and retention best practices for students, faculty, and staff</li><li>Experience with collaboration across disciplines and/or with multiple stakeholders</li><li>Leadership professional development experience</li><li>Evidence of cultivating entrepreneurial opportunities</li></ul><div><br></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp; Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. &nbsp; It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Biology & Microbiology https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49005 2026-07-15T16:56:47-05:00 2026-07-15T16:56:48-05:00 Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturer of Mechanical Engineering <div>The Department of Mechanical Engineering at the South Dakota School of Mines &amp; Technology invites applications for fall 2026 and/or spring 2027 semester Instructor, Lecturer, or Senior Lecturer positions. These are part-time, temporary, non-benefited positions and may continue semester-by-semester, dependent upon performance, department need, funding, and student enrollment.<br><br></div><div>Expectations will include teaching, in-person, undergraduate mechanical engineering courses, and any accompanying laboratory section.<br><br></div><div>An earned MS in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field is required; a PhD in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field is preferred. Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, are required. The ideal candidates will have prior teaching experience at the university or college level and engineering experience in industry or government.<br><br></div><div>The anticipated start date is August 2026 for the fall semester and January 2027 for the spring semester. The successful applicant is required to be physically located at the school with the course(s) being taught fully in-person.</div><div><br><strong>To Apply</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin July 14, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.</div> SDSMT-Leslie A. Rose Department of Mechanical Engineering https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49554 2026-08-27T13:24:49-05:00 2026-08-27T13:24:50-05:00 Facility Worker <div>USD Facilities Management is hiring for Facility Workers in the Custodial Services department. Duties include, but are not limited to: collect and remove trash; clean and dust furniture, windows, and walls; wet mop, strip and wax floors; vacuum and shampoo carpets; mop and/or buff floors; clean and disinfect bathrooms and restock supplies; room set ups; change light bulbs and clean light fixtures; remove snow/ice; report needed repairs; and maintain a safe environment by cleaning up spills and removing hazards. Hiring for multiple shifts. Starting rate is $16/hour with an excellent benefits package, including generous vacation and sick leave and 11 paid holidays per year. Multiple shifts available.<br><br>USD Facilities Management is committed to the highest standard of customer relations principles for its customers, fellow staff members, students, and visitors. Staff will serve as role models by practicing exemplary behaviors when working with customers, fellow staff members, and the supervisory team. Applicants who exemplify those standards are encouraged to apply.</div> USD-Custodial Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/25548 2021-10-28T14:55:57-05:00 2021-10-28T14:55:59-05:00 Adjunct Instructor <div>The Division of Counseling and Psychology in Education invites applications for Adjunct Instructors with expertise in Educational Psychology, Human Development, Counseling, Research Methods, or Statistics for its pool of part-time adjunct instructors. Applications for part-time faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the program coordinator when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a term-by-term basis, which may include fall, spring and/or summer.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Successful applicants will be expected to teach primarily on-campus undergraduate courses in human development.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Depending on expertise, applicants may occasionally have the opportunity to teach more advanced coursework in educational psychology, human development, counseling, research methods, or statistics. These courses may be offered on campus, hybrid, or online.<br><br></div><div><strong>Minimum Qualifications: </strong>M.S. or M.A. in Educational Psychology, Human Development, Counseling, or a closely related field.<br>&nbsp;<br>Please provide a CV, names and contact information for 3 professional references, and a letter of application, which should include a statement of teaching interests and evidence of effectiveness. A copy of previous teaching evaluations or relevant syllabi may also be included. Inquires may be directed to <a href=\"mailto:gabrielle.strouse@usd.edu\">gabrielle.strouse@usd.edu</a></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><br><br></div> USD-Counseling & Psychology in Ed. https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49304 2026-08-06T13:39:39-05:00 2026-08-06T13:39:40-05:00 Adjunct, Biology <div>Black Hills State University invites applicants for an adjunct instructor in Biology to teach Survey of Biology I and II courses on the Spearfish campus.&nbsp;<br><br>Successful candidates must possess at least an MS in Biology or related discipline, and teaching experience in higher education is preferred.<br><br></div><div>Applications may be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7CTami.Roberts%40bhsu.edu%7Ca239fc35de8c455bebf008def3e0878e%7C9bfcf28b3a114fd7a8138f519cdb0db2%7C0%7C0%7C639216342841827550%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=2Lx8HxlTSphC8dmjxNYncNOhDqK2k0SVK9z1DadzKtE%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Interested individuals should complete an online application and also attach a cover letter, C.V., copies of transcripts from graduate institutions, and the names and contact information of three references. For application assistance, contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Inquiries specific to the position and C.V.’s may be sent to <a href=\"mailto:Dan.Asunskis@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Dan.Asunskis@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-School of Natural Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49660 2026-09-04T09:52:53-05:00 2026-09-04T09:52:54-05:00 Program Assistant II (4-H Educator) Meade County <div>Do you want to inspire and empower the next generation of South Dakota leaders? At South Dakota State University (SDSU) 4-H Programs, we are dedicated to providing youth with supportive adults, hands-on learning experiences, and opportunities to reach their full potential. We’re seeking a collaborative, people-focused professional who is passionate about mentoring, guiding, and helping others grow.<br><br></div><div>SDSU Extension 4‑H is a community that provides experiences where young people learn by doing. Kids complete hands-on projects in areas like health, science, agriculture and citizenship, in a positive environment where they receive guidance from adult mentors and are encouraged to take on proactive leadership roles. Kids experience 4‑H through in-school and after-school programs, school and community clubs and 4‑H camps. We recognize that the youth of today are our future leaders and what they learn and experience in 4-H will help them develop into contributing citizens who will give back to their communities in the future.<br><br></div><div>This position is located in Sturgis, South Dakota.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Provide timely 4-H Youth Development research based information, resources, education, leadership and support to meet the needs of youth in the county while building relationships to enhance and carry out the mission of SDSU Extension and South Dakota 4-H. <strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong></div><div><strong>Knowledge of:&nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Computer systems and software (i.e., MS Word, Outlook, Excel).</li><li>Planning, teaching, and evaluating educational programs for a variety of youth audiences.</li><li>Mentoring and supervisory techniques.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:</strong></div><ul><li>Strong interpersonal skills and excellent verbal communication skills.</li><li>Use effective written communication skills.</li><li>Organizational and time management skills.</li><li>Work as a contributing member of a team.</li><li>Plan, implement and complete events.</li><li>Manage a budget</li></ul><div><strong><br>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in Education, Child, Youth, or Human Development, or other relevant fields with relevant youth development experience.</li><li>Previous 4-H or similar youth development experience.</li><li>Demonstrated use of technology in managing and/or delivering educational programs.</li><li>Experience in publishing materials and/or curricula.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required License:</strong></div><ul><li>Valid driver’s license</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Comments:</strong></div><div>This position is classified as Program Assistant II. <strong><br><br>Application Procedures:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div><div><br>[EE9723; 11043]</div> SDSU-4-H Programs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49154 2026-07-27T13:43:48-05:00 2026-07-27T13:43:48-05:00 Program Assistant I, University Libraries <div>The University Libraries seeks a motivated, communicative and well-organized team member to advance the libraries' support for the mission of the University of South Dakota.<br><br>The successful individual will have knowledge and experience with, or will readily learn USD and SDBOR Human Resources and Payroll systems, policies and procedures; demonstrate a record of excellent interpersonal skills; demonstrate effective written and spoken communication; have experience in using Microsoft Office applications; and have experience with or an interest in event planning.<br><br>Responsibilities includes managing all aspects of library employee hiring, onboarding and personnel processes; supporting the dean of libraries through the management of calendars, communication and coordination with internal and external constituencies; coordinate the libraries' campus/public-facing events; develop and maintain administrative policies; ensure and carry out library-wide information management; and support administrative processes related to grants and externally-funded projects and programs.<br><br>The position is based at I.D. Weeks Library on the USD campus in Vermillion, SD. Hybrid work is an option. The University of South Dakota offers a wide range of benefits including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, paid holidays and retirement plans. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matched contribution to the state retirement system. Employees also have access to reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions.&nbsp;</div> USD-Libraries https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49614 2026-09-01T10:10:57-05:00 2026-09-01T10:10:57-05:00 Program Assistant I <div>Join the college of Nursing as a Program Assistant I and become an essential member of our Undergraduate Nursing team. We’re seeking a detail oriented and service focused professional who enjoys supporting students, faculty, and staff while helping ensure the smooth operation of our academic programs. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.visitrapidcity.com/\"><strong>Rapid City</strong></a>, South Dakota.</div><div><br></div><div>The College of Nursing has a long history of exceptional nursing education, and this is recognized through its designation as a Center of Excellence in Nursing Education by the National League for Nursing. Nursing’s history of excellence, innovation, and achievement across its graduate, undergraduate and continuing education programs provides an excellent foundation for growth and innovation and lifelong learning.</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Provides administrative support for the academic programs and day-to-day operations of the College of Nursing Rapid City site. Serves as the primary point of contact for the Rapid City location, working collaboratively with Academic Shared Services, the Director of Nursing Operations, and the College of Nursing Dean's Office to support accounting, hiring, purchasing, and other administrative functions. Supports testing center activities, including exam proctoring and scanning of completed examinations, while providing excellent customer service and operational support to faculty, staff, students, and campus partners.</div><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Principles and practices of public administration</li><li>South Dakota State University and Board of Regents policies and procedures</li><li>General administrative methods and processes, including human resources functions such as I-9 verification, interview scheduling, and onboarding support, and facilities management</li><li>Financial and business processes in collaboration with Academic Shared Services and the Director of Nursing Operations</li><li>Testing center procedures, operations, and best practices&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:</div><ul><li>Exercise independent judgement in evaluating situations and making decisions</li><li>Communicate information clearly, concisely, accurately, and efficiently</li><li>Plan and project future functional needs in terms of facilities, class operations, faculty support, events, and supplies</li><li>Interpret objectives and develop practical applications</li><li>Microsoft Office Suite applications</li><li>Manage confidential information</li><li>Provide customer service, responding to unique circumstances and direct inquiries to appropriate individuals</li><li>Learn and effectively use computer systems, software applications, and office equipment</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required License:</strong></div><div>Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire.</div><div><strong><br>Application Procedures:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Undergraduate Nursing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48469 2026-06-05T13:36:00-05:00 2026-06-05T13:36:01-05:00 Assistant Professor, Biology (Organismal Zoology) <div>The School of Natural Sciences at Black Hills State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track, Assistant Professor position in organismal zoology, beginning August 2026. The successful candidate will join a diverse Natural Science department and complement other faculty in areas of ecology, evolution, physiology, genetics and cell-molecular biology.<br><br>DUTIES:<br>The successful candidate will help shape and grow the new wildlife emphasis within the Biology major by teaching upper-level courses that support wildlife students (ecology, mammalogy, herpetology, ichthyology, environmental policy, etc), as well as introductory courses in Biology as needed. We seek a broadly trained wildlife biologist or ecologist who will complement existing faculty strengths in the School of Natural Sciences and develop collaborations with local and regional agencies. Individuals with expertise in wildlife or fisheries management are especially encouraged to apply. Primary responsibilities include successful teaching and advising, development of a research program that includes undergraduate and graduate students, and service related to student professional opportunities. Other opportunities include supervision of graduate students in the Integrative Genomics MSc. program, and course instruction in the Sustainability MSc. program.<br><br>QUALIFICATIONS:<br>A PhD in Biology, Wildlife Ecology, Natural Resources or related field. ABD accepted.<br><br>COMMENTS:<br>The School of Natural Sciences at Black Hills State University is a vibrant, growing division with approximately 23 faculty members in biology, chemistry, geology, and physics. Faculty emphasize undergraduate teaching and mentoring, and conduct research involving students in multiple biological and environmental disciplines. Projects are funded through a variety of state wildlife, federal agency, and partnership grants. Research resources include the largest Herbarium in the state, and well-equipped laboratories including a scanning electron microscopy lab. The Center for the Conservation of Biological Resources (CCBR) is a shared research laboratory containing research space and commonly used equipment required for genetics and genomics research. WestCore is a Genetics/Genomics sequencing core facility that provides services including NextGen genome, transcriptome, and Sanger sequencing, genotyping, and quantitative real-time PCR services. WestCore also houses a cell culture area and an RNA isolation room. The Black Hills State University Underground Campus (BHUC) at the Sanford Underground Research Facility (SURF) in Lead, SD houses Sanford Lab’s low background counting facility, a class-1,000 cleanroom, and an adjoining workspace available for use in a variety of disciplines. Managed by BHSU, the underground campus partners with groups around the globe to create unique opportunities for collaborative research in physics, chemistry, biology, and geophysics.<br><br>SPECIAL COMMENTS:<br>The successful applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br>TO APPLY:<br>Applications must be made online at http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, statement of proposed research, transcripts, and names and contact information for at least three professional references. Letters of reference/recommendation are not accepted. (Please note, you may need to combine documents into one file to upload into the system.) This position is open until filled with a first review date of June 19, 2026 at 11:00 PM (mountain time). For application assistance, contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Please direct inquiries regarding the position to Dr. Jessica Graham, search committee chair, at Jessica.Graham@bhsu.edu.<br><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-School of Natural Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49461 2026-08-19T17:59:48-05:00 2026-08-19T17:59:49-05:00 NSF NRT Project Coordinator <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Civil &amp; Environmental Engineering<br><br></div><div><strong>Starting Hourly Rate: </strong>Minimum of $19.27 per hour, depending upon education and experience, GF</div><div><br><strong>POSITION PURPOSE:</strong></div><div>The Project Coordinator serves as the primary operational coordinator for projects including the South Dakota Mines’ NSF Research Traineeship (NRT) program, led through the 2D-Materials for Biofilm Engineering, Science, and Technology (2DBEST) Center. The position translates program leadership priorities into coordinated day-to-day implementation and helps ensure a consistent, high-quality trainee experience across an interdisciplinary program focused on AI, intelligent materials, microbiome engineering, and digital twins. The coordinator works closely with the Principal Investigator and program leadership to coordinate trainee recruitment and onboarding; seminars, workshops, meetings, and other program activities; assessment, data collection, documentation, and NSF reporting; communications among faculty, trainees, institutional partners, evaluators, and external stakeholders; and access to shared research and training resources. The position also tracks milestones, deadlines, and deliverables to support timely, organized, and compliant execution of the NRT program.<br><br></div><div><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>principles and practices of project and program coordination, preferably in a higher-education, research, or grant-funded environment;</li><li>professional written English, including grammar, spelling, punctuation, and business correspondence;</li><li>common office, productivity, collaboration, spreadsheet, database, and virtual-meeting software applications;</li><li>recordkeeping, data tracking, document management, and basic sponsored-project reporting and confidentiality practices.</li></ul><div>Ability to:</div><ul><li>coordinate multiple program activities, priorities, timelines, and deliverables simultaneously;</li><li>support trainee recruitment, selection-process logistics, onboarding, and ongoing program participation;</li><li>plan and coordinate meetings, seminars, workshops, training activities, and related logistics;</li><li>collect, organize, verify, maintain, and summarize program data for assessment, reporting, and decision-making;</li><li>prepare, proofread, and edit professional correspondence, program materials, reports, presentations, and other documents;</li><li>communicate clearly, professionally, and effectively with faculty, students, administrators, institutional partners, evaluators, and external stakeholders;</li><li>read, interpret, and apply written program requirements, institutional procedures, and sponsor guidance;</li><li>maintain accurate records and handle sensitive or confidential information with appropriate discretion;</li><li>research and compile information and follow through on action items, deadlines, and requests;</li><li>establish and maintain effective working relationships across interdisciplinary teams and with individuals from varied backgrounds;</li><li>exercise sound judgment, tact, initiative, patience, and discretion in resolving routine program issues and coordinating competing needs;</li><li>work independently with limited supervision while contributing effectively to a collaborative team and adapting to changing program needs.</li></ul><div><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 20, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a resume and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Civil & Environmental Engineering 1 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49669 2026-09-04T14:00:20-05:00 2026-09-04T14:00:21-05:00 Facilities Services Supervisor I <div>Dakota State University is seeking applications a full-time Facilities Services Supervisor I. This position will work an 8 hour shift Monday through Friday with some weekends as needed to help with preparation/clean-up for events on campus. The hours will be 4:00am-12:30pm<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities Include:</strong></div><ul><li>General cleaning of an academic building.</li><li>Floor care mainly vacuuming and mopping but could include scrubbing, waxing, and shampooing carpets.</li><li>Clean and sanitize restrooms and breakrooms.</li><li>Collect and remove trash from building.</li><li>Dust and wash walls, woodwork, and windows (inside and out).</li><li>Remove snow from steps and sidewalks near buildings.</li><li>Supervise a team of facility workers.</li><li>Select personnel.</li><li>Schedule and assign work of subordinates.</li><li>Work with other supervisors to coordinate summer cleaning.</li><li>Conduct performance appraisals.</li><li>Order and maintain inventory.</li><li>Maintain high quality and safety standards.</li><li>Perform minor maintenance projects.</li><li>Maintain the outside parameters of the buildings.</li><li>Monitor the buildings for property safety.</li><li>Supervise preparation for special events in buildings and clean up for those events.</li><li>Move furniture and check equipment as necessary.</li></ul><div><br><strong>The successful applicant must be able to or have knowledge of:</strong></div><ul><li>Follow written and oral instructions</li><li>Work with students, staff, and the public courteously.</li><li>Work independently.</li><li>Lift up to 50 pounds regularly.</li><li>Maintain a valid driver’s license.</li><li>Knowledge of building cleaning and sanitation techniques.</li><li>Knowledge of proper use of equipment and supplies.</li><li>Knowledge of use of various hand and power tools.</li><li>Knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook.</li><li>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply:</strong><br> DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please submit a resume and a list of at least three references.<br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:Alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>Alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br> Applications will begin to be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div> DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49022 2026-07-16T16:27:17-05:00 2026-07-16T16:27:18-05:00 Nutrition Aide <div>USD Head Start is seeking a Nutrition Aide for the Head Start classroom in Beresford. This position is a part-time position. The position works from Mid-August until End of May annually.<br><br>Responsibilities include serving breakfast and/or lunch and preparing and serving snack for children ages 3-5 attending a Head Start classroom.<br><br>Prefer applicant that has experience with food service and with children ages 3-5. Must pass fingerprint background check.</div> USD-Head Start https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49557 2026-08-27T15:21:20-05:00 2026-08-27T15:21:21-05:00 Project Archivist <div>Join the Agricultural Heritage Museum as a Project Archivist and play a key role in preserving and expanding access to our historical collections. This temporary, two-year position will oversee the project of cataloging and digitization of a 40,000-photograph collection. This includes working with the Collections Coordinator in developing a processing plan and establishing an achievable timeline. We are seeking a detail-oriented professional with strong leadership skills who thrives in a collaborative environment.<br><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/about-us\"><strong>SDState</strong></a> is the state’s largest, most comprehensive university with over $94 million annual research expenditures, more than 200 academic programs and an enrollment of approximately 12,000 students. The university is part of a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IT8OnH5eIgQ&amp;feature=youtu.be\"><strong>dynamic community</strong></a> for families, students, young professionals, and retirees, which offers an abundance of attractions and activities.<br><br></div><div>The South Dakota Agricultural Heritage Museum’s mission is to<strong> </strong>inspire a passion for the diverse history, culture, and science of agriculture in South Dakota. Its vision is to connect multi-generational audiences to the importance of agriculture to their daily lives. It is the official State museum for preserving the history of agriculture and rural life of South Dakota as well a department of South Dakota State University. <br><br>This position is located in the historic Stock Judging Pavilion on the SDSU campus in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Arrange, describe, preserve, catalog and digitize visual materials in accordance with professional archival standards and national best practices.</li><li>Supervise student assistants and interns.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><strong><br>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:<br></strong>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>Working in archives, museums, or other cultural heritage settings</li><li>Professional standards and best practices for digitization, digital asset management, and preservation of photographic materials. Experience Arranging and describing archival collections and creating archival descriptions and metadata using professional standards and schema, such as DACS and Dublin Core</li></ul><div><br>Skills &amp; Ability to:</div><ul><li>Organize, prioritize, and maintain attention to detail while managing multiple projects and records.</li><li>Digitize photographs and negatives and manage digital files in accordance with established professional standards and best practices</li><li>Strong written and verbal communication skills, as well as critical thinking and active listening abilities.</li><li>Use basic computer applications, including word processing, spreadsheets, and databases at a proficiency level.</li><li>Train, direct, and delegate work assignments.</li><li>Ability to lift boxes weighing over 40 pounds, climb ladders while carrying boxes, and push or pull fully loaded carts.</li></ul><div><br>Preferred: 2 years of experience in photograph processing.</div><div><strong><br>Application Procedures:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Agricultural Heritage Museum https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/41967 2024-12-20T09:29:41-06:00 2024-12-20T09:29:42-06:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>The Nanoscience &amp; Biomedical Engineering Department at South Dakota Mines invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position within Dr. Shan Zhou’s research group. This is a full-time benefited position. This position will conduct research in the area of nanoparticle synthesis and self-assembly, as well as electron microscopy studies on nanoscale building blocks. This position will be responsible for conceiving, designing, and conducting experiments, with an emphasis on using wet chemistry methods to prepare nanomaterials and soft materials for microscopy imaging, and operating transmission electron microscope. This position will be expected to conduct data analysis, prepare publications, and present research findings in regional and national conferences.<br><br></div><div>A PhD in Chemistry, Materials Science and Engineering, Physics, Nanoscience and Nanoengineering or equivalent is required. Prior experiences with electron microscopy, electrochemistry, photocatalysis, and nanomaterials synthesis are highly preferred.<br><br></div><div>South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an excellent comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage options for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Individuals interested in this position must apply online at <a href=\"https://www.sdsmt.edu/about/offices-and-administration/human-resources/careers-at-mines.html\"><strong>Careers at Mines (sdsmt.edu)</strong></a>. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203. Review of applications will begin December 20, 2024 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume, representative publications (up to three), and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference). Candidates are encouraged to directly contact Dr. Shan Zhou (<a href=\"mailto:shan.zhou@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>shan.zhou@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>) for more information.</div> SDSMT-Nanoscience and Nanoengineering 1 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49330 2026-08-10T09:32:38-05:00 2026-08-10T09:32:38-05:00 Department Head of Electrical Engineering & Computer Science and Professor <div>The McComish Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) at South Dakota State University (SDSU) is seeking dynamic and collaborative leader to serve as the Department Head at the rank of Professor. Depending on the selected candidate’s area of expertise, faculty endowment may also be available. We are looking for a leader who is committed to providing a rigorous and practical educational experience with an emphasis on expanding federally funded research and graduate programs to support South Dakota State University’s R1 Our Way mission, as well as establishing and providing scientific support to local industry and government. This position is 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position, located in Brookings SD and reports to the Dean of the Jerome J. Johr College of Engineering (JJLCOE). Anticipated start of January 2027.<br><br></div><div>The McComish Department of EECS offers BS, MS, and Ph.D. in Artificial Intelligence Engineering, Computer Science; and Electrical Engineering; Specialization in <a href=\"https://catalog.sdstate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=60&amp;poid=15911\"><strong>Power Systems Engineering;</strong></a> and minors in Informatics, Computer Engineering, and Software Engineering. Currently, the department has over 250 undergraduate students, over 50 graduate students, and a vibrant graduate program with external annual funding of approximately $2.5M. The BS program in Computer Science is accredited by the CAC of ABET under the General Criteria and the Program Criteria for Computer Science and Similarly Named Computing Programs and the BS program in Electrical Engineering is accredited by the EAC of ABET, under the General Criteria and Program Criteria for Electrical, Computer, Communications, Telecommunication(s) and Similarly Named Engineering Programs.<br><br></div><div>The department, college, and University provide excellent facilities for cutting-edge research. Several faculty members in the college, including faculty members in the EECS department, have received NSF-CAREER or equivalent awards. Currently, the EECS Department has three endowed faculty positions. The department is committed to providing a rigorous and practical educational experience, with an emphasis on design and problem-solving, conducting world-class research relevant to the region, and providing technical assistance to existing and emerging businesses, industries, and government.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>The Department Head will work closely with the Dean and the leadership team of the Jerome J. Lohr College of Engineering (JJLCOE) to promote the land-grant mission and an ambitious agenda to address the world’s grand challenges in the areas of computer science, computer engineering, artificial intelligence, and electrical engineering. The selected candidate is expected to lead the EECS Department in identifying future areas of growth and investment while providing organizational and administrative expertise to the Department and the JJLCOE. The candidate is expected to steer the growth of the department consistent with SDSU’s refreshed strategic plan titled “Pathway to Premier 2030”. The strategic plan includes a goal to elevate SDSU as a research university and pursue a pathway to achieve designation as an R1 Research University by Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education.<br><br></div><div>It is imperative that this position maintains an understanding of current and emerging issues in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, and Electrical Engineering as defined by rapidly changing workforce needs as well as applied and fundamental research needs in varied yet integrated areas related to cloud computing, machine learning, materials and sensor development, IOT, embedded software, high-performance computing, and the power industry. This knowledge will guide both research and teaching initiatives within the department. It is the Department Head's responsibility to lead the faculty in their efforts to provide high-quality service courses at all levels, engage with client departments to determine their course needs, monitor trends in general education and service courses, and implement high-impact teaching and learning strategies. Along with leadership, the Department Head is an advocate for the McComish Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science both within and outside the University, fostering a commitment to interdisciplinary and interagency collaboration.<br><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a closely related field by date of application.</li><li>A distinguished record of teaching, research, scholarship, and service consistent with being eligible for tenure and rank of Professor at SDSU in EECS. Standards documents are available upon request.</li><li>Evidence of effective leadership and administrative skills including management of academic and research programs, managing complex budgets, fiscal matters, and/or personnel within an academic setting.</li><li>Experience securing nationally competitive grants for research from federal, industry, and/or corporate sources.</li><li>An understanding of the land-grant mission.</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills.</li><li>Familiarity with ABET accreditation processes and procedures, or experience as an ABET Program Evaluator/Team Chair.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Experience mentoring faculty in developing strategies for pursuing external funding and in creating strong research programs.</li><li>Experience in academic administration, including the development, evaluation and oversight of undergraduate academic programs, curricula and/or instructional operations.</li><li>Active engagement in technical societies such as the IEEE and ACM.</li><li>Experience with collaboration across disciplines and/or with multiple stakeholders</li><li>Experience with recruitment, retention, and success of faculty, staff and students from a variety of backgrounds.</li><li>Experience with successfully leading a department through an ABET accreditation visit.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a 1.) cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, 2.) curriculum vitae, 3.) teaching statement (3-page limit, attached as “other”), 4.) research statement (3-page limit, attached as “writing or work sample”) and a 5.) reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Electrical Engr & Computer Science https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49209 2026-07-29T14:07:20-05:00 2026-07-29T14:07:22-05:00 Digital Accessibility Specialist <div>The Digital Accessibility Specialist helps ensure that university technology, digital content, and services are accessible to all users. This position provides support and training on assistive technology, evaluates digital content for accessibility compliance, and partners with departments across campus to promote accessibility best practices.</div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Support students, faculty, and staff in the use of assistive technology software and hardware.</li><li>Provide training and guidance on assistive technology tools and accessibility best practices.</li><li>Evaluate and remediate digital documents, web content, and other electronic materials to meet ADA and WCAG 2.1/2.2 Level AA standards.</li><li>Train university employees on creating accessible digital content and conducting basic accessibility evaluations.</li><li>Conduct accessibility testing of websites, applications, and digital resources using automated and manual testing methods.</li><li>Review VPATs (Voluntary Product Accessibility Templates) and assess software and technology purchases for accessibility compliance.</li><li>Collaborate with Information Technology Services and campus departments to address accessibility concerns before technology is implemented.</li><li>Stay current with accessibility standards, regulations, and industry best practices.</li></ul><div><strong>Preferred</strong> <strong>Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in a related field or equivalent combination of education and experience.</li><li>Experience supporting assistive technology and accessibility initiatives.</li><li>Knowledge of ADA requirements and WCAG 2.1/2.2 accessibility standards.</li><li>Strong communication, training, and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Experience in higher education.</li><li>Familiarity with assistive technologies, accessibility testing tools, and document remediation.</li><li>Experience reviewing VPATs and conducting accessibility assessments.</li><li>IAAP certification (CPACC, WAS, or similar) preferred.</li></ul><div>The Digital Accessibility Specialist plays an important role in creating an inclusive university environment by helping ensure that digital content, technology, and services are accessible to all students, employees, and visitors. This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact while collaborating with colleagues across campus to advance accessibility and equity.<br><strong><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position</strong></div> USD-Office of Accessibility https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49620 2026-09-01T15:40:26-05:00 2026-09-01T15:40:27-05:00 Assistant Professor of History <div><strong>Position Summary: </strong><br>The Department of History and Social Sciences at Northern State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of History. This position offers the opportunity to teach and mentor students in Early American History through the Civil War era while contributing to the department’s research culture and to university life more broadly. The anticipated start date is August 2027. <br><br><strong>Minimum Qualifications: </strong><br>• PhD in History, with a specialty in Early American History through the Civil War era; any focus within that broad period is welcome. ABD candidates with a definite completion date prior to the position’s start date may also be considered.&nbsp;<br>• Experience teaching or developing digital public history projects is preferred.&nbsp;<br>• Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate education Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach twelve credit hours per semester in introductory and upper-level American History courses. Beyond the classroom, the successful candidate will serve as an active member of the department and university community by:&nbsp;<br>• Directing student learning opportunities, including experiential learning and other applied student experiences&nbsp;<br>• Building and sustaining connections with community businesses and organizations to support student learning&nbsp;<br>• Advising students on career pathways • Supporting departmental student recruitment and retention efforts&nbsp;<br>• Engaging in research and scholarly activity • Maintaining a visible, engaged presence within the department and across campus&nbsp;</div> NSU-History https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48669 2026-06-17T14:50:56-05:00 2026-06-17T14:50:57-05:00 Postdoctoral Researcher, QE9076 <div>The Chen Lab in the Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences (BaTS) at the University of South Dakota (USD) Sanford School of Medicine (SSOM) invites applications for a Postdoctoral Fellow position in the field of Cardiovascular Regenerative Engineering, Medicine, and Technology, with a translational research focus. The fellow will work with Dr. William C.W. Chen and his team at USD and have the opportunity to conduct research in collaborating laboratories at world-leading institutions, such John’s Hopkins University, Harvard University, and Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT).<br><br></div><div>The candidate must have a PhD in Biomedical Sciences, Biological/Biomedical Engineering, Molecular/Cell Biology, Synthetic Biology, or a related biological, medical, or engineering field with excellent oral and written communication skills. The candidate must have solid wet-lab training and expertise in molecular biology techniques and mammalian cellular disease models, particularly in vitro models using cardiomyocytes or stem cells. Other preferred expertise or research experience includes molecular cloning, primary cardiac cell isolation, genome editing, high-throughput screening, transgenic animal models, rodent cardiac surgery, and rodent echocardiography. Preference will be given to candidates with background or experience in cardiac inflammatory/immune responses, metabolic perturbation/stability, and/or cardioprotective intervention.</div><div><br>The Postdoctoral Fellow will design, conduct, and interpret experiments and organize and publish the original research results in research journals. The Fellow will also support the lab manager and assume certain general responsibility for scientific operations of the laboratory. The Fellow is expected to provide supervision and guidance to junior lab members, including graduate and undergraduate students.</div><div><br>USD takes pride in its world-class research activities, outstanding research support and collaborative environment, and excellent educational programs and outreach endeavor. The division is based in the Lee Medical Building located on the USD main campus in Vermillion, SD. For more information, please visit the BaTS webpage: https://www.usd.edu/Academics/Colleges-and-Schools/sanford-school-of-medicine/Divisions-and-Departments/Biomedical-and-Translational-Sciences.<br><br>The USD School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required until the move is complete.<br><br></div><div>Applicants MUST complete the application process through the University of South Dakota’s on-line application system at: https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. The application should include a cover letter with past/current research experiences and achievements, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. <br><br>Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.<br><br><strong>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</strong></div> Biomedical & Translational Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49468 2026-08-20T10:41:21-05:00 2026-08-20T10:41:22-05:00 Department Assistant (QE9678) <div>The Office of Medical Student Affairs is a great place to make a difference!<br><br>This student-centered department is seeking a highly motivated, detail oriented support person to join its close-knit team. The position will assist with managing the MSA office and providing administrative support to the Senior Academic Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, the SSOM financial aid office and play a vital role in supporting both students and leadership within the Sanford School of Medicine.&nbsp;<br><br>The position requires a professional who can<br><br></div><ul><li>Successfully manage competing priorities,</li><li>Meet strict deadlines,</li><li>Maintain accurate records while utilizing data management systems and Microsoft Office applications,</li><li>Strong commitment to confidentiality,</li><li>Exceptional customer service,</li><li>Communicate effectively,</li><li>and work collaboratively with students, faculty, and administrators</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>The USD Sanford School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical &amp; Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required.<br><br></em>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> Dean of Medical Student Affairs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49351 2026-08-11T11:34:28-05:00 2026-08-11T11:34:29-05:00 Advisor-Academics <div>South Dakota State University’s College of Nursing is seeking an Academic Advisor who is passionate about student growth and success. This role offers the opportunity to build meaningful connections with students while contributing to a collaborative and supportive academic environment. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a> and is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.</div><div><br>The <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/nursing\"><strong>College of Nursing</strong></a><strong> </strong>has a long history of exceptional nursing education and this is recognized through its designation as a Center of Excellence in Nursing Education by the National League for Nursing. The college’s fully accredited Healthcare Simulation Center across all 3 sites is further evidence of our commitment to high quality education for all students. Nursing’s history of excellence, innovation and achievement across its graduate and undergraduate programs provides an excellent foundation for growth and innovation.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Advise pre-nursing and nursing students, monitor academic performance, and track progress toward graduation requirements.</li><li>Conduct interviews with prospective students and facilitate evaluation of transfer credits for admitted students.</li><li>Collaborate with the Director of Nursing Student Services (NSS) on recruitment and retention activities, including orientation for students entering the major.</li><li>Verify academic standing for purposes related to financial aid and the Board of Nursing.</li><li>Assist with the distribution and review of applications for admission to the nursing major.</li><li>Maintain accurate and up-to-date student records in accordance with college requirements.</li><li>Coordinate with the NSS Program Assistant I to ensure timely communication with prospective and enrolled students.</li><li>Work closely with campus partners such as the Registrar, Admissions, and Financial Aid offices to support student success.</li></ul><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree related to duties completed by date of application;</li><li>At least one year of experience in Counseling, Advising, Education, or other related field;</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively with a variety of audiences;</li><li>Excellent oral and written communication skills;</li><li>Demonstrated organizational and time management skills; and</li><li>Valid driver's license or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire, and a willingness to travel.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Demonstrated experience with evaluating transcripts and new student orientation.</li><li>Demonstrated experience with Banner Student or other student information systems.</li></ul><div><strong><br>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Undergraduate Nursing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49680 2026-09-04T16:52:44-05:00 2026-09-04T16:52:44-05:00 Training and Development Coordinator <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking a <strong>Training and Development Coordinator</strong> to help build and deliver a comprehensive employee training and development program that supports faculty, staff, supervisors, managers, and institutional leaders. This is an exciting opportunity to join a forward-thinking Human Resources team and play a key role in advancing employee growth, leadership development, and organizational excellence across the university.<br><br></div><div>At USD, we are moving beyond one-time training events to create meaningful learning experiences that foster competency development, demonstrated application, and professional mastery. As the Training and Development Coordinator, you will help design learning programs, coordinate training initiatives, support leadership development programming, administer learning platforms, and partner with subject matter experts across campus to strengthen training quality and effectiveness.</div><div><strong>What You'll Do<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Design and coordinate engaging in-person, virtual, and online learning experiences.</li><li>Develop training materials, job aids, guides, and competency-based learning tools.</li><li>Administer learning management systems and track participation, completion, and learning outcomes.</li><li>Coordinate leadership and supervisor development programs.</li><li>Partner with academic and administrative units to improve training content, accessibility, and effectiveness.</li><li>Support the creation of role-based learning pathways for employees at all levels.</li><li>Analyze training data and provide insights to support continuous improvement and organizational development initiatives.</li><li>Help build a culture of continuous learning and professional growth across the university.</li></ul><div><strong><br>What We're Looking For<br></strong><br></div><div>Successful candidates will bring a combination of creativity, organization, relationship-building, and a passion for helping others develop.</div><div><br><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Human Resources, Education, Organizational Development, Communication, or a related field.</li><li>At least two years of related professional experience.</li><li>Experience coordinating training programs, facilitating learning experiences, instructional design, learning management systems, or employee development initiatives.</li><li>Excellent communication, project management, and organizational skills.</li><li>Ability to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders across a complex organization.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Experience developing competency-based learning programs.</li><li>Experience with leadership development programming.</li><li>Experience working in higher education or another large, decentralized organization.</li><li>Strengths Certification or similar professional development credentials.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Why Join USD?<br></strong><br></div><div>The University of South Dakota is committed to supporting the success of its people. This position offers a unique opportunity to help shape the future of employee learning and development while partnering with leaders across campus to create impactful growth opportunities.<br><br></div><div>Join a team dedicated to developing talent, strengthening leadership, and fostering a culture of continuous improvement and lifelong learning.</div> USD-Human Resources https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49051 2026-07-20T10:01:39-05:00 2026-07-20T10:01:40-05:00 Head Start Teacher Aide <div><strong>USD Head Start is seeking a caring, energetic Teacher Aide to join our Head Start classroom in the Tea School District.</strong><br>In this role, you’ll support a positive, engaging learning environment for children ages 3–5 and work closely with the Head Start Teacher to help each child reach important developmental milestones.<br><br></div><div><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></div><ul><li>Supervise children in the classroom and on the playground</li><li>Support daily learning activities and routines</li><li>Assist the Head Start Teacher in implementing developmentally appropriate practices</li><li>Help create a safe, nurturing, and inclusive environment for all children</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Position Details</strong></div><ul><li>Full‑time, 40 hours per week</li><li>Schedule: Monday–Friday, 7:45 a.m. – 4:15 p.m.</li><li>9.5‑month position (August 16 – May 31 annually)</li><li>Benefits‑eligible role with the State of South Dakota</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Child Development Associate (CDA) Credential preferred, willing to get one within two years</li><li>Experience working with young children required</li><li>A passion for supporting early learning and child development</li></ul> USD-Head Start https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49564 2026-08-28T08:54:43-05:00 2026-08-28T08:54:44-05:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div><strong>Position Summary</strong></div><div>The Department of Geology and Geological Engineering at South Dakota Mines is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to support a newly funded U.S. Department of Energy project focused on advanced sensing and characterization for critical minerals. The postdoctoral</div><div>researcher will primarily lead and support research in experimental rock mechanics, block-scale laboratory testing, and mechanical development of sensing tool prototypes. The position will involve close collaboration with an interdisciplinary team. This is a full-time, benefited position.<br><br></div><div><strong>Primary Responsibilities</strong></div><div>The successful candidate will contribute to the following activities:</div><ul><li>Design, prepare, and characterize synthetic rock blocks for controlled laboratory experiments.</li><li>Develop and conduct block-scale experiments under relevant subsurface conditions.</li><li>Assist with the mechanical design, fabrication, assembly, and integration of downhole tools.</li><li>Design experimental fixtures, pressure chambers, tool housings, and other mechanical components.</li><li>Install and integrate sensors, instrumentation, data-acquisition, and experimental control components.</li><li>Contribute to technical reports, project meetings, journal publications, and conference presentations.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>A Ph.D. in geological engineering, petroleum engineering, mechanical engineering, civil engineering, geomechanics, rock mechanics, or a closely related field by the position start date.</li><li>Strong background in experimental rock mechanics, geomechanics, or rock-physics testing.</li><li>Demonstrated hands-on experience in laboratory experiment design, equipment operation, or experimental system development.</li><li>Ability to independently plan, conduct, troubleshoot, and document laboratory experiments.</li><li>Strong written and oral communication skills.</li><li>Ability to work independently and effectively within a multidisciplinary research team.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><div>Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable:</div><ul><li>Preparation, casting, machining, or characterization of synthetic rocks, geomaterials, or ore analogs.</li><li>Mechanical design using SolidWorks, AutoCAD, or similar software.</li><li>Downhole tools, wireline logging systems, drilling tools, or subsurface instrumentation.</li><li>Prototype development, machining, fabrication, and assembly.</li><li>Sensors, data-acquisition, signal conditioning, control systems, or experimental automation.</li><li>Pressure vessels, sealing systems, high-pressure fluid systems, and mechanical testing fixtures.</li></ul><div><br><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 28, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter describing relevant research experience, technical qualifications, and interest; a current curriculum vitae; one to three selected publications or technical work samples; and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Geology & Geological Engineering 1 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/44461 2025-07-09T15:13:23-05:00 2025-07-09T15:13:24-05:00 Facility Worker - Student Life Building Services (Various Shift Opportunities) <div>Looking for a rewarding career with great benefits and paid time off? Join our team! Student Life Building Services is a highly dedicated team of individuals who ensure building safety, security, and cleanliness of SDSU’s residence halls, student union and Miller Wellness Center.<br><strong><br>Job Responsibilities:</strong> Ensure building safety, security, cleanliness, and setups meet the needs in accordance with SDSU Wellness Center, Residential Life, and Student Union standards.<br> <strong><br>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong><br> <em>Knowledge of:</em></div><ul><li>Cleaning equipment, and cleaning chemicals.</li></ul><div><br><em>Skill &amp; Ability to:</em></div><ul><li>Operate cleaning equipment</li><li>Communicate effectively, orally and in writing</li><li>Follow oral and written instructions</li><li>Lift and carry up to 65 pounds; move equipment and supplies up stairs</li><li>Work on a 3 to 6 ft ladder</li><li>Work in subzero temperatures and temperatures above 90 degrees</li><li>Associate positively and professionally with students, co-workers and the public</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Comments:</em></strong> Applicants should detail prior professional cleaning experience on their application. Multiple shifts available. Plus an on call rotation and occasional adjusted schedule.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Application Procedures:</em></strong> SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-University Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49228 2026-07-30T13:27:33-05:00 2026-07-30T13:27:33-05:00 Construction Project Manager <div>The individual will need experience managing construction projects of all sizes and scope. They will be responsible for client satisfaction, contract management, billing, design, construction administration, and project closeout. This position will complete project management from start to end and will be responsible for coordinating with campus departments, design professionals, operations and maintenance, construction, and project closeout. They will be required to manage the project efficiently so that the project is completed on budget and on schedule.<br><br>Preferred qualifications include an associate degree in Construction Management or a related field, a bachelor's degree in Construction Management or a related field, and 5+ years of commercial construction project management experience. A valid driver's license is required, and the position may require work outside of normal business hours.<br><br>Final classification and compensation will be based on the qualifications and experience of the final candidate.</div> USD-Planning and Construction https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49624 2026-09-02T08:26:52-05:00 2026-09-02T08:26:53-05:00 Information Specialist <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is currently seeking an Information Specialist to join our Animal Science department. This position will play a critical role in the department’s three primary missions which are learning, discovery, and engagement. If you have a strong attention to detail and excellent writing, editing and proofreading skills then this position may be for you!</div><div><br>Tomorrow's animal and natural resources industry leaders gain the educational foundation they need in the Department of Animal Science. With our multidisciplinary approaches toward production efficiency, product enhancement and natural resources management, both our undergraduate and our graduate students gain strong skill sets.<br><br></div><div>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>This position will be responsible for preparing, coordinating, and developing Animal Science Department informational communications following university and department guidelines, meeting required deadlines as well as providing vital administrative services for faculty, staff, and students. <strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><strong><br>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong></div><div><strong>Knowledge of:&nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Proficient in Microsoft Office: Word, and Outlook</li><li>Knowledge of Microsoft Office: Excel, Publisher, PowerPoint</li><li>Computer processes related to website content and social media presence.</li><li>Modern office equipment</li><li>Grammar, punctuation, and spelling</li></ul><div><strong><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:</strong></div><ul><li>Write, proofread, and edit written materials.</li><li>Manage time and meet deadlines while balancing multiple projects at once.</li><li>Communicate effectively both verbally and in writing.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Previous experience developing newsletters or managing company social media</li></ul><div><strong><br>Application Procedures:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.<br><br></div><div>[SE8689; 11722]&nbsp;</div> SDSU- Animal Science https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48712 2026-06-23T08:08:02-05:00 2026-06-23T08:08:04-05:00 Mechanical Engineer <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) – Facilities &amp; Services is looking for a Mechanical Engineer to support the operation, maintenance, and repair of the Animal Resource Wing (ARW) and other campus buildings. In this role, you’ll manage facility maintenance, oversee repairs and alterations, and contribute to mechanical project planning and design across campus. This position will help ensure safe, reliable facilities that support our teaching and research mission.</div><div><br>The <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/facilities-services/energy-systems-sustainability\"><strong>Energy Systems Division of Facilities and Services</strong></a> manages the production and distribution of the heating and cooling for campus. Our staff of engineers and technicians continually assess new technologies and energy options to assure SDSU utilizes the most efficient and reliable systems both environmentally and fiscally.<br><br>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, SD</strong></a> and is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>This position is responsible for planning, designing, and managing Mechanical Engineering projects within the Animal Resource Wing (ARW) and throughout the campus. This includes contributing to and assisting with the oversight of maintenance, alteration, and repair services for campus buildings and utility systems. The goal is to meet the needs of campus clients and to support the institution’s teaching and research programs.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS:<br></strong><br></div><div>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:<br>· Earned Bachelor of Science degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field.</div><div>· Understanding of mechanical systems such as HVAC, plumbing, building automation, or utilities.</div><div>· Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings, specifications, and technical documents.</div><div>· Strong analytical and problem‑solving abilities.</div><div>· Proficiency with engineering software (e.g., AutoCAD, Revit, or similar tools).</div><div>· Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines.</div><div>· Effective written and verbal communication skills.</div><div>· Ability to work collaboratively with contractors, maintenance staff, and campus stakeholders.</div><div>· Commitment to safety and compliance.</div><div>· Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>· Valid driver’s license</div><div><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:<br>· Master of Science in Mechanical Engineering</div><div>· At least one year of relevant engineering experience</div><div>· Professional Engineering license</div><div>· Experience in facility maintenance, construction, or project management</div><div><strong><br>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Energy Systems https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49474 2026-08-20T13:42:55-05:00 2026-08-20T13:42:55-05:00 Operations Coordinator <div>The Beacom School of Business at The University of South Dakota is a vibrant, internationally accredited business school that has served students since 1927. It is the State’s flagship business school and a regional leader with consistently high national rankings.<br><br>We are seeking a self-motivated, detail-oriented, and customer service-focused individual to provide support to the Prairie Family Business Association (PFBA), a Beacom School of Business outreach center. PFBA helps family businesses thrive through generations by providing a resource network for family business success.<br><br>Main responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Provide excellent customer service to PFBA members, sponsors, advisors, program participants, and partners</li><li>Manage membership, sponsorship, and program invoicing, collections, and payment processing</li><li>Complete financial transactions and maintain accurate records in Banner Finance</li><li>Administer vendor contracts, purchasing processes, reimbursements, and vendor payments</li><li>Maintain accurate member, sponsor, and participant information in HubSpot CRM</li><li>Coordinate program and event registrations and assist participants with registration, payment, travel, and logistical questions</li><li>Provide executive assistant support to the Executive Director, including scheduling, meeting preparation, travel coordination, and follow-up</li><li>Provide administrative support to the entire PFBA team</li><li>Coordinate day-to-day office operations and maintain organized electronic and physical records</li><li>Follow University and Board of Regents policies and procedures related to financial, purchasing, contracting, and administrative activities</li><li>Manage multiple competing priorities and ensure deadlines and follow-up activities are completed</li></ul><div><br>Preferred qualifications:<br>• Strong customer service focus with excellent oral and written communication skills.<br>• Excellent attention to detail with proven ability to prioritize and problem solve.<br>• Proficient in all Microsoft Office applications.<br>• Aptitude for or experience in data entry, analysis, and reporting.<br>• Able to work independently with little direct supervision.<br>• Limited flexible hours and locations may be required for events.<br>• Experience using Banner, WordPress, and HubSpot (CRM) software<br>• Office management experience.<br><br>Education/Experience:<br>• Bachelor’s degree preferred, ideally in business, communications, or related field.<br>• The preferred applicant will have experience in customer service, communications, or office management.<br><br><br></div> USD-School of Business https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49376 2026-08-12T16:38:20-05:00 2026-08-12T16:38:21-05:00 Assistant Professor of Interior Design <div>Bring your creative vision and design expertise to South Dakota State University! The School of Design invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Interior Design. We are seeking a collaborative educator with a strong foundation in interior design or interior architecture and specialized expertise in one or more content areas such as materials, computer aided design software (Revit, Sketchup, Enscape), codes and regulations, design expertise in a curricular studio area (commercial, hospitality, education, civic, health care, residential). The position is typically 60% teaching. 30% research and 10% service. This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a> and is a tenure-track, 9-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/school-design\"><strong>The School of Design</strong></a> includes accredited degrees in the visual arts: graphic design, and studio arts and the built environment: architecture, interior design and landscape architecture. Collectively, School faculty form a collaborative teaching and research environment that values cross-program and interdisciplinary initiatives. The successful candidate will contribute to building national and international stature and recognition for the discipline, School and University.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDSU offers a 4-year CIDA and NASAD accredited Bachelor of Fine Arts in Interior Design degree. <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/school-design/interior-design\"><strong>The mission of Interior Design</strong></a> is to prepare graduates for professional practice or advanced study in interior design through research informed, design thinking infused and practice-based projects and opportunities.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Teach courses within the professional curriculum covering disciplinary content such as materials, computer aided design software (Revit, Sketchup, Enscape), codes and regulations, design expertise in a curricular studio area (commercial, hospitality, education, civic, health care, residential).</li><li>Provide service to the discipline, university, and community.&nbsp;</li><li>Teach in multi-disciplinary courses within the School of Design.</li><li>Conduct a research agenda with dissemination of peer reviewed products.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>A PhD in interior design or interior architecture; OR a bachelor’s or master’s degree in interior design or interior architecture AND a PhD in a related field by appointment start date.</li><li>Potential to develop and teach academic coursework in one or more of the disciplinary content areas.&nbsp;</li><li>Potential to conduct research with peer reviewed dissemination of products.</li><li>Effective written communication skills. &nbsp;</li><li>Effective verbal and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Evidence of teaching interior design or interior architecture at university level.</li><li>Record of service within the discipline, profession, or community.</li><li>NCIDQ certification or NAAB licensure.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div><strong>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a 1.) cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement as well as a statement of academic interest, 2.) Curriculum Vitae, 3.) a reference page with the contact information for three professional references, and 4.) a portfolio (25 page max. and 10MB max.) that demonstrates research, scholarship, teaching and/or service activity related to the position qualifications (links will not be reviewed). Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div> SDSU-School of Design https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49068 2026-07-20T12:37:36-05:00 2026-07-20T12:37:37-05:00 Peer Support Specialist <div>The Department of Addiction Counseling and Prevention at the University of South Dakota is hiring a Peer Support Specialist. This position will be responsible for providing a variety of services to participants involved in the Minnehaha Drug and DUI Courts. To provide these services, a variety of activities are required:</div><ul><li>Connecting participants to court related and non-court related resources</li><li>Support participants navigating resources and finding/utilizing transportation</li><li>Ensure participant’s understand requirements of Drug/DUI Court</li><li>Collect and report data as required</li><li>Attend court hearings, team meetings, and case reviews as needed</li><li>Participate in community outreach efforts</li><li>Work with the courts, legal professionals, probation/parole officers, and other key stakeholders</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Required Qualifications:</div><ul><li>Associate’s or technical school degree in a helping profession (social work, psychology, nursing, criminal justice, etc.)</li><li>Certified, or willing to become certified, as a Peer Support Specialist, Addiction Counselor, or Prevention Specialist</li></ul><div><br>Preferred Qualifications:</div><ul><li>Personal and/or work experience in the Treatment Courts</li><li>Familiarity with recovery processes, substance use disorder treatment, harm reduction, and criminal justice system protocols, particularly treatment courts</li><li>Basic computer skills for case documentation and reporting. Familiarity with case management software is an advantage</li><li>Strong interpersonal, listening, and verbal communication skills; ability to build rapport and trust with participants</li><li>Prior work experience where confidentiality and discretion were important</li><li>Ability to work independently</li></ul><div><br>The Peer Support Specialist is a grant funded position. The anticipated end date of the grant is 9/30/2029.<br><br>This position offers state health insurance and benefits, which includes a retirement plan with 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and 11 paid holidays.<br><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> Addiction Counseling & Prevention https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49577 2026-08-28T13:20:17-05:00 2026-08-28T13:20:18-05:00 Database Systems Engineer <div>SDState is seeking a skilled System Engineer specializing Microsoft Cloud Offerings (Azure, Intune, Microsoft 365, Entra) to join its IT Systems Administration Department. This role is ideal for well-organized, self-motivated team players who want to contribute to the Office of Information Technology’s (OIT) mission of providing technology, skills, and services that empower the university community. OIT is committed to creating an environment in which staff, faculty, and students will have opportunities to succeed and advance their career, education, and creative activities. This is an on-site position located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Located in the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IT8OnH5eIgQ&amp;feature=youtu.be\"><strong>vibrant community</strong></a> of Brookings, South Dakota, employees enjoy a welcoming environment ideal for families, students, young professionals, and retirees. The area offers abundant recreation, cultural attractions, dining, and entertainment—combining the charm of a small town with the energy and amenities of a thriving university community.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:</em></strong> As a Systems Engineer, you will provide technical support in planning, designing, installing, maintaining, programming, testing, and implementing systems, integration, endpoint management, and/or database software, hardware, and products to ensure efficient integration and functioning of SDSU’s IT systems. In this role, you’ll be part of a Systems Administration team that delivers high‑level 2nd and 3rdtier support, troubleshoots complex issues, and maintains seamless integration across SDState’s varied technology stack. Your work will directly empower staff, faculty, and students by driving stable, modern, and innovative platforms that support teaching, learning, and digital transformation across campus.<br><br></div><div><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em></div><ul><li>Endpoint management tools (Microsoft Intune and SCCM, Jamf, etc.)</li><li>Windows Server Roles and Features, including but not limited to Active Directory, DHCP, IIS, RADIUS, Web Server</li><li>Microsoft cloud offerings (Azure, M365)</li><li>VMWare virtualization, server hardware (Cisco UCS, HPE and Dell), and storage technologies (NetApp and Synology)</li><li>Database and database management technologies, including MSSQL</li><li>Linux OS familiarity</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:</div><ul><li>Problem solve across an integrated, multi-server environment</li><li>Work independently and research/resolve technical issues and solutions</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>Desired Qualifications:</em></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field or equivalent experience;</li><li>Minimum of 3 years technical experience;</li><li>Technical certifications in Microsoft or other industry certifications are highly desired.</li></ul><div><em>Other Skills:</em></div><ul><li>Be well-organized, self-motivated, a team player, able to work unsupervised and possess strong self-management skills.</li><li>Excellent verbal and written communications skills.</li><li>Ability to:<ul><li>Communicate directly with peers, managers, and clients while leading development to a complete and successful solution.</li><li>Analyze and maximize technical and operational performance characteristics based upon specified guidelines.</li><li>Organize, manage, and work on multiple projects and priorities.</li></ul></li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Application Procedures:</em></strong> SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco-free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-IT Systems Administration https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/45683 2025-10-15T12:43:27-05:00 2025-10-15T12:43:27-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Studio Art <div>Black Hills State University invites applicants for an adjunct instructor in Studio Art to teach 2D and/or 3D courses and potentially other courses on the Spearfish campus. Successful candidates must possess at least an M.F.A. and teaching experience in higher education is preferred.<br><br></div><div>Applications may be made online athttps://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Interested individuals should complete an online application and also attach a cover letter, c.v., copies of transcripts from graduate institutions, and the names and contact information of three references. For application assistance, contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Inquiries specific to the position and c.v.’s may be sent to Quintin.Owens@bhsu.edu.<br><br></div><div>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div><div><br><br></div> BHSU-School of Arts and Humanities https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49247 2026-07-31T16:49:22-05:00 2026-07-31T16:49:23-05:00 Senior Accountant <div>Black Hills State University seeks applicants to fill an Senior Accountant position.</div><div><br>DUTIES:</div><div>Acts as a paraprofessional to accounting and fiscal professionals by performing assigned accounting practices to assist with fundamental accounting and routine fiscal procedures. This position will assist bank reconciliations, general ledger entries, department billing along with other duties as assigned.</div><div><br>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:</div><div>Generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), practices, and standards, analyze and interpret financial data and information and reach conclusions, establish and maintain effective working relationships with coworkers, managers, and representatives of other agencies or departments.</div><div><br>REQUIREMENTS:</div><ul><li>A Bachelor’s degree with an emphasis in accounting is required OR three or more years of accounting experience.</li></ul><div>PREFERRED:</div><ul><li>Higher education accounting and Banner accounting experience is preferred.</li></ul><div><br>COMMENTS:<br>Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br>TO APPLY:</div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7CRuth.Moore%40bhsu.edu%7Cc409047222fd4629e61c08dc1d1fad9e%7C9bfcf28b3a114fd7a8138f519cdb0db2%7C0%7C0%7C638417269101443805%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=OInp1QM3QsDp9MGq5PEHddr5nmdnDTx1OwPnwZ4HKgY%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Candidates will need to attach a cover letter, resume and the names/contact information of at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date August 6, 2026 at 11pm mountain time. For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may directed towards Rob Houdek at&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:rob.houdek@bhsu.edu\"><strong>rob.houdek@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.</div><div><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Administrative Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49629 2026-09-02T10:56:01-05:00 2026-09-02T10:56:02-05:00 Speech-Language Pathologist <div>The University of South Dakota invites applications for a full-time, ten or eleven-month Speech-Language Pathologist position based in Sioux Falls within the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders.<br><br></div><div><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Master's degree in speech-language pathology.</li><li>Ability to provide clinical education and supervision.</li><li>Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as an SLP.</li><li>Possession of or eligibility for South Dakota state licensure as an SLP.</li><li>ASHA CCC-SLP certification or eligibility.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Supervise SLP graduate student clinicians at the Scottish Rite Children's Clinic for Language and Speech.</li><li>Provide direct clinical services to patients across a broad spectrum of speech-language pathology practice areas, including articulation and phonological disorders, receptive and expressive language disorders, fluency, voice and resonance, social communication, cognitive-communication, augmentative and alternative communication (AAC), and accent modification.</li><li>Conduct comprehensive dyslexia evaluations and provide evidence-based intervention services for children and adolescents experiencing reading and written language difficulties.</li><li>Mentor and educate graduate student clinicians in evidence-based assessment and intervention practices.</li><li>Contribute to the department, college, and university through service.</li><li>Collaborate with faculty, clinical staff, and community partners to support the clinical education mission of the program.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Salary:</strong> Commensurate with qualifications.<br><br></div><div><strong>Application Review:</strong> Ongoing until the position is filled.<br><br></div><div>We look forward to welcoming a new member to our team who is passionate about advancing the field of speech-language pathology through clinical practice and the mentorship of future clinicians.</div> USD-Communication Sciences & Disorders https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48782 2026-06-29T09:53:02-05:00 2026-06-29T09:53:03-05:00 Vice President for Institutional Advancement <div>Dakota State University (DSU) invites applications and nominations for the position of Vice President for Institutional Advancement and President/CEO of the Dakota State University Foundation. Reporting to the Foundation Board of Trustees and serving as a member of the DSU President’s Cabinet, the Vice President provides strategic leadership for the university's comprehensive advancement program while serving as the chief executive officer of the DSU Foundation.<br><br></div><div>Dakota State University is experiencing unprecedented momentum in enrollment growth, academic innovation, research investment, and philanthropic engagement. As DSU continues to expand its national reputation as a leader in cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies, the university seeks an accomplished fundraising executive who can build on this momentum and secure transformational philanthropic investments that advance its mission and strategic priorities.<br><br></div><div>The Vice President serves as the university's chief fundraising officer and principal philanthropic ambassador, leading efforts to cultivate, solicit, and steward major gifts while strengthening relationships with alumni, donors, corporations, foundations, and community partners. Working closely with the President, Foundation Board of Directors, university leadership, and key stakeholders, this individual will play a critical role in advancing institutional priorities and creating opportunities that transform the lives of students and strengthen the future of DSU.<br><br><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide strategic leadership for all advancement and Foundation activities, including fundraising, donor relations, alumni engagement, stewardship, communications, and Foundation operations.</li><li>Serve as the university's chief fundraiser, personally cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major, principal, planned, corporate, and foundation gifts.</li><li>Develop and execute comprehensive fundraising strategies and campaigns that achieve ambitious philanthropic goals and increase long-term institutional support.</li><li>Partner with the President, Foundation Board, and university leadership to identify and advance funding priorities that support student success, academic excellence, research, and innovation.</li><li>Expand and strengthen relationships with alumni, donors, corporations, foundations, and community leaders.</li><li>Provide leadership and oversight of the Dakota State University Foundation, ensuring sound governance, financial stewardship, and growth of Foundation assets and endowment resources.</li><li>Lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing advancement team committed to excellence, collaboration, and results.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>A bachelor's degree is required.</li><li>The successful candidate will possess a demonstrated record of success in fundraising, advancement leadership, donor engagement, and organizational management.</li><li>Experience securing major and principal gifts, building strategic partnerships, and working effectively with governing boards and senior leaders is essential.</li><li>The ideal candidate will be a collaborative leader, exceptional communicator, strategic thinker, and relationship builder who is energized by philanthropy and inspired by the opportunity to advance a bold institutional vision.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply</strong>:<br> DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please submit a cover letter, resume, transcript, and a list of at least three professional references. <br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:Alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>Alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br><br></div> DSU-President https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49502 2026-08-24T09:30:21-05:00 2026-08-24T09:30:22-05:00 Postdoctoral Researcher <div>The Department of Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science at South Dakota Mines is seeking applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher. This is a full-time, benefited position. The Postdoctoral Researcher supports the department’s and institution’s objectives by advancing cutting-edge electromagnetic sensor research, strengthening externally funded research activities, contributing to student training, and enhancing innovation and technology development in engineering and applied science. This position will be responsible for conducting independent and collaborative research in electromagnetic sensor systems, including theoretical analysis, numerical modeling, AI-assisted sensing algorithm development, and experimental validation<br><br></div><div><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>An earned PhD degree at the time of hire in the field of Electrical Engineering and with expertise in applied electromagnetic and microwave imaging algorithm development.</li><li>3 years of experience in applied electromagnetics.</li><li>Familiar with FEKO/HFSS/CST, ADS, and Matlab.</li><li>Experience in antenna design, fabrications, and measurements.</li><li>Ability to analyze complex data and generate microwave images.</li><li>Strong laboratory skills and hands-on experience with experimental setups.</li><li>Excellent communication, problem-solving, and collaboration abilities.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 24, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a curriculum vitae, and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Electrical Engineering & Computer Science https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/46910 2026-02-04T10:37:47-06:00 2026-02-04T10:37:48-06:00 Instructional Designer <div>&nbsp;<strong>Position Summary:</strong> <br>Northern State University seeks a collaborative faculty-support professional to lead instructional design initiatives and coordinate Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL) operations in support of continuous improvement in teaching and learning. <br><br>A key priority is helping NSU faculty leverage Northern’s unique e-learning mission to enhance teaching and learning across all modalities, including on campus, online, and HyFlex. <br><br><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong> <br>* Faculty Support &amp; Instructional Design <br>• Guide course development and improvement across all modalities (on campus, online, and HyFlex) using best practices in instructional and universal design. <br>• Lead the Quality Assurance Review process for online and HyFlex courses. <br>• Consult with faculty on course design, technology integration, experiential learning, and digital tools. <br>• Ensure compliance with accreditation standards and federal regulations in coordination with Online Learning and Continuing Education. Leadership in Pedagogy <br>• Champion experiential learning and support faculty in adopting new technologies, expanding student engagement, and redesigning assessments to support student learning outcomes.<br> • Design and deliver trainings, including creating micro-credentials for online and HyFlex instruction. <br>• Share research in teaching and learning, assessment, teaching innovations, and student success through CETL communications and strategic initiatives. CETL Program Coordination<br> • Manage CETL events, trainings, communications, and day-to-day operations. <br>• Supervise CETL graduate assistant and technology fellow. Represent NSU in SDBOR and COPLAC teaching networks and coordinate faculty mentoring efforts.<br><br><strong>Knowledge of</strong>: <br>* Pedagogy, learning management systems, learning theories, technologies and computer software. <br><br><strong>Skill &amp; Ability to:</strong> <br>Communicate effectively, maintain confidentiality, collaborate across faculty of various ranks and disciplines, prioritize daily tasks while advancing long-term goals, host events and trainings, organize an office and manage student employees, and maintain detailed records. <br><br><strong>Education and Experience: </strong>Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. Degree in instructional design, technology, pedagogy, education, preferred.&nbsp;<br><br><br></div> NSU-Graduate School https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49410 2026-08-14T16:06:37-05:00 2026-08-14T16:06:39-05:00 Building Maintenance Specialist - HVAC <div>Dakota State University is seeking applications for a full-time Building Maintenance Specialist - HVAC. This position is responsible for maintaining existing plumbing, heating and cooling systems on the facilities and installing new systems according to state code. The position will report to the Assistant Director of Facilities Trades. <br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Create estimates for new installations of HVAC equipment and plumbing systems.</li><li>Troubleshoot, repair, and upgrade HVAC and plumbing systems.</li><li>Replace and maintain plumbing fixtures (sinks, toilets, etc.)</li><li>Track the service and inspection dates for air handlers, air compressors, HVAC pumps, chillers, A/C units, water softeners, food service equipment, etc.</li><li>Timely response to work orders.</li><li>Track project time, effort, and expenses.</li><li>Perform preventative maintenance on equipment and systems.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Requirements:</strong></div><ul><li>EPA Refrigeration Certification is required or must be obtained.</li><li>Technical degree in HVAC or a related field is required.</li><li>State of South Dakota Plumbing or Electrical license is preferred.</li><li>1 – 3 years of relevant work experience is preferred.</li><li>Ability to follow written and oral instructions.</li><li>Ability to operate required equipment.</li><li>Knowledge of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and Outlook).</li><li>Ability to work independently.</li><li>Ability to lift up to 50lbs regularly.</li><li>Ability to maintain a valid driver's license.</li><li>Deal tactfully and work effectively with others.</li><li>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability coverage</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply</strong>: <br> DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please submit a resume and a list of at least three references.<br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br> Applications will begin to be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled.<br><br>5/20/26 - Updated Requirements</div> DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49074 2026-07-21T08:50:55-05:00 2026-07-21T08:50:56-05:00 Klingbeil Endowed Department Head and Professor <div>The Department of Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering at South Dakota State University (SDState) invites applications for the Klingbeil Endowed Department Head and Professor. We are seeking a visionary and dynamic leader with a strong record of scholarship, teaching, and service, who can provide strategic direction and foster excellence in education, research, and Extension outreach. The Department Head will report directly to the Dean of the College of Agriculture, Food, and Environmental Sciences. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>. This position is a 12-Month administrative appointment with an academic rank of Professor, full-time, benefits-eligible position.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering (ABE) is a dynamic, collaborative community advancing education, research, and outreach in agriculture and engineering. The department offers undergraduate programs in Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering, Agricultural Systems Technology, and a joint Precision Agriculture program with the Department of Agronomy, Horticulture and Plant Science, along with graduate programs including an M.S. and Ph.D. in Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering. Faculty and students engage in innovative research and Extension activities in areas such as precision agriculture, bioprocessing, livestock systems, land and water management, and 4-H STEM education. ABE houses the Mesonet, South Dakota’s live weather network, and the Water Resources Institute, providing leadership on critical water challenges. We offer a collaborative environment where faculty, staff, and students work together to tackle real-world challenges and make a meaningful impact. Learn more at https://www.sdstate.edu/agricultural-biosystems-engineering.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>The Klingbeil Endowed Department Head of Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering serves as the academic and administrative leader of the department. The Department Head will:</div><ul><li>Provide strategic leadership for the department’s teaching, research, and Extension programs, ensuring excellence and relevance in all areas.</li><li>Establish goals and objectives, foster collaboration, and build strong relationships within the department, across campus, and with stakeholders throughout the state.</li><li>Recruit, mentor, evaluate, and retain faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Develop and manage departmental budgets, coordinate fundraising efforts, and oversee revenue-generating activities.</li><li>Oversee management and maintenance of departmental facilities and resources.</li><li>Facilitate research and intellectual property development opportunities for faculty and students.</li><li>Represent the department in official communications with the college, university, industry partners, and other external stakeholders.</li><li>Maintain an active program of research, scholarship, and/or teaching consistent with the rank of Professor, contributing to the department’s academic mission.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><strong><br>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</div><ul><li>Ph.D. Degree in Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering, Precision Agriculture, or a closely related field completed by date of application;</li><li>At least five years of directing/supervising experience;</li><li>Eligible for the rank of Professor at SDState in Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering, Precision Agriculture, or a closely related field;</li><li>Productive history in research, teaching, or Extension outreach;</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively with a variety of audiences;</li><li>Excellent verbal and written communication skills;</li><li>Demonstrated organizational and time management skills;</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills;</li><li>Ability to work as a contributing team member;</li><li>Demonstrated use of technology in managing and/or delivering educational programs;</li><li>Demonstrated ability or potential to plan, develop, implement, and evaluate educational materials and direct effective programs.</li><li>Ability to advocate ABE programs to and collaborate with a variety of stakeholders and allied industries;</li><li>Show a commitment to and understanding of agriculture, public service, and the university’s mission and goals;</li><li>Authorized to work in the United States. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</li><li>Valid driver’s license, or ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire, and willingness to travel.</li></ul><div><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</div><ul><li>Recognized nationally or internationally in field of expertise;</li><li>Ability to manage personnel and budgets;</li><li>Demonstrated collaboration in securing resources to support new and/or enhanced departmental programs and services;</li><li>Ability to foster a student-centered environment;</li><li>Familiarity with agricultural and conservation practices in the Midwest and Great Plains regions;</li><li>Commitment to public service;</li><li>Demonstrated understanding of the Land Grant University philosophy and system.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Ag, Food & Environmental Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49588 2026-08-31T09:07:51-05:00 2026-08-31T09:07:52-05:00 Senior Building Maintenance Worker <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Facilities<br><br></div><div><strong>STARTING HOURLY RATE: </strong>Minimum of $18.45+ per hour, depending upon education and experience, GE<br><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE:</strong> Responsible for paint and wall repair in remodeling and renovation projects including painting walls, ceilings, metal doors and frames.. General maintenance duties include basic plumbing work on drains, faucets, etc. installing light bulbs and shelves; moving furniture, hanging pictures; repairing and replacing stair tread, handrails, doors, hardware and ceiling tiles; completing roof inspections and making minor repairs and maintenance; repairing damaged floor coverings (carpet, VCT, wood, ceramic tile and cove base), removing old floor coverings, preparing surface and installing new floor coverings; snow removal; preventative maintenance tasks; assisting in grounds, custodial, and shop departments; and other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge of:</strong></div><ul><li>methods and practices of general building or facility maintenance;</li><li>building construction;</li><li>tools and equipment associated with the project.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Ability to:</strong></div><ul><li>communicate information clearly and concisely, exercising tact, patience, discretion and professional demeanor;</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner;</li><li>work independently, prioritize assigned work, establish timetables, and meet deadlines;</li><li>read and understand blueprints and drawings, and follow instructions;</li><li>lift and carry heavy items in excess of 50lbs, perform physical labor and work in all types of extreme temperatures or weather conditions;</li><li>work from ladders, scaffolding or in confined areas;</li><li>operate required tools and equipment;</li><li>direct the work of others;</li><li>provide outstanding customer service.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>COMMENTS: </strong>Valid driver’s license is required.<br><br></div><div><strong>To APPLY:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin September 8, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please complete application and provide resume (optional) and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Facilities Management https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49507 2026-08-24T10:48:17-05:00 2026-08-24T10:48:17-05:00 Accounting Assistant <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused Accounting Assistant to support the Enrollment Management organization. This position plays a critical role in ensuring the timely and accurate processing of financial transactions while providing exceptional service to faculty, staff, students, and external partners.<br><br></div><div>The Accounting Assistant serves as a key resource for accounting, purchasing, travel, and general administrative processes across the division. This position works closely with university departments, vendors, and employees to ensure compliance with institutional policies and procedures while maintaining accurate financial records.<br><br><em>Work Authorization: Employee must be authorized to work in the United State. This position is not eligible for sponsorship.</em></div> USD - Enrollment Management https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49259 2026-08-03T17:38:49-05:00 2026-08-03T17:38:50-05:00 Faculty, QE9811 (Physiology) <div>The Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences at the University of South Dakota Sanford School of Medicine invites applications for an Academic Biomedical Science Educator to teach Human Medical Physiology. This is a 12-month position, tenure track. Degree requirement: Ph.D. in Medical Physiology or closely related field OR Professional Degree at the doctoral level in the healthcare field. Applicants must have experience teaching systems Physiology to health science professionals (MD, PA, PT, OT students). Previous experience with problem-based/active learning pedagogy in a health sciences context is desired. Salary will be commensurate with training and experience. <br><br><em>The </em>USD<em> Sanford School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical &amp; Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required until the move is complete.<br></em><br></div><div>To apply, submit a curriculum vitae, a summary of teaching experience and interests, and contact information for three references. All materials must be posted to the University of South Dakota online employment website at <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>.<br><br>Review of applications will begin on September 7, 2026, and continue until position is filled.</div> Biomedical & Translational Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49642 2026-09-03T08:42:09-05:00 2026-09-03T08:42:10-05:00 Outreach & Event Coordinator <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Marketing &amp; Communications<br><br></div><div><strong>STARTING HOURLY RATE: </strong>$21.41-$23.99 hourly, depending upon education and experience, GG</div><div><br><strong>Position Summary:</strong></div><div>Support South Dakota Mines' public image and K-12 education pipeline by planning and executing public relations and K-12-focused events, and by developing community and K-12 outreach efforts that connect prospective students with Mines resources.</div><div><br><strong>Duties include:</strong></div><ul><li>Plan, organize, and execute public relations events and K-12 programming, such as the science fair and Engineering &amp; Science Week</li><li>Manage event budgets, including projections and expenditure tracking</li><li>Collaborate and coordinate events with other departments, university personnel, and outside entities</li><li>Serve as chair or participant on committees</li><li>Build and maintain a public-facing outreach webpage in partnership with Marketing &amp; Communications</li><li>Maintain a campus-wide inventory of K-12 and community outreach activities</li><li>Build relationships with area teachers and coordinate outreach events connecting them with SD Mines STEM faculty</li><li>Partner with the database administrator to track prospective students from outreach events</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned</li></ul><div><br><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>planning and effectively executing both large and small events;</li><li>public relations principles and practices for building and maintaining a positive public image;</li><li>K-12 education environments and effective approaches to engaging teachers and school partners;</li><li>professional office environment and procedures, including excellent interpersonal skills;</li><li>work processes and practices pertaining to public administration, management, and professional subject areas;</li><li>basic statistical measures, research methods, database development and maintenance;</li><li>high level of proficiency with computer systems and common applications (Google Calendar, Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel), including basic website content management.</li></ul><div><br>Ability to:</div><ul><li>communicate information clearly and concisely in person and/or writing, exercising tact, patience, discretion and professional demeanor;</li><li>organize work, manage multiple events and outreach relationships simultaneously, work independently and learn quickly;</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner with a variety of cultures and personalities, within a high-pressure environment;</li><li>build trust and sustain long-term relationships with external partners such as teachers and school contacts;</li><li>read, comprehend, gather, prepare, and summarize data from a variety of sources;</li><li>type accurately, be detail oriented, have excellent organizational skills, handle multiple tasks, prioritize accordingly and meet strict deadlines;</li><li>maintain confidential and sensitive information, including student data collected at outreach events;</li><li>use a computer, copy machine, and other office equipment;</li><li>provide excellent customer service.</li></ul><div><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 14, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Marketing & Communications https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48852 2026-07-06T14:56:25-05:00 2026-07-06T14:56:26-05:00 Department Head & Professor <div>The Department of Construction and Concrete Industry Management at South Dakota State University (SDState) invites applicants for the position of Professor and Department Head. We seek an innovative leader to advance academic programs, grow funded research, and strengthen outreach to stakeholders in the state and region. The individual selected for this role will work with the Dean and the leadership team for the Jerome J. Lohr College of Engineering (JJLCOE) to promote the land-grant mission while implementing a shared vision with the faculty and staff on strategic initiatives for the department.<strong> </strong>This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>. This is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible, tenure-track position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/construction-concrete-industry-management\"><strong>Department of Construction and Concrete Industry Management</strong></a> is one of five departments in the <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/jerome-j-lohr-engineering\"><strong>Jerome J. Lohr College of Engineering</strong></a>, serving 1500 undergraduate and graduate students.&nbsp; The 13-faculty-member CCIM Department serves 350 students in its undergraduate programs, which include Construction Management, Concrete Industry Management, and Manufacturing Automation and Electronics Engineering Technology. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Jerome J. Lohr College of Engineering has benefitted from substantial investment by its stakeholders in the past 15 years, resulting in new buildings, state-of-the-art teaching and research labs, and renovated classrooms.&nbsp; The five academic units are Civil &amp; Environmental Engineering, Construction &amp; Concrete Industry Management, Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science, Mathematics &amp; Statistics, and Mechanical Engineering.&nbsp; Engineering Extension, SD LTAP, the EDA University Center, and the Image Processing Lab provide outreach and services to the state and region.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>The Department Head of Construction and Concrete Industry Management serves as the academic and administrative leader of the department. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Provide leadership, strategy, and vision for the department and its programs in collaboration with faculty, staff, and other college and university administrators. This role will work towards advancing SDSU’s Pathway to Premier strategic plan, including transforming SDSU into R1 Research University by Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education.</li><li>Advance the department in all components of its mission: education and student advisement, research/creative activities, and industry and community engagement.</li><li>Supervise curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation activities through program and assessment coordinators and collaboration with faculty.</li><li>Create a supportive environment for faculty, graduate and undergraduate student research and extramural funding.</li><li>Recruit, mentor, develop, evaluate, and retain faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Manage and assign faculty workload and plan student throughput through the development of course schedules.</li><li>Advocate for the needs of the department’s programs, faculty, students, and staff.</li><li>Develop and manage departmental budgets and coordinate fundraising efforts.</li><li>Oversee management and maintenance of departmental facilities and resources.</li><li>Maintain an active program of teaching, research, and/or scholarship consistent with the rank of Professor for the agreed upon workload percentage, contributing to the department’s academic mission.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Earned doctorate in construction management, Civil engineering, or a closely related field by application date.</li><li>A record of achievement in academic leadership, teaching, scholarship, research and service commensurate with the performance expectations for a tenured full professor in the department.</li><li>Financial management experience including revenue, expenditures, and/or budgeting.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience in academic administration and/or parallel experience in the private industry sector.</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><br><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Professional experience at the middle manager level or higher within the construction or concrete industry management industry.</li><li>Experience with recruitment, and retention of faculty, staff, and students from various backgrounds.</li><li>Understanding of current and emerging trends in the construction and concrete industries as demonstrated by the candidate’s knowledge of rapidly changing workforce needs, and the implications on interdisciplinary education and research.</li><li>Experience implementing administrative policies.</li><li>Experience building relationships with regional industry leaders which led to collaboration.</li><li>Experience leading and managing ABET and other programmatic accreditation procedures.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><br>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp; Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. &nbsp; It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div> SDSU-Construction & Concrete Industry Management https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/47678 2026-04-08T09:01:41-05:00 2026-04-08T09:01:42-05:00 Assistant Professor QE9855 <div>The Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences at the University of South Dakota’s Sanford School of Medicine invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. We seek an energetic and collaborative individual that will interact with faculty within the Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences. The Division has current strengths in Neuroscience, Cardiovascular Science, Protein Quality Control, Cancer Biology and Microbiology/Immunology. Applicants must have a PhD in Biomedical Sciences or closely related OR M.D.<em> </em>and at least two years of post-doctoral experience is required. <br><br>Applicants should have strong potential for developing an innovative, independent, and translational research program that has or is likely to attract significant extramural funding. Experience in teaching Systems Physiology is required. In addition, the applicant should have the ability to mentor and teach graduate, health sciences and/or medical students. Excellent start-up funds, state-funded salary commensurate with experience and state-of-the-art research facilities will be provided. <br><br>The USD Sanford School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical &amp; Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required until the move is complete. <br><br>To apply, submit a curriculum vitae, a summary of past/current research and teaching experiences/interests, teaching philosophy, future plans for research and contact information for three references. All materials must be posted to the University of South Dakota online employment website at <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>.</div> Biomedical & Translational Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49433 2026-08-18T11:58:45-05:00 2026-08-18T11:58:45-05:00 Cook <div><strong>Make a Difference&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Join our team at the <strong>South Dakota School for the Blind and Visually Impaired</strong> and play an important role in creating nutritious, welcoming meals for our students. This full-time position offers the opportunity to work in a supportive school environment where your cooking skills directly contribute to the daily experience and well-being of students.</div><div><strong>Position Summary</strong></div><div>The Cook prepares meals and snacks according to established menus and recipes, serves students and staff, accommodates special dietary needs, and maintains a clean and sanitary kitchen and dining environment.</div><div><strong>Essential Duties</strong></div><ul><li>Prepare and cook meals and snacks according to established menus and recipes.</li><li>Prepare meals that meet individual student dietary requirements.</li><li>Serve meals to students, staff, and visitors.</li><li>Monitor food and supply needs and communicate shortages to the supervisor.</li><li>Set up and maintain the dining and food service areas.</li><li>Wash dishes and clean and sanitize kitchen, dining, and storage areas.</li></ul><div><strong>Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>High school diploma or equivalent preferred.</li><li>Previous cooking or food service experience preferred.</li></ul><div><strong>Physical Requirements</strong></div><div>This position requires extended periods of standing and the ability to perform food preparation, serving, dishwashing, cleaning, and other physical tasks associated with a school kitchen.</div><div><strong>If you enjoy cooking and want to make a meaningful difference in the lives of students, we invite you to apply!</strong></div> SDSBVI-Food Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49080 2026-07-21T15:33:46-05:00 2026-07-21T15:33:47-05:00 Assistant Director of Residential Life for Community and Connection <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an Assistant Director of Residential Life for Community and Connection in Housing and Residential Life. This position will provide collaborative leadership that advances Housing and Residential Life’s mission by cultivating environments where student communities, connection, and belonging are central to the residential experience and on campus experience. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota and is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.<br><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/housing-residential-life\"><strong>Housing &amp; Residential Life</strong></a> creates welcoming, supportive communities where students can thrive. Our team of professional and student staff work together to foster connection, growth, and a positive on-campus living experience.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>The Assistant Director of Residential Life for Community and Connection through intentional partnerships and evidence‑informed approaches, will create residential learning environments that promote holistic development, leadership development, meaningful engagement, service learning, and sustained student success<strong><em>. </em></strong>This is achieved through serving as the professional advisor for the Residence Hall Association, supervision of professional live-in Residence Hall Director staff, overseeing the training process for the Housing and Residential Life professional and para-professional staff, and serve as the department expert on community engagement within the residence halls.<br><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.<br><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree. Would be willing to consider a bachelor’s level candidate with four years of directly related experience, completed by start date;&nbsp;</li><li>At least three years of relevant work experience connected to student leadership, advising, campus housing, outreach, etc.;</li><li>Previous experience working in student leadership, student organizations, on campus housing (K-12 or higher education), advising, student success or outreach, service learning, or student affairs at an institution of higher education;</li><li>Supervision experience;</li><li>Effective written communication skills;</li><li>Ability to work as a contributing team member;</li><li>Effective verbal communication and interpersonal skills; and</li><li>Valid drivers license.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Graduate school degree in Student Personnel Administration, Guidance and Counseling, Higher Education, Student Affairs, or related field;</li><li>Relevant experiences such as student conduct experience, crisis/emergency experience, student leadership or advising experience, and/or programming experience;</li><li>Strong leadership skills;</li><li>Experience in community building in a college or university residential setting or advising student leadership programs specifically within housing and residential life areas;</li><li>Ability to motivate staff members and problem solve within a student-centered developmental model; and</li><li>Demonstrated organizational and time management skills.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-University Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49594 2026-08-31T11:15:17-05:00 2026-08-31T11:15:19-05:00 Facility Worker <div>SDSU Facilities &amp; Services is in search of motivated and dependable individuals to join our cleaning team as Facility Workers. No prior professional cleaning experience is needed. You bring your willingness to learn, and we will equip you with all the training and tools to complete the job. <br><br>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:</em></strong> Provide cleaning services to SDSU Academic and Athletic Buildings and to promote a clean and safe environment for students, staff, and the public. The work duties will include hard and soft surface floor maintenance, restroom care, classroom, and office detailing, building security, trash handling, as well as some exterior and miscellaneous maintenance tasks.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;<br><br><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em> &nbsp;</div><ul><li>Or willingness to learn how to operate basic computer software applications and various electronic systems.</li></ul><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Follow oral instructions.</li><li>Follow written instructions.</li><li>Stand for extended periods of time.</li><li>Bend, stretch, climb ladders, twist, and walk.</li><li>Lift up to 50 pounds.</li></ul><div><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><strong><em>Required License: </em></strong>Valid driver’s license&nbsp;<br><br><strong><em>Application Procedures:</em></strong> SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.<br>&nbsp;</div><div>[SE5287; 80214]&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Custodial Svc https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48873 2026-07-07T15:58:43-05:00 2026-07-07T15:58:44-05:00 Senior Secretary <div>The University of South Dakota School of Law invites applications for a Senior Secretary. This is a 12-month, Civil Service, regular position eligible for state benefits.<br><br>This position will serve in an administrative support capacity for law school faculty members and other Law School staff, as needed. They will also interact often with students, alum, and the community including frequent contact with practicing lawyers, judges, and professors from other law schools and disciplines. Thus, the successful applicant will reflect a high level of professionalism and cooperation.<br><br>Preferred skills include:<br>- Knowledge of modern office practices<br>- Demonstrated proficiency with modern office software to include Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Adobe.<br>- Ability to use general office equipment<br>- Ability to communicate effectively in oral and written form<br>- Ability to review and proof documents for accuracy, grammar, spelling, and punctuation<br>- Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with diverse people<br>- Ability to maintain strict confidentiality<br><br>Preferred professional skills include effective organizational skills and interpersonal skills at a level that can effectively support faculty and students. Familiarity with internet research, database research, legal research, legal writing and the practice or education of law is a plus.</div> USD-School of Law https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49520 2026-08-25T12:08:29-05:00 2026-08-25T12:08:30-05:00 Financial Aid Advisor <div>Black Hills State University is seeking a dynamic, student-focused professional to join our Student Financial Aid Office as a Financial Aid Advisor. This position is an integral part of the Enrollment Management team and is based on the Spearfish campus. <br><br>The Financial Aid Advisor serves as a key resource for students and families navigating the financial aid process. This position provides personalized financial aid counseling, supports the administration of federal and institutional aid programs, and helps students understand their options for financing their education. <br><br>The ideal candidate is approachable, organized, detail-oriented, and committed to helping students succeed. Financial aid can be complex, and we are looking for someone who can turn complicated regulations and processes into information students and families can understand and use. <br><br><strong>This position is grant funded for two years, with the intention of transitioning to a university-funded position following the grant period.</strong><br><br>Key Responsibilities:<br>• Provide comprehensive, individualized financial aid counseling to prospective and current students and their families regarding federal, state, institutional, and alternative financial aid programs.<br>• Explain financial aid eligibility, award requirements, policies, deadlines, and student responsibilities in a clear and student-friendly manner.<br>• Respond to student and family inquiries by phone, email, and in person with professionalism, accuracy, and a commitment to excellent customer service.<br>• Review and process financial aid information and documentation in accordance with federal, state, and university regulations.<br>• Manage Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) processes, including monitoring, student communication, and review of SAP appeals.<br>• Coordinate and administer the Federal Work-Study (FWS) program, including awarding, monitoring, tracking, and communication with students and campus departments.<br>• Utilize the National Student Loan Data System (NSLDS) and other federal and institutional systems to research student eligibility and financial aid history.<br>• Maintain accurate student records and ensure compliance with applicable federal, state, and university policies and regulations.<br>• Collaborate with campus partners across Enrollment Management and other university departments to support student enrollment and retention.<br>• Participate in financial aid outreach activities, including financial aid workshops, FAFSA information nights, student orientations, and other recruitment or enrollment events.<br>• Stay current on changes to federal and state financial aid regulations, institutional policies, and financial aid programs.<br>• Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned.<br><br>Minimum Qualifications:<br>• Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience.<br>• 1–3 years of general office or administrative experience.<br>• Strong written and verbal communication skills.<br>• Strong interpersonal and customer service skills with the ability to work effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, and campus partners.<br>• Ability to explain complex information clearly to individuals with varying levels of knowledge and experience.<br>• Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive student information appropriately.<br>• Ability to work independently while also contributing effectively as part of a collaborative team.<br>• Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.<br><br>Preferred Qualifications:<br>• Previous experience working in financial aid or higher education.<br>• Experience with Banner Student Information System (SIS) or another student information system.<br>• Knowledge of federal financial aid regulations, including FAFSA, Federal Pell Grant, Direct Loans, Federal Work-Study, and Satisfactory Academic Progress.<br>• Experience counseling students or providing financial aid advising.<br>• Experience working with NSLDS or other federal financial aid systems.<br><br>Comments:<br>Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br>To Apply:</div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7CRuth.Moore%40bhsu.edu%7Cc409047222fd4629e61c08dc1d1fad9e%7C9bfcf28b3a114fd7a8138f519cdb0db2%7C0%7C0%7C638417269101443805%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=OInp1QM3QsDp9MGq5PEHddr5nmdnDTx1OwPnwZ4HKgY%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Candidates will need to attach a cover letter, resume and the names/contact information of at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date August 31, 2026 at 11pm mountain time. For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may directed towards Tirzah Knight at Tirzah.Knight<a href=\"mailto:rob.houdek@bhsu.edu\"><strong>@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.</div><div><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Financial Aid https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49264 2026-08-04T08:47:39-05:00 2026-08-04T08:47:40-05:00 Grant Specialist I <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Office of Sponsored Programs<br><br></div><div><strong>STARTING HOURLY RATE: </strong>Minimum of $28.54 per hour, depending upon education and experience, GJ<br><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE: </strong>Monitoring compliance with applicable laws and rules and accounting and reporting systems. Creation/preparation of subaward documents and reverse contract for services, including completion of forms, certification requirements, interpretation of guidelines, and compliance with regulations. Review/approval of subaward invoices and expenditures. Processing all sub awardee change requests. Review of cost share documentation received from subawardees. Financial and data reporting including completion of reports for multiple agencies. Updating outside agency systems with our current information and other duties as assigned.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), practices and standards;</li><li>generally accepted auditing standards (GAAS).</li></ul><div>Ability to:</div><ul><li>develop subawards and reverse contract for services;</li><li>review/approve subaward invoices and expenditures;</li><li>interpret, comprehend and apply laws, rules and regulations for a variety of funding agencies and the State of SD;</li><li>research, compile and analyze data, providing high level of accuracy with attention to detail;</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner with students, faculty, staff and outside agencies;</li><li>communicate information clearly, concisely and accurately to others both in oral and written form, expressing ideas in a manner that the user can understand, exercising tact, patience and professional demeanor;</li><li>handle multiple tasks, prioritize accordingly and meet strict deadlines;</li><li>use a computer;</li><li>provide outstanding customer service.</li></ul><div><br><strong>COMMENTS: </strong>Occasional travel, including overnight stays, may be required.</div><div><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 4, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Sponsored Programs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49650 2026-09-03T11:35:55-05:00 2026-09-03T11:35:56-05:00 Assistant Athletic Trainer <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an Assistant Athletic Trainer to join our team. This role supports the coordination of athletic training services, ensuring the health and well-being of our student-athletes. From injury prevention and evaluation to rehabilitation and return-to-play management, this position plays a vital role in keeping athletes performing at their best. We’re looking for someone who is passionate about sports medicine and thrives in a team environment. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>This recruitment will fill two Assistant Athletic Trainer positions. The selected candidates will provide athletic training support for either Women's Basketball or Cross Country and Track &amp; Field.</div><div>SDState is an NCAA Division I institution and competes in the Summit League for all sports except football (Missouri Valley Football Conference), wrestling (Pac 12), and women’s equestrian (National Collegiate Equestrian Association).</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate and provide care for sport teams filtered through the main training room in the Sanford Jackrabbit Athletic Complex Athletic Training Room (especially sports assigned – women’s basketball and/or track/field and cross country).</li><li>Coordinate and follow up with physician clinics.</li><li>Assist with scheduling, supervision, and evaluation of athletic training students (ATS).</li><li>Assist with the administration of services related to the sports medicine program as requested (i.e. day to day operations/cleaning; limited insurance, setting up yearly physicals for student-athletes).</li><li>Play an active role in developing goals and objectives of the Athletic Training Education Program, specifically assisting with the design of clinical education and field experience.</li></ul><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training, Athletic Administration or Sports Science completed by appointment date;</li><li>At least one year of experience with intercollegiate athletics or clinical setting (an equivalent combination will be considered);</li><li>Effective communication (oral, written, and interpersonal) skills;</li><li>BOC certification for athletic training and CPR/First Aid certification or ability to obtain these certificates by employment;</li><li>Demonstrated organization and time management skills; and</li><li>Demonstrated computer application skills.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in Athletic Training, Kinesiology, Sports Medicine, Exercise Science, or Administration;</li><li>At least one year of experience supervising athletic training students;</li><li>Division I intercollegiate experience;</li><li>Experience providing athletic training services to the sport of women’s basketball and/or track/field and cross country;</li><li>Eligible for state license in South Dakota;</li><li>Experience with team travel responsibilities;</li><li>Knowledge and/or understanding of medical records following HIPAA, FERPA and Sportsware; and</li><li>Knowledge and/or understanding of medical insurance.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Intercollegiate Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48256 2026-05-21T10:11:03-05:00 2026-05-21T10:11:04-05:00 Nursing Faculty - Medical Surgical QE9766 <div>The Nursing Department of the University of South Dakota (USD) invites applications for a 9-month full-time nursing faculty position for the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program at the Vermillion campus.<br><br>This position includes responsibility for delivering high-quality classroom and clinical instruction; guiding students in the development of clinical judgment; and contributing to curriculum design and evaluation.<br><br>The ideal candidate brings strong clinical expertise in medical surgical nursing, excellent communication skills, interpersonal skills, and the ability to work collaboratively and independently. A commitment to student success and the ability to foster an engaging and supportive learning environment are essential.<br><br><strong>Required Qualifications</strong> Current, unencumbered RN license and eligibility for licensure in South Dakota. Minimum of a master’s degree in nursing from a nationally accredited program prior to starting the position.<br> <br><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong> Experience in medical surgical nursing. Experience teaching in a baccalaureate program. Strong nursing background with excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively within a team. Ability to work with technology.<br><br> Candidates must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> USD-Nursing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49435 2026-08-18T17:13:28-05:00 2026-08-18T17:13:29-05:00 Department Head for Mathematics and Statistics and Professor <div>The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (Math &amp; Stat) at South Dakota State University (SDSU) invites applicants for the Department Head and Professor position. We are looking for a dynamic and collaborative leader who is committed to providing a rigorous and practical educational experience with an emphasis on expanding federally funded research and graduate programs to support South Dakota State University’s R1 Our Way mission, as well as establishing and providing scientific support to local industry and government. This position is 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position, located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings SD</strong></a> and reports to the Dean of the Jerome J. Johr College of Engineering (JJLCOE). Anticipated start of January 2027.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Mathematics and Statistics offers the following undergraduate programs: AS in Data Science, BS in Data Science, and BS in Mathematics. The BS in Mathematics includes the following specialty areas: Actuarial/Financial Concentration, Applied Mathematics Concentration, Data Science Concentration, and Teaching Specialization. Graduate programs include the following: Data Science Certificate, MS in Data Science, MS in Mathematics, MS in Statistics, and PhD in Computational Science and Statistics. Many students in our vibrant graduate program serve in GTA and GRA positions. Currently, the department has approximately 180 undergraduate majors, 60 graduate students, 17 tenure-track faculty, and 9 full-time lecturers.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>The Department Head will work closely with the Dean and the leadership team of the JJLCOE to promote the land-grant mission and an ambitious agenda to address the world’s grand challenges in the areas of mathematics, statistics, and data science. The selected candidate is expected to be the leader in identifying future areas of growth and investment while providing organizational and administrative expertise to the Department and the College. The candidate is expected to steer the growth of the department consistent with SDSU’s refreshed strategic plan titled “Pathway to Premier 2030”. The strategic plan includes a goal to elevate SDSU as a research university and pursue a pathway to achieve designation as an R1 Research University by Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education.<br><br></div><div>It is imperative that this position maintains an understanding of current and emerging needs in mathematics, statistics, and data science to guide both research and teaching initiatives. It is the Department Head's responsibility to lead the faculty in their efforts to provide high-quality service courses at all levels, engage with client departments to determine their course needs, monitor trends in general education and service courses, and implement high-impact teaching and learning strategies. Along with leadership, the Department Head is an advocate for the Department of Mathematics and Statistics both within and outside the University, fostering a commitment to interdisciplinary and interagency collaboration</div><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Ph.D. in mathematics, statistics, data science, or closely related field by date of application.</li><li>A distinguished record of teaching, research, scholarship, and service consistent with eligibility for tenure and rank of Professor at SDSU in the Math &amp; Stat Department. Standards documents are available upon request.</li><li>Evidence of effective leadership and administrative skills including management of academic and research programs, managing complex budgets, fiscal matters, and/or personnel within an academic setting.</li><li>Experience securing competitive grants for research from federal, industry, and/or corporate sources.</li><li>An understanding of the land-grant mission.</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Experience mentoring faculty in developing strategies for pursuing external funding and in creating strong research programs.</li><li>Experience in academic administration, including the development, evaluation and oversight of undergraduate academic programs, curricula and/or instructional operations.</li><li>Experience interacting and cultivating relationships with businesses in the medical, insurance, and financial sectors in the region.</li><li>Familiarity with ABET accreditation process.</li><li>Engagement in professional organizations for mathematics &amp; statistics (e.g., SIAM, AMS, MAA, ASA, etc.)</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a 1). cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, 2.) curriculum vitae, 3.) teaching statement (3-page limit, attached as “other”), 4.) research statement (3-page limit, attached as “writing or work sample”) and a 5.) reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Mathematics & Statistics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49095 2026-07-22T11:21:44-05:00 2026-07-22T11:21:45-05:00 Part-Time Digital Accessibility Specialist <div>Dakota State University is seeking a temporary, part-time Digital Accessibility Specialist to support campus-wide accessibility initiatives. This position plays an important role in helping ensure that digital content is accessible to all users while supporting faculty, staff, and students in creating inclusive learning and working environments.<br><strong><br>Key Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with training and support on digital accessibility tools, techniques, and best practices.</li><li>Review and remediate digital documents, including Word, PowerPoint, PDF, and other electronic materials, to ensure compliance with accessibility standards.</li><li>Help faculty and staff create and format accessible course materials, communications, and resources.</li><li>Conduct accessibility evaluations using approved tools such as Microsoft Accessibility Checker and other accessibility testing resources.</li><li>Support the creation of accessible multimedia content by assisting with captioning, transcripts, and other accommodations.</li><li>Manage and track accessibility requests through a digital ticketing system, ensuring timely follow-up and completion.</li><li>Provide excellent customer service while supporting accessibility-related projects and initiatives.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities</strong></div><ul><li>Experience supporting digital accessibility initiatives in educational, professional, or other complex digital environments.</li><li>Working knowledge of digital accessibility standards and guidelines, including WCAG 2.1 Level AA guidelines.</li><li>Ability to explain accessibility concepts to individuals with varying levels of technical expertise.</li><li>Experience reviewing and remediating digital content for accessibility, including documents, presentations, PDFs, multimedia, and web-based content.</li><li>Proficiency with Adobe Acrobat Pro or similar PDF editing tools for accessibility tagging and remediation.</li><li>Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, PowerPoint, and Excel, with the ability to create and edit accessible documents.</li><li>Strong communication and customer service skills.</li><li>Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines.</li><li>Ability to work independently while also collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, and technical stakeholders.</li><li>Experience using accessibility evaluation tools, such as screen readers, automated testing tools, accessibility checkers, and captioning platforms.</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply</strong>:</div><div>DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of at least three references. <br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.</div> DSU-Information Technology Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49603 2026-08-31T15:27:19-05:00 2026-08-31T15:27:20-05:00 Family & Community Health Educator <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking multiple Family &amp; Community Health Educators. These positions improve the health and well-being of South Dakotans by delivering evidence-based health education programs, supporting behavior change, and connecting individuals with resources that promote healthy lifestyles and chronic disease self-management. This position is grant funded, continuation is dependent on performance and funding availability.<br><br></div><div>As the outreach arm of our state’s land grant, South Dakota State University, SDSU Extension is able to provide farmers, ranchers, agri-business people, communities, families and youth with the research-based information they need to succeed. SDSU Extension meets the changing needs of South Dakotans with progressive outreach services, ranging from one-on-one interaction and forums to 24/7 online access through our website (formerly iGrow.org).<br><br></div><div>These positions are located at one of the Extension Regional Centers in <a href=\"https://www.experiencesiouxfalls.com/\"><strong>Sioux Falls</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.visitrapidcity.com/\"><strong>Rapid City</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.aberdeen.sd.us/\"><strong>Aberdeen</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://www.cityofpierre.org/\"><strong>Pierre</strong></a>, and Wager.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Provides program delivery which includes delivering comprehensive, evidence-based public health and nutrition education to youth and adults through group instruction. Leads networking and partnership development efforts by establishing, maintaining, and strengthening relationships with community organizations, agencies, and stakeholders that support varied and limited-resource populations to enhance collaboration and community impact. Manages reporting and data tracking processes, ensuring accurate documentation, timely completion of reports, and adherence to established deadlines. Monitors and tracks participant progress and outcomes while demonstrating strong organizational, prioritization, and time management skills.</div><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:</strong></div><div><strong>Knowledge of:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Chronic disease prevention, health promotion, physical activity, and nutrition education</li><li>Food safety, preparation, household budgeting, and smart shopping techniques</li><li>Basic teaching methodologies for youth and adults</li><li>Basic statistical and arithmetic concepts, including calculating percentages</li><li>Assigned service area (community) and existing community services and resources</li><li>Basic computer skills with working knowledge of Microsoft applications and technology, including data entry and record maintenance</li></ul><div><strong><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:</strong></div><div><strong>Skills:</strong></div><ul><li>Managing inventories and budgets</li><li>Working or volunteering with limited-resource families and varied populations</li><li>Managing volunteers, adults, or students in classroom or educational settings, including teaching adults in group settings</li><li>Organizing work, managing time, and working independently</li><li>Maintaining accurate, complete, and compliant records</li></ul><div><strong><br>Ability to:</strong></div><ul><li>Conduct participant interviews, collect feedback, and organize data</li><li>Gather, interpret, and report basic health and nutrition findings</li><li>Interpret and apply program guidelines, procedures, and curricula</li><li>Oral, written, and listening communication skills with varied audiences</li><li>Work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a team</li><li>Network and build relationships with partners, agencies, and participants</li><li>Promote and market programming to rural and limited-resource audiences and organizations serving those populations</li><li>Lift up to 40 pounds and bend or stand for extended periods</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Required Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>High school diploma or GED</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>College coursework, associate’s degree, or bachelor’s degree preferred</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required License:</strong></div><ul><li>Valid Drivers License</li></ul><div><strong><br>Application Procedures:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div><div><br>[EE9510, SE8573, EE9222, EE8819, EE9255; 11041]</div> SDSU-Food & Families Programs-Ext https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48955 2026-07-10T16:27:50-05:00 2026-07-10T16:27:52-05:00 Student Services Coordinator <div>Black Hills State University is seeking applicants to fill a Student Services Coordinator.<br><br><strong>General Summary:</strong></div><div>Black Hills State University (BHSU) seeks a dynamic, student-focused professional to serve as the Student Services Coordinator at the BHSU–Rapid City campus.<br><br></div><div>Reporting to the Vice President for Continuing Education &amp; Workforce Development, this position serves as the primary front-facing representative of the university and plays a central role in recruitment, admissions, and enrollment services. The coordinator leads the student journey from initial inquiry through registration and transition to academic advising, ensuring a seamless and student-centered experience.<br><br></div><div>This role is responsible for developing and executing strategic recruitment and outreach initiatives to support a broad range of student populations, including first-time/full-time students, adult learners, transfer students, and military-affiliated students (active duty, guardsmen, and veterans).<br><br></div><div>The Student Services Coordinator also serves as the primary coordinator for BHSU–Rapid City events, leading the planning and execution of campus visits, preview days, recruitment events, and New Student Registration experiences.<br><br></div><div>This position requires a highly motivated, self-directed professional who exercises independent judgment, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and is passionate about helping students succeed.<br><br></div><div><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><div><strong>Recruitment &amp; Enrollment Growth</strong></div><ul><li>Lead strategic recruitment efforts to support enrollment growth across multiple student populations</li><li>Develop partnerships with regional high schools, community colleges, workforce partners, and community organizations</li><li>Coordinate and represent BHSU at recruitment events, community engagement activities, and outreach initiatives</li><li>Develop targeted communication strategies and engagement plans to attract prospective students</li><li>Analyze recruitment data and trends to inform strategy and improve outcomes</li></ul><div><strong><br>Admissions &amp; Enrollment Operations</strong></div><ul><li>Review and evaluate admissions applications and supporting documentation</li><li>Make informed admissions-related decisions in alignment with university policies</li><li>Coordinate application processing workflows and ensure timely progression from application to admission</li><li>Maintain accuracy and integrity of student data within institutional systems</li><li>Resolve enrollment barriers using sound judgment and problem-solving</li></ul><div><strong><br>Student Engagement &amp; Enrollment Navigation</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as the primary point of contact for prospective and incoming students (in-person, phone, and events)</li><li>Lead students through the enrollment process from inquiry through registration</li><li>Facilitate course registration when appropriate, including during peak periods and events</li><li>Direct students to appropriate campus resources, ensuring smooth transitions to advising and other services</li><li>Monitor student progression and intervene proactively to support completion of enrollment steps</li></ul><div><strong><br>Financial Aid &amp; Academic Pathway Support</strong></div><ul><li>Provide front-line guidance on financial aid processes, including FAFSA completion</li><li>Deliver general academic pathway information aligned with university programs</li><li>Coordinate referrals to financial aid and advising specialists as needed</li><li>Maintain working knowledge of financial aid processes, timelines, and requirements</li></ul><div><strong><br>Student Services Coordination</strong></div><ul><li>Lead coordination of student services across admissions, advising, and financial aid within the Rapid City location</li><li>Facilitate regular team meetings and support cross-functional collaboration</li><li>Coordinate service coverage, workflow alignment, and cross-training efforts</li><li>Identify service gaps and implement improvements to enhance the student experience</li><li>Strong ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment</li><li>Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills</li><li>Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment</li><li>Strong customer service orientation and commitment to student success</li><li>Ability to learn and apply complex policies and processes</li></ul><div><strong><br>Events Coordination &amp; Campus Experience</strong></div><ul><li>Lead planning, coordination, and execution of BHSU–Rapid City events, including:<ul><li>Preview Days</li><li>Campus visits and student tours</li><li>Local recruitment events</li><li>New Student Registration experiences</li></ul></li><li>Coordinate event logistics, communication, staffing, and materials</li><li>Develop engaging, student-centered experiences that support recruitment and enrollment goals</li><li>Evaluate event effectiveness and implement continuous improvements</li></ul><div><strong><br>Communications &amp; Social Media Engagement</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinate and contribute to social media strategy for the Rapid City campus, including platforms such as Facebook and ZeeMee</li><li>Develop and maintain engaging digital content aligned with institutional branding</li><li>Support outreach campaigns through effective communication strategies and messaging</li></ul><div><strong><br>Requirements</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree required</li><li>One to three years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, student services, advising, enrollment management, or a related field</li><li>Valid driver’s license required</li><li>Ability to travel and work occasional evenings and weekends</li></ul><div><strong><br>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Experience working with diverse student populations, including traditional-aged, adult, transfer, and military-affiliated students</li><li>Experience in higher education recruitment, admissions, or student services</li><li>Familiarity with student information systems such as Banner, DegreeWorks, or similar platforms</li><li>Experience coordinating events or programs</li><li>Demonstrated ability to build strong partnerships with community organizations and stakeholders</li></ul><div><br><strong>COMMENTS</strong><br>Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>TO APPLY</strong></div><div>Applications must be made at <a href=\"http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please attach a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information of at least three professional references.<br><br></div><div>This position is open until filled with a first review date of July 23, 2026 at 11:00 PM MDT.<br><br></div><div>For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may be directed to Ashley Armstrong at <a href=\"mailto:ashley.armstrong@bhsu.edu\"><strong>ashley.armstrong@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Rapid City Campus https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49535 2026-08-26T10:16:00-05:00 2026-08-26T10:16:01-05:00 Help Desk Analyst <div><strong>Black Hills State University seeks applicants for a Help Desk Analyst in our Network and Computer Services department. This position serves as a key customer-facing member of the Information Technology team and requires exceptional customer service, communication, and problem-solving skills.<br><br>RESPONSIBILITIES:<br>- Manage university Help Desk operations and ensure faculty, staff, students, and other customers receive timely, professional, and courteous technical support;<br>- Interview, select, train, schedule, supervise, and evaluate Help Desk student employees;<br>- Develop, maintain, and revise Help Desk protocols, procedures, technical documentation, knowledge-based articles, and service standards;<br>- Administer and support assigned systems, including TeamDynamix and the Druva endpoint backup system;<br>- Coordinate TeamDynamix administration, standards, and processes with other South Dakota Board of Regents administrators;<br>- Configure and deploy computers for faculty and staff and support state-owned computers, applications, printers, scanners, and peripheral devices;<br>- Apply and maintain operating system patches, hotfixes, updates, and upgrades;<br>- Create, test, maintain, and deploy standardized computer images;<br>- Diagnose and resolve hardware, software, account-access, connectivity, and network-related problems;<br>- Manage file permissions and security for network shares;<br>- Plan, test, document, and implement system upgrades and related procedures;<br>- Accurately document, categorize, prioritize, track, and escalate service requests;<br>- Provide end-user support by telephone, email, live chat, remote-support tools, and in person; and - Maintain positive, professional relationships and communicate clearly with university customers and technology staff.<br><br>KNOWLEDGE OF:<br>- Microsoft Windows operating systems;<br>- Microsoft 365 applications;<br>- macOS operating systems and applications;<br>- Networking concepts, protocols, connectivity, and troubleshooting;<br>- Computer design, installation, configuration, compatibility, and operating system principles;<br>- Information security concepts, practices, and principles;<br>- A diverse range of computer hardware, software, and peripheral devices.<br><br>ABILITY TO:<br>- Explain technology and information security issues clearly to nontechnical individuals;<br>- Communicate clearly, concisely, and professionally with students, parents, faculty, staff, administrators, and other stakeholders;<br>- Provide courteous and effective customer service to individuals with varying levels of technical knowledge;<br>- Supervise, train, mentor, and support Help Desk student technicians;<br>- Assist with planning and implementing campus-wide technology projects;<br>- Diagnose and resolve technical problems independently;<br>- Collaborate effectively with BHSU technology and support staff;<br>- Develop and implement system-wide technology solutions;<br>- Anticipate potential issues and take appropriate preventive action;<br>- Collect, evaluate, and analyze technical information from multiple sources and system components;<br>- Maintain current technical knowledge of hardware, software, security, and industry developments;<br>- Research, evaluate, and implement innovative technologies;<br>- Lift and move computer equipment weighing up to 50 pounds.<br><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:<br>- A bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience is preferred.<br><br>CERTIFICATIONS:<br>- The Lenovo Certified Warranty Technician exam will need to be completed in the first three months of employment.<br><br>REQUIRED LICENSE:<br>- A valid driver’s license is required.<br><br>COMMENTS:<br>This is a full-time, 12-month, overtime-eligible position. Normal working hours are 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., Monday through Friday. Travel is required. The position is performed primarily in office and classroom environments and includes supervising and directing Help Desk student technicians.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br>TO APPLY:<br>Applications for this position must be made online at http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Complete the online application and attach a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of September 7, 2026 @ 11PM Mountain Time. For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Inquiries directly related to the position should be sent to Fred Nelson at fred.nelson@bhsu.edu.<br><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or </strong><a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a><strong>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</strong></div> BHSU-Network & Computer Support Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49286 2026-08-05T09:33:58-05:00 2026-08-05T09:33:59-05:00 Advisor - Student Success <div>If you have a passion for helping students succeed, South Dakota State University has an opportunity for you. The Office of International Student and Scholar Engagement is looking for an Advisor for Student Succes dedicated to serving students with an emphasis on the international student population. The ideal candidate will guide students through ongoing maintenance of legal status, assist in safeguarding institutional and student compliance with university, state, and federal mandates as well as initiate and implement educational programs to proactively assist with the engagement and retention of international students. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position and is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, SD</strong></a>.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/international-student-scholar-engagement\"><strong>International Student and Scholar Engagement</strong></a> is a comprehensive home for international student and scholar services. All services and activities are intended to help enrich the experience of international students here at SDSU and to expand global engagement for all students, faculty and staff. The office is part of the <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/student-engagement-center\"><strong>Student Engagement Center</strong></a>, which supports student success by fostering connection and community, removing barriers, and promoting academic, personal, and professional growth. The center brings together departments with shared goals to strengthen collaboration and elevate service to students, including Veterans Services and Engagement, the American Indian Student Center, International Student and Scholar Engagement, the Office of Student Accessibility, and Student Connection and Engagement.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>This position provides services to potential and current international students and their family members including preliminary immigration advice through education on the federal government naturalization and immigration regulations, keeping students in compliance with university, state, &amp; federal guidelines as well as initiating and implementing educational and social programs including advising student organizations.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>In addition, this position requires the ability to assume Alternative Responsible Officer (ARO) status for SDSU’s U.S. Department of State approved J-1 Exchange Visitor Program and Designated School Official (DSO) status for the F-1 student program. Pursuant to 22 CFR (Code of Federal Regulations) Part A §62.2, ARO Status requires U.S. citizenship or U.S. permanent residence status. DSO Status also requires U.S. citizenship or U.S. permanent residence status, per Department of Homeland Security regulations.</div><div><strong><br>&nbsp;BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s Degree with a minimum of one (1) year of professional experience with international education by start date.</li><li>Organizational and time management skills.</li><li>Ability or potential to plan, develop, implement, and evaluate educational materials and direct effective programs.</li><li>Effective written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate with faculty, staff and students.</li><li>Effective interpersonal skills with the ability to work as a contributing team member.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Knowledge and experience with university policies pertaining to international students and federal laws affecting international students coming to the U.S.</li><li>Knowledge of college student activity programs, program assessment, and retention initiatives.</li><li>An understanding of current trends in higher education impacting student success.</li><li>Knowledge of the development of peer mentoring.</li><li>Ability to apply student development theory as well as interpret and implement policy.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp; Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. &nbsp; It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div> SDSU-International Student & Schol Engment https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49655 2026-09-03T17:02:53-05:00 2026-09-03T17:02:54-05:00 Accountant <div>USD is seeking an energetic, creative problem solver, and strategic thinker to fill an open Accountant position. The individual hired must be able to interpret, analyze, and determine accuracy of financial data in the maintenance of controlling funds. Individual must be able to provide exceptional customer service and interpret USD and State of SD policies and procedures.</div><div>Specific tasks will include:</div><ul><li>Audit direct pays and journal vouchers.</li><li>Process and track state contracts</li><li>Plan and Provide traning on Banner accounting processes campus wide</li><li>Manage data interface transactions into Banner and review for accuracy</li><li>Manage 1099 process</li><li>Reconcile accounts and disburse payment</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Candidates must demonstrate:</div><div>- Extensive knowledge of accounting principles and practices</div><div>- Ability to interpreting complex policies and regulations</div><div>- Ability to work effectively with a variety of units to create effective relationships for problem solving and positive interactions</div><div>- Ability to use computers and software for detailed accounting and budgeting transactions</div><div>- Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and electronically.</div><div>- Ability to work with staff whose understanding of financial operations will be at various levels<br><br><em>This position is not eligible for sponsorship, all eligible candidates must be authorized to work in the United States.&nbsp;</em></div> USD-Accounting Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49609 2026-08-31T16:04:02-05:00 2026-08-31T16:04:03-05:00 StoreKeeper <div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) is searching for a Storekeeper who will be responsible for processing all incoming and outgoing U.S. and campus mail, as well as delivering mail, packages, and warehouse materials across campus. Manages all shipping and receiving activities for items entering and leaving the central warehouse. Supports mail-related accounts payable functions and assists with the operations of multiple in‑house shop inventories. Provides courteous and efficient customer service to faculty, staff, students, and campus visitors. <br><br>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, SD</strong></a></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><strong><br>Job Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Ensure all Facilities &amp; Services mailing and shipping operations are completed accurately, efficiently, and on schedule.</li><li>Maintain full compliance with federal USPS regulations, including permit management and proper handling of all outgoing mailings.</li><li>Oversee and manage the flow of USPS and campus mail to ensure daily deadlines are consistently met.</li><li>Protect SDSU’s mailing permits and reduced‑postage eligibility by adhering to all postal requirements and preventing violations that could result in fines or loss of the 57007 ZIP code.</li><li>Process and handle suspicious mail, confidential HR documents, and sensitive Residential Life materials with discretion and security.</li><li>Assist students, parents, and campus departments in locating and resolving issues with missing or delayed packages.</li><li>Support mail‑related accounts payable functions and billing processes</li></ul><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Knowledge of: &nbsp;</div><ul><li>Customer service techniques</li><li>General Mail Room Knowledge</li><li>General Shipping/Receiving Knowledge</li><li>General warehouse/supply room and inventory procedures</li><li>Basic computer skills</li></ul><div><strong><br></strong>Skill &amp; Ability to: </div><ul><li>Communicate concisely and effectively, both orally and in writing</li><li>Work within time constraints and with unpredictable workload</li><li>Work in all weather conditions</li><li>Lift and carry up to 50 pounds</li><li>Prioritize work assignments</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required License:&nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Valid Driver’s License</li></ul><div><br><strong>Application Procedures:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Customer Service Ctr https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48346 2026-05-29T14:14:37-05:00 2026-05-29T14:14:38-05:00 Research Assistant Professor - Chemistry <div>The Chemistry Department of the University of South Dakota (USD) invites applicants to apply for a long-term Research Faculty position in chemistry related to modern refrigeration including but not limited to broadly defined fluorine chemistry. The initial appointment for this position will be at the Assistant Professor level. This hiring is in response to the R&amp;D needs of newly established NSF Engineer Research Center: Environmentally Applied Refrigerant Technology Hub (NSF ERC EARTH), a large collaborative effort involving six academic institutions and fifteen industrial partners. A successful candidate is expected to bring in knowledge and skills that are align with the NSF ERC EARTH goals, and complementary to the expertise of current department faculty. The new research faculty is expected to provide guidance to graduate and undergraduate students, either through individual or collaborative effort with the department EARTH faculty. In addition to publication record, demonstrated ability to securing external funding is further thought to be an area of strength for a successful candidate. The position requires a PhD degree in chemistry, or closely related field, with preference given to candidate with postdoctoral experience or equivalent industrial working experience. Further questions regarding to the ERC EARTH program at USD campus, please reach out to the ERC EARTH’s USD lead person Dr. Haoran Sun at <a href=\"mailto:Haoran.Sun@usd.edu\"><strong>Haoran.Sun@usd.edu</strong></a>; and questions regarding to the Chemistry Program, please reach out to the Department Chair Dr. James Hoefelmeyer at <a href=\"mailto:James.Hoefelmeyer@usd.edu\"><strong>James.Hoefelmeyer@usd.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Interested applicants shall provide the following documents to the search committee through the SD BOR online job application portal: (1) cover letter, (2) CV, (3) detailed research plans (no more than 10 pages total including reference citation, with 1 inch margin around, single space, and font 11); (4) student mentoring plans (two page maximum, with 1 inch margin around, single space, and font 11); and (5) a list of contact information of three professional references.<br><br></div><div>As the South Dakota’s flagship institution and one of the five core-partner institutions of the recently funded NSF ERC EARTH, the University of South Dakota provides vibrant study and working environment for its students and faculty. The Chemistry Department at USD offers BS and MS degrees in Chemistry and PhD degree in Materials Chemistry. Over the past twenty years, the Chemistry Program at USD receives very strong external funding support from federal, state, and industries including highly competitive NSF CAREER and NRT grants, and lately large collaborative NSF ERC grants.<br><br></div><div>For more information about the Chemistry Department of the University of South Dakota, please go to the website at <a href=\"http://www.usd.edu/Academics/Colleges-and-Schools/college-of-arts-sciences/chemistry\"><strong>www.usd.edu/Academics/Colleges-and-Schools/college-of-arts-sciences/chemistry</strong></a>; and about the ERC EARTH please go to the website at <a href=\"https://erc-earth.ku.edu\"><strong>https://erc-earth.ku.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div> USD-Chemistry https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49442 2026-08-19T08:57:50-05:00 2026-08-19T08:57:51-05:00 Senior Associate Athletic Director of Internal Operations <div><strong>Position Information:</strong></div><div>South Dakota Mines is seeking a confident, energetic, and highly organized servant leader to serve as Senior Associate Athletic Director of Internal Operations. This is a full-time, benefited position. Located in Rapid City, South Dakota Mines is an NCAA Division II institution and member of the Rocky Mountain Athletic Conference (RMAC). Hardrocker Athletics sponsors 13 NCAA Division II sports.<br><br></div><div>The Senior Associate Athletic Director serves on the Athletics leadership team and advises the Director of Athletics on departmental operations and strategic priorities. The successful candidate will value collaboration, accountability, gender equity, and academic success, health, and overall well-being of student-athletes.<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Provide leadership, direction, and supervision for the internal operations of Hardrocker Athletics, which may include business operations, student-athlete academic services, compliance, event management, facilities, and ticketing.</li><li>Following the selection and appointment of the successful candidate, additional administrative responsibilities may be assigned based on departmental needs and the qualifications of the successful candidate, consistent with applicable NCAA and institutional requirements. Such responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, serving as the institution’s Senior Woman Administrator (SWA) and/or a Title IX liaison for Athletics. In these roles, the successful candidate would promote gender equity, support compliance with applicable laws and policies, foster a positive work environment, and support the success and well-being of student-athletes and staff.</li><li>Coordinate all home athletic events, including scheduling, staffing, facility readiness, ticket and ramp operations, visiting-team communication, athletic training coverage, and collaboration with campus departments and participating organizations.</li><li>Assist with managing departmental operating budgets and discretionary accounts while ensuring fiscal responsibility and compliance with university policies.</li><li>Supervise assigned sports and support head coaches in budgeting, scheduling, personnel matters, compliance, facilities, student-athlete welfare, recruiting, and postseason planning.</li><li>Oversee the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee, including meetings, leadership development, NCAA legislative engagement, and community service activities.</li><li>Serve as the primary liaison to the RMAC office and represent South Dakota Mines at RMAC, NCAA, and professional meetings and conventions.</li><li>Collaborate with campus leaders to develop and implement policies and procedures that strengthen departmental effectiveness.</li><li>Participate in Athletics leadership meetings, contribute to the department’s strategic plan, serve on assigned committees, and perform other duties assigned by the Director of Athletics.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree preferred.</li><li>Minimum of three to five years of collegiate athletics administration, coaching, business operations, academic services, compliance, event management, or related experience.</li><li>Working knowledge of NCAA rules, Title IX requirements, and intercollegiate athletics administration.</li><li>Previous collegiate student-athlete experience is welcomed but not required.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Required Skills:</strong></div><ul><li>High personal integrity, sound professional judgment, and commitment to accountability.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to lead, collaborate, delegate, and build trusted relationships.</li><li>Strong organizational, problem-solving, decision-making, and time-management skills.</li><li>Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment and work evenings, weekends, holidays, and athletic events as required.</li><li>Strong written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><br><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 17, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional references (include name, mailing and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Intercollegiate Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49122 2026-07-23T12:18:57-05:00 2026-07-23T12:18:59-05:00 Leadership Giving Officer <div>Dakota State University seeks a passionate relationship builder to serve as its next Leadership Giving Officer. This role is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parents, and friends of the university capable of making gifts of $5,000 or more, helping to create philanthropic partnerships that fuel the university's vision and strengthen its future. <br><br><strong>Requirements</strong>:</div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree is required in Marketing, Education, Accounting, Finance, or other related field.</li><li>1-3 years or experience in fundraising, particularly in major gifts or leadership giving.<ul><li>Experience in a higher education setting is preferred.</li></ul></li><li>Strong ability to build relationships, listen to donor needs, and cultivate donor loyalty.</li><li>Ability to analyze donor data and fundraising trends to develop strategies.</li><li>Comfortable with public speaking and presenting to groups of various sizes. .</li><li>Strong combination of creative, analytical and organizational skills; attention to detail.</li><li>Proficiency with database management systems.</li><li>Commitment to maintaining confidentiality of philanthropic partners</li><li>Excellent computer skills, including Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel and Word.</li><li>Effective written, oral, and interpersonal skills.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Identify and qualify potential donors through research, interviews, and other engagement methods.</li><li>Develop and implement personalized strategies to cultivate relationships with prospects.</li><li>Solicit gifts that align with the strategic needs of the University.</li><li>Maintain and strengthen relationships with existing donors through consistent communication and recognition efforts.</li><li>Ensure accurate and up-to-date records of all interactions, proposals, and contributions in Raiser’s Edge.</li><li>Work closely with University leadership to understand funding priorities and translate these needs into compelling donor opportunities.</li><li>Partner with colleagues across the University to identify potential prospects and create comprehensive donor engagement plans.</li><li>Plan and attend events to engage with potential and existing donors, representing the University’s mission and goals.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability coverage</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply:</strong>To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. The employment site will allow the attachment of a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and contact information for at least three professional references. <br><br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.</div> DSU-Institutional Advancement https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48998 2026-07-15T09:01:56-05:00 2026-07-15T09:01:57-05:00 Assistant Professor of Business Analytics and Information Systems <div>Northern State University’s School of Business is accepting applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business Analytics. The successful candidate will support the School’s newly established Analytics major and contribute to the School’s existing Information Systems major.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>*Qualifications:</strong><br> Candidates holding a Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Business Analytics, Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Decision Sciences, Data Science, Computer Science, or a closely related field will be considered for a tenure-track appointment. Candidates from related quantitative business or technology fields may also be considered if their teaching and research background demonstrates expertise in analytics, information systems, business intelligence, data management, or applied technology. Applicants with a master’s degree in one of these areas will be considered for non-tenure-track positions.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>*Responsibilities:</strong><br> The successful candidate will be able to teach undergraduate information systems and analytics-related courses in both face-to-face and online settings. Potential teaching areas include management information systems, database management systems, business intelligence, systems analysis and design, data mining, and artificial intelligence in business. These courses support both the School’s newly established Analytics major and the existing Information Systems major. Depending on expertise, interest, and program needs, the successful candidate may have opportunities to develop additional analytics-related coursework, such as data visualization or other courses that support the continued growth of Northern’s School of Business. Additional responsibilities include academic advising and mentoring, scholarly activity, and service to the university, profession, and community.</div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div> NSU-Management Information Systems https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49551 2026-08-27T09:25:59-05:00 2026-08-27T09:25:59-05:00 Director of Northern State Early College <div>Northern State University seeks a collaborative and strategic leader to serve as Director of Northern State Early College.<br><br></div><div>This role provides leadership for a unified early college model that expands access to postsecondary education and strengthens student transition from high school to college. The Director will lead the integration of dual credit programs into a single, coordinated system and build a consistent, high-quality experience for students, families, and school partners.</div><div><br>The Director works closely with faculty, academic units, student support services, and school districts across South Dakota. This position focuses on creating clear pathways, strengthening advising and student support, and increasing college-going and persistence for students participating in early college programs.</div><div><br><strong>What You Will Do</strong></div><ul><li>Lead strategy and execution for all Early College and dual credit initiatives</li><li>Build a unified program that brings together multiple pathways and delivery models</li><li>Design consistent onboarding, advising, and transition experiences for students</li><li>Strengthen partnerships with high schools, counselors, families, and communities</li><li>Oversee advising systems, student success programming, and transition support</li><li>Align academic pathways and ensure quality across online, on-campus, and high school delivery</li><li>Supervise staff, manage operations, and oversee program resources</li><li>Use data to guide decisions, improve outcomes, and inform stakeholders</li></ul><div><br><strong>What You Bring</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in higher education, education, leadership, or a related field</li><li>Experience in higher education, K-12 partnerships, or student success initiatives</li><li>Ability to collaborate across campus and with external partners</li><li>Experience designing advising, student success, or access-focused programs</li><li>Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills</li><li>Commitment to expanding access and supporting students who face barriers to higher education</li></ul><div><br><strong>Additional Information</strong> This position reports to the Provost and requires regular travel to partner schools across South Dakota.</div><div><br>Northern State University is committed to expanding access to higher education and creating strong pathways and opportunities for all students. The Director of Northern State Early College plays a central role in building a coordinated, statewide model that supports students from their first college course through degree completion.</div> NSU-Provost https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49302 2026-08-06T12:26:28-05:00 2026-08-06T12:26:29-05:00 Dean, Beacom School of Business <div>The University of South Dakota (USD) invites applications for the next <strong>Dean of the Beacom School of Business</strong>, a pivotal academic leader who will shape the future of business education across South Dakota and the region.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will be an <strong>entrepreneurial, innovative visionary</strong> who values all Beacom programs, students, faculty, and staff — and who celebrates their successes. The new dean will <em>“aggressively seek partnerships in the rapidly growing Sioux Falls market and be a visible advocate for the business school’s service to the entire state.”</em></div><div><br>This is a moment of transformation for USD and Beacom: expanding into Sioux Falls, strengthening experiential learning, elevating AACSB excellence, and building the next generation of business leaders.<br><br>For more information, or to provide a nomination please contact BeacomDeanSearch@usd.edu</div> USD-School of Business https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49658 2026-09-04T08:36:02-05:00 2026-09-04T08:36:02-05:00 Financial Program Assistant <div>South Dakota State University's Facilities &amp; Services Department is seeking a Financial Program Assistant to support essential financial and operational services across campus. This multifaceted role combines accounts payable, purchasing, mail services, and warehouse support, making it an excellent opportunity for an organized and detail-oriented professional looking to make a campus-wide impact. <br><br>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota.&nbsp;<br><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:</em></strong> This position performs all departmental routine accounts payable duties such as processing purchase order invoices, direct pays, standing contract and spot purchase invoices for payment. This process involves working with shop supervisors and project managers via work order management system for invoice reviews, approvals and payments; ensuring invoices are paid on correct funds and issued to correct work orders for tracking and billing. Handling any questionable invoices and contacting vendors about invoice details. This position will also handle returns, Banner/accounts payables reconciliation, and assist the Program Assistant II with purchasing for F&amp;S according to state guidelines. Additional duties are to provide back-up support when needed for the Mail Center and Warehouse by assisting with shipping, receiving, processing outgoing/incoming US &amp; campus mail, and packages.&nbsp;<br><br><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;<br><br><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em> &nbsp;</div><ul><li>Purchasing practices, procedures, and applicable regulations.&nbsp;</li><li>Accounting principles, accounts payable processes, and inventory management practices.</li></ul><div><em>&nbsp;</em></div><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Manage multiple priorities, adapt to changing demands, and provide responsive service in a fast-paced environment</li><li>Collaborate effectively and contribute positively within a team-orientated work environment</li><li>Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel</li><li>Learn quickly and utilize new software applications</li><li>Excellent customer service skills</li><li>Communicate effectively, both written and oral.</li><li>Strong attention to detail and organization skills&nbsp;</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Required License:<br>&nbsp;</em></strong>Valid driver’s license<br><br><strong>Application Procedures:<br></strong>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted.<br><br>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Customer Service Ctr https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49135 2026-07-24T10:45:47-05:00 2026-07-24T10:45:48-05:00 Associate Vice President for Research Affairs <div><strong>Position Information:</strong></div><div>South Dakota Mines invites applications for the Associate Vice President for Research Affairs within the Research Affairs office. This is a regular, full-time, benefited position. This position is responsible for managing technology transfer, intellectual property, and supporting, as needed, faculty and student innovation and entrepreneurship programming. The position oversees several areas of compliance including human subjects research, Bayh-Dole requirements and reporting, and export control assurances. This position also reviews and negotiates contracts on behalf of the research enterprise and upper administration. The position will also be the principal investigator for the university’s NSF I-Corps grant.<br><br></div><div>A PhD in a STEM field, a J.D. with focus on intellectual property or contracts, or an MBA is required. 5 years of experience in higher education technology transfer is required.<br><br></div><div><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin July 24, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional references (include name, mailing and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Research Affairs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49613 2026-09-01T09:17:27-05:00 2026-09-01T09:17:27-05:00 Custodial Services Supervisor I <div>The Custodial Services department within USD Facilities Management is seeking a Custodial Supervisor I. This position is responsible for supervising and coordinating the activities of approximately 30 custodial personnel to maintain and provide quality custodial services for our campus facilities in Vermillion, SD. This person will be responsible for the presentation and cleanliness of our academic buildings. This person will interact closely with staff, customers, students, and faculty on campus. As part of a team, this person is responsible for the well planned, timely and safe delivery of custodial services.</div><div><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>One to Three years of supervisory experience that includes direct supervision of staff</li><li>Knowledge of the practices, procedures, equipment, chemicals, and materials common to the custodial profession</li><li>Excellent verbal and written communication skills</li><li>Knowledge of Microsoft Office software including Excel, Word and Outlook</li><li>Ability to supervise, train, and evaluate the work of your staff in a fair and planned matter</li><li>Ability to deal with personnel matters and dealing with conflict</li></ul> USD-Custodial Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48369 2026-06-01T14:15:59-05:00 2026-06-01T14:16:00-05:00 Data Services Librarian <div>The University Libraries of the University of South Dakota seeks a motivated individual to serve as a core team member of the Digital Scholarship and Research Services initiative.<br><br>The successful candidate will proactively collaborate with students, faculty, and staff to support their information and data needs, helping them transform information into scholarship.<br><br>As a member of the University Libraries faculty, the Data Services Librarian:<br><br></div><ul><li>Joins the University Libraries’ Digital Scholarship and Research Services initiative to develop and offer workshops on data analysis, data visualization, data management, and more.</li><li>Serves on the University Libraries’ Instruction team to teach information literacy sessions that support the University’s General Education curriculum.</li><li>Excels as a liaison to divisions, centers, and programs within the Beacom School of Business and other assigned academic programs.</li></ul><div><br>Specific responsibilities include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Advancing the University Libraries’ Digital Scholarship and Research Services initiative by developing and delivering workshops on data science tools and skills, helping to manage and promote the Virtual Reality Lab, and staying up-to-date on emerging trends and changes in technologies related to data science (i.e., AI).</li><li>Providing statistical and other data-related support for the USD Sanford School of Medicine graduate and residency programs, including holding regular office hours for consultations.</li><li>Promoting the NIH’s <em>All of Us </em>biomedical database by keeping up-to-date on developments, maintaining Controlled Access by completing the annual trainings, and teaching various groups and departments about storing and analyzing data with the Researcher Workbench.</li><li>Serving as a liaison to the Beacom School students and faculty by promoting and supporting the discovery, use, and management of data; conducting reference and research assistance consultations; providing course-integrated instruction; and creating and maintaining research guides, online tutorials, and other teaching and learning tools.</li><li>Assisting students and faculty in transforming information into research-ready formats.</li><li>Promoting services that advance and support Open Access (OA) publishing and Open Data initiatives.</li><li>Faculty of the University Libraries carry service assignments and may be assigned research and scholarship loads.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Minimum Qualifications:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA-accredited program <strong>or</strong> a master’s degree in a related field such as data science, statistics, computer science, or a relevant discipline;</li><li>A minimum of two years of professional experience in an academic or research library or in a data-focused role;</li><li>Demonstrated experience with statistical analysis and data science tools and software (e.g., R, Python, SPSS, Stata, or similar);</li><li>Evidence of effective teaching or instructional experience, including workshops, classroom instruction, or one-on-one consultations;</li><li>Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively with diverse groups and departments;</li><li>Strong written and verbal communication skills.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Desirable Qualifications:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Experience providing research data services in an academic library or similar environment;</li><li>Experience with scholarly publishing at institutions of higher education;</li><li>Familiarity with research data management practices, including data management plans and funder requirements;</li><li>Knowledge of data curation, preservation, and sharing, including FAIR data principles;</li><li>Experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI) or GIS platforms;</li><li>Demonstrated experience supporting faculty and students in data-intensive research;</li><li>Experience developing and delivering data literacy or data science instruction;</li><li>Familiarity with open science practices, including open data, OA, and OER;</li><li>Experience assessing user needs and developing data-related services or programs.</li></ul><div><br>Position reports to the Associate Dean for Teaching, Learning, and Research Services.<br><br>Application Procedure: Apply on-line at <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/</strong></a> by submitting a curriculum vita, a letter addressing required qualifications, and complete contact information for at least 3 professional references.</div> USD-Libraries https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49457 2026-08-19T15:51:52-05:00 2026-08-19T15:51:52-05:00 Selma Kendrick Assistant, Associate, or Full Professorship in Nursing <div>The endowment holder for the Selma Kendrick Endowed Professorship in Nursing in the SDState College of Nursing will partner with the college’s Native American Nursing Education Center with the goal of growing research and scholarly activities to impact the health of Native American Communities in South Dakota. The College of Nursing prides itself in commitment to excellence in education, research, and clinical practice. The College of Nursing is especially interested in candidates who have significant potential to build extramural funding to support the goals of improving health in Native American communities. This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.visitrapidcity.com/\"><strong>Rapid City</strong></a>, South Dakota. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The SDSU College of Nursing, located in Brookings, Rapid City, and Sioux Falls, has a long history of exceptional nursing education and this is recognized through its designation as a Center of Excellence in Nursing Education by the National League for Nursing. The college’s fully accredited Healthcare Simulation Center encompassing all three sites is further evidence of our commitment to high quality education for all students. SDSU Nursing’s history of excellence, innovation and achievement across its graduate and undergraduate programs provides an excellent foundation for growth and innovation.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Embedded in the SDSU College of Nursing’s Native American Nursing Education Center (NANEC), this endowed professorship will fulfill a collaborative role with the advising and mentoring team in NANEC to:</li><li>Build supportive relationships with Native American Students across the college.</li><li>Develop collaborative relationships with tribal communities across South Dakota.</li><li>Develop teams responsible for innovative health research that impacts the health and well-being of indigenous populations across South Dakota.&nbsp;</li><li>Grow a body of health research that informs health policy, population well-being, and healthy communities.</li><li>Develop consistent extramural funding to support the research endeavors to support NANEC and the innovative research focus for Native American populations.</li><li>Support teaching teams and NANEC in development of pedagogically sound educational offerings.</li></ul><div><strong><br>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><strong><br>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing, completed by application date;</li><li>Graduate Degree in Nursing, completed by application date;</li><li>A Ph.D. in nursing or related field, completed by start date;</li><li>Teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate levels;&nbsp;</li><li>A history of successfully funded research and relevant clinical practice;&nbsp;</li><li>Licensed by the South Dakota Board of Nursing or eligible for licensure as a registered nurse as evidenced by current licensure in another state;</li><li>Hold a national and/or international reputation for scholarship in Indigenous and rural health, community engaged research, and interdisciplinary approaches that inform<strong> </strong>health policy, strengthen educational practices, and improve population health outcomes, and/or aligned areas of value that will advance the strengths of the college.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience developing collaborative partnerships across academic, government, industry, and nonprofit sectors;&nbsp;</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills;</li><li>Valid driver’s license, or ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire, and willingness to travel.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Active program of research and dissemination, preferably related to Native American health and well-being;</li><li>Experience with simulation technology and distance delivery;</li><li>Demonstrated potential or ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams;</li><li>Evidence of service to the nursing profession.</li></ul><div><strong><br>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp; Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. &nbsp; It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div> SDSU-Graduate Nursing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49667 2026-09-04T13:52:41-05:00 2026-09-04T13:52:42-05:00 Facility Worker <div>Dakota State University is seeking applications for a full-time facility worker. Primary responsibilities include custodial care and minor maintenance at the Community Center.<br><br>The position will be scheduled Monday through Friday from 10pm to 6:30am. <br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Floor care will be daily vacuuming, scrubbing and mopping, occasional carpet shampooing and floor waxing.</li><li>Clean and sanitize restrooms and locker rooms.</li><li>Clean and sanitize restrooms and locker rooms.</li><li>Collect and remove trash from building.</li><li>Dust and wash walls, woodwork, and windows (inside and out).</li><li>Remove snow from steps and sidewalks near buildings.</li><li>Moving furniture.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Successful candidate must be able to:</strong></div><ul><li>Follow written and oral instructions.</li><li>Stand for extended periods of time.</li><li>Work with students, staff, and the public courteously.</li><li>Work independently.</li><li>Lift 50 pounds.</li><li>Bend, stretch, climb ladders, twist and walk.</li><li>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. (Sponsorship is not available for this position.)</li></ul><div><br><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability coverage</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply</strong>:</div><div>DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. <br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br> Applications will begin to be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div> DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49010 2026-07-16T09:24:52-05:00 2026-07-16T09:24:53-05:00 Adjunct University Supervisor for Field Experiences <div><strong>Responsibilities</strong>: Northern State University invites applications for an Adjunct University Supervisor to support clinical field experiences within the teacher preparation programs. The successful candidate will be responsible for supervising undergraduate teacher candidates, collaborating with cooperating teachers and candidates at multiple points throughout the field experience, and completing all required documentation, evaluations, and assessments related to candidate performance and professional dispositions. Some travel may be required. <br><br><strong>Qualifications:</strong> Applicants with a master’s degree in education are preferred. Individuals holding a bachelor’s degree in education will also be considered with a letter of recommendation. A minimum of three years of teaching experience is required. The ideal candidate will demonstrate versatility and flexibility in supervising multiple teacher candidates across various field experiences throughout the semester.</div> NSU-Education General https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49556 2026-08-27T14:09:40-05:00 2026-08-27T14:09:41-05:00 Part-Time Facility Worker <div>Dakota State University is seeking applications for a part-time, non-benefit eligible Facility Worker to work Monday – Friday. Preferred hours are 8pm - 12am.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Floor care: sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, but could also include waxing, and shampooing carpets.</li><li>Clean and sanitize designated areas.</li><li>Collect and remove trash from building.</li><li>Wash walls, woodwork, and windows.</li><li>Remove snow from steps and sidewalks near buildings.</li></ul><div><strong>Successful candidate must be able to:</strong></div><ul><li>Follow written and oral instructions.</li><li>Operate required cleaning equipment.</li><li>Work positively and professionally with students, co-workers, and the public.</li><li>Work independently.</li><li>Work on a 3 to 6 ft ladder</li><li>Lift 50 pounds.</li></ul><div><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong>How to Apply</strong>:</div><div>DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>.<br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br> Applications will begin to be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div> DSU-Physical Plant - Facilities Mgmt https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/27615 2022-03-15T11:10:56-05:00 2022-03-15T11:10:56-05:00 Adjunct Instructor or Lecturer <div>The Division of Teacher Residency &amp; Education invites applications for Adjunct Instructors with expertise in the following areas: Elementary Education, Physical Education, Secondary Education, and Special Education for its pool of part-time adjunct instructors. Applications for part-time faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed by the Division Chair when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a term-by-term basis, which may include fall, spring and/or summer.<br><br></div><div>Successful applicants will be expected to teach primarily on-campus undergraduate courses in teacher education at the Vermillion campus. Occasionally, courses may be offered on the USD Sioux Falls campus or online. Applicants are encouraged to indicate the locations (Vermillion, Sioux Falls, online) where they are interested in teaching on their letter of application.<br><br></div><div>Minimum Qualifications: M.S. or M.A. in Elementary Education, Secondary Education, Special Education, or a closely related field.<br><br></div><div>To Apply: Please provide a CV, names and contact information for 3 professional references, and a letter of application, which should include a statement of teaching interests and evidence of effectiveness. A copy of previous teaching evaluations or relevant syllabi may also be included.<br><br></div> USD-School of Education https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49327 2026-08-10T08:17:13-05:00 2026-08-10T08:17:13-05:00 Assistant Dean for Academic Programs <div>South Dakota State University is seeking an Assistant Dean for Academic Programs with the College of Agriculture, Food and Environmental Sciences. This position will manage college-level activities related to student success in the College of Agriculture, Food and Environmental Sciences (CAFES) including Scholarships, Career Fair, New Student Orientation, Academic Advising, and student engagement. Additionally, this position will oversee the academic unit of Agricultural Leadership, Education, Communication and Science (ALECS). Teaching and advising responsibilities are also included. This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The College of Agriculture, Food, and Environmental Sciences’ Office of Academic Programs oversees all academic activities within the college. This includes curriculum development (majors, minors, certificates, etc.) student recruitment and retention, scholarships, career fair and internships, and student organizations. The College of Agriculture, Food and Environmental Sciences is one of the eight colleges that make up South Dakota State University. Like the university, the college has a three-fold mission to teach, conduct research and use extension programs to serve people in South Dakota, the nation and the world. This position would contribute to supporting the college’s research and teaching efforts. In addition to the main campus in Brookings, the SDSU West River Research and Extension in Rapid City is an outreach facility of the college that supports teaching, research and extension in the western part of the state. Other locations throughout the state include eight regional extension centers, three Federally Recognized Tribal Extension Program offices and eight research field stations. The college is made up of six academic departments. Research and extension staff are distributed among the academic departments. Nearly all faculty have an appointment that is a combination of two or three of the mission areas.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>This position will lead student success activities, serve as coordinator of ALECS academic program, primary instructor for AGED 119 First Year Seminar, AFES 494 Internship and other courses as needed. They will also assist when needed in various administrative duties related to curriculum development and academic activities within the college.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in agriculture, biological sciences, educational counseling, or related field by start date.</li><li>1-3 Years of related experience in postsecondary Ag Education or closely related discipline.</li><li>Experience in advising, teaching, student success, and curriculum management.</li><li>Valid Drivers License.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Doctorate in a discipline of agriculture, biological sciences, education or related field by start date.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Ag, Food & Environmental Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49157 2026-07-27T14:39:52-05:00 2026-07-27T14:39:53-05:00 Accommodations Coordinator <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking an Accommodations Coordinator to join the Office of Accessibility. This role supports students registered with the university by coordinating reasonable and appropriate accommodations that allow full access to academic programs and services.</div><div>Under the direction of the Director of Accessibility/504 Compliance, the successful candidate will be energetic, able to work with a team, and committed to helping students strengthen their self‑advocacy and self‑reliance as they work toward their academic and personal goals.</div><div>Key Responsibilities</div><ul><li>Serve as the primary contact for students requesting accommodations.</li><li>Review medical and psychological documentation to determine eligibility.</li><li>Approve, coordinate, and monitor accommodation plans.</li><li>Provide exam accommodations, including proctoring, scribing, or reading.</li><li>Assist with accessible technology and accessible media needs.</li><li>Maintain accurate case files and documentation.</li><li>Work with faculty and staff to address accommodation needs and support classroom implementation.</li><li>Provide case management and collaborate on process improvements.</li><li>Supervise student workers who assist with accommodation delivery.</li><li>Serve as a Campus Security Authority under the Clery Act.</li></ul><div>Qualifications</div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in a related or transferable discipline.</li><li>1–3 years of related experience.</li><li>Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of individuals.</li><li>Ability to interpret documentation, manage multiple priorities, and maintain accuracy.</li></ul><div>Why This Role Matters<br>Accommodation requests continue to grow each year, and timely coordination is essential to meeting institutional obligations and supporting student success.</div> USD-Office of Accessibility https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49618 2026-09-01T14:58:54-05:00 2026-09-01T14:58:55-05:00 Carpenter - Senior Building Maintenance Worker <div>South Dakota State University is seeking a skilled and highly motivated Carpenter – Senior Building Maintenance Worker to join our Facilities and Services team. This position is ideal for an individual who takes pride in quality craftsmanship, enjoys hands-on work, and is committed to maintaining and improving the university's facilities. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>.<br><br>Facilities and Services is the internal department overseeing the growth, maintenance, repair and changes of the facilities, infrastructure and grounds of campus and satellite locations. Campus Maintenance staff have technical expertise in all trades including electrical, plumbing, carpentry, welding, mechanics, HVAC, repair work, relocation, and grounds. Services include the operation, maintenance, repair and remodeling of university buildings and grounds and the operation and repair of certain types of equipment.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:</em></strong> Installing windows, doors, framing, siding, trim, flooring, roofing, ceilings, partitions, and other building components. Replacing or repairing a variety of building elements including stair treads, handrails, ceilings, sheetrock, siding, and roofing. Remodeling spaces including demolition and construction of interior walls. Building and/or installing cabinets, shelves, frames, trim, and countertops. Reading and interpreting construction drawings and technical information.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em></div><ul><li>Experience in a variety of carpenter specialties, including framing &amp; sheetrock, flooring, trim, windows, doors, roofing (metal or shingles),</li><li>Safe work practices.</li><li>Math including geometry and fractions.</li></ul><div><em>&nbsp;</em></div><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Perform basic and customized carpentry work.</li><li>Read and understand construction drawings, as well as technical product information.</li><li>Work safely with various types of power and hand tools</li><li>Demonstrate attention to detail and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Collaborate as a contributing member in a team environment&nbsp;</li><li>Willingness to learn new things</li><li>Lift and carry up to 50 pounds&nbsp;</li><li>Work outside in extreme weather conditions</li><li>Work from heights (ladders, scaffolding, lift equipment).</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Required License:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div>Valid Driver’s License</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Application Procedures:</em></strong> SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Bldg Maint https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48661 2026-06-17T11:56:44-05:00 2026-06-17T11:56:45-05:00 Software Engineer <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking a Software Engineer to provide application, development, data, and integration support for the USD Vermillion campus. This role works closely with campus stakeholders to understand business needs, translate requirements into technical solutions, and support systems that improve operations, reporting, and data quality.<br><br><strong>This role requires working on location; remote work is not offered</strong><br><br></div><div><strong>Role Overview<br></strong><br></div><div>The successful candidate will support existing applications, develop new solutions, manage integrations and data workflows, and contribute to the university’s business intelligence and data platform strategy.</div><ul><li>Develop, test, maintain, and troubleshoot campus and statewide administrative applications, ERP interfaces, APIs, and ETL or pipeline processes</li><li>Gather requirements, define project specifications, estimate timelines and resources, and deliver solutions that align with business needs</li><li>Design and support business intelligence solutions that provide accurate, timely data for campus decision-makers</li><li>Identify, investigate, and resolve data quality issues across enterprise systems</li><li>Design, build, and maintain scalable data environments, including lakehouse technologies and Microsoft Fabric where applicable</li><li>Collaborate with administrative offices and technical partners to map processes, improve workflows, and support system changes</li><li>Coordinate with SDBOR Regent Information System staff on system-level issues, integrations, and shared initiatives</li><li>Create clear technical and process documentation for technical, functional, and leadership audiences</li><li>Provide technical guidance and mentorship to junior team members as needed</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>What We’re Looking For<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Experience with ERP systems, enterprise application development, SQL databases, API integration, ETL development, and reporting or analytics tools</li><li>Strong skills in program design, coding, testing, troubleshooting, and supporting business-critical applications</li><li>Ability to analyze complex problems, reason through technical and business constraints, and deliver practical solutions</li><li>Ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to technical and non-technical audiences</li><li>Demonstrated customer service orientation and ability to collaborate effectively with campus partners</li><li>Ability to manage multiple priorities, adapt to shifting project needs, and deliver work within defined scope and timelines</li><li>Strong attention to detail, documentation practices, and willingness to learn new systems quickly</li><li>Understanding AI concepts</li><li>Understanding of Data Analysis and Data Science</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Preferred Experience and Technologies<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Microsoft Fabric, Power BI, lakehouse architecture, and data pipeline tools</li><li>Data science, data analysis, business intelligence, and institutional reporting</li><li>Higher education systems, administrative processes, or statewide ERP environments</li><li>Project management, process improvement, and cross-functional technical coordination</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</strong><br><br></div> USD - Information Technology Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49464 2026-08-20T08:38:08-05:00 2026-08-20T08:38:09-05:00 Administrative Assistant, QE8701 <div>The Division of Biomedical &amp; Translational Sciences seeks a full-time, 12 month Administrative Assistant to provide customer service to faculty, staff, and students by supporting the academic, research, administrative and some financial functions of the Dean's office. The successful candidate will be expected to assist in both administrative and financial needs specifically assisting with purchasing, shipping and receiving, and coordinating travel for faculty, staff, and students.<br><br>The successful candidate must have strong customer service and organizational skills, be team oriented, exhibit attention to detail, have the ability to multi-task, and be comfortable with the use of Microsoft Office products specifically Word, Outlook, and Excel.</div><div><br></div><div>The <em>USD Sanford School of Medicine has announced the move of the first 18 months of the M.D. program and the Division of Biomedical &amp; Translational Sciences from Vermillion to Sioux Falls. Travel between sites may be required until the move is complete.<br><br></em>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<em><br></em><br></div> Biomedical & Translational Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49671 2026-09-04T14:00:47-05:00 2026-09-04T14:00:48-05:00 Alumni Relations Officer <div>Dakota State University is seeking an enthusiastic and creative Alumni Relations Officer to join our team. This is an excellent role for a professional who is ready to make an impact by supporting alumni engagement and strengthening lifelong relationships between graduates and DSU. <br><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong>:</div><ul><li>Develop, plan, and implement engaging alumni events and programs that connect former students with current campus life and fellow alumni.</li><li>Create and maintain communication channels with alumni through social media, newsletters, and university publications.</li><li>Collaborate with various campus departments to highlight alumni achievements and strengthen alumni engagement with university initiatives.</li><li>Assist in identifying, recruiting, and managing alumni volunteers and ambassadors for events and university outreach.</li><li>Represent the university at events and gatherings, serving as a confident and dynamic spokesperson.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree is required.</li><li>Excellent computer skills, including Microsoft Office Suite.</li><li>Creativity and innovation in developing programs and outreach efforts.</li><li>Comfortable with public speaking and presenting to groups of various sizes. .</li><li>Ability to build and maintain meaningful relationships with alumni and other stakeholders.</li><li>Effective written, oral, and interpersonal skills.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Benefits:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible benefits package – health, dental, vision, life insurance, short-term disability, hospital indemnity insurance, flexible spending account, health savings account, health reimbursement account.</li><li>South Dakota Retirement System. Employees receive 6% fully matched contributions from SDRS and are vested after three years of service.</li><li>Paid time off – full time 12-month employees earn 15 days per year of annual leave and 14 days of sick leave per year. In addition, employees receive 11 federal paid holidays.</li><li>Reduced tuition for education.</li><li>Professional liability coverage</li><li>Paid family leave</li></ul><div><br><strong>How to Apply</strong>: <br>DSU accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Please submit a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and a list of at least three references. <br> <br> For questions concerning the position, contact Alicia Entringer at <a href=\"mailto:alicia.entringer@dsu.edu\"><strong>alicia.entringer@dsu.edu</strong></a>.</div> DSU-Institutional Advancement https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49046 2026-07-20T09:38:14-05:00 2026-07-20T09:38:15-05:00 Support Services Analyst <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking an energetic and motivated Support Services Analyst to join the Information Technology Services team, providing exceptional IT support services to faculty, staff, and students. Candidate will be a member of the Service Desk team and located at the USD Vermillion SD campus. Candidate is responsible for customer support and services via phone, remote, and onsite support. Candidate will report to the Service Desk/Knowledge Manager and collaborate with other ITS personnel to follow best practices and established processes to support service offerings, resolve customer issues, and provide excellent customer service.</div><div>Responsibilities</div><ul><li>Provide customer service for IT services including installation, assessment, troubleshooting, maintenance, and upgrades of equipment and software used by faculty, staff, and students</li><li>Follow Knowledge Centered Service (KCS) process for documenting and resolving issues.</li><li>Respond to requests according to established service level agreements</li><li>Assist in project activities related to new services or service enhancements</li><li>Communicate through email, phone and in person with faculty, staff, and students to understand requirements and set expectations</li><li>Follow established processes and procedures while responding and resolving customer questions or issues</li><li>Follow established processes for creating, updating, and resolving tickets</li><li>Prioritize tasks to ensure the highest level of customer satisfaction</li><li>Provide Coyote Card Office support for USD faculty, staff, and students</li><li>Upload student, faculty, and staff information, take ID pictures and print USD Coyote ID cards</li><li>Assist with reservations for activity readers for campus events. Program and troubleshoot event reader issues</li><li>Assist with Point-of-Sale Coyote Cash devices for on campus and outside vendors</li></ul><div>Required skills</div><ul><li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills</li><li>Excellent customer service with demonstrated results</li><li>Technical background with ability to communicate with a non-technical audience</li><li>Technical experience with Windows, Apple and Microsoft applications</li></ul><div>Desired skills</div><ul><li>Familiarity with IT process management especially Knowledge Based processes</li><li>College degree</li></ul> USD - Information Technology Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49559 2026-08-27T16:30:13-05:00 2026-08-27T16:30:14-05:00 Athletics Business Manager <div>Black Hills State University is seeking applicants for an Athletics Business Manager in the Athletics department. <br><br>DUTIES: <br>• Manage the day-to-day business operations within the athletic department including but not limited to tracking departmental (sport) budgets, purchase order processing, credit card reconciliation, travel reimbursements, deposits. <br>• Assist with management and administration of athletics concessions including but not limited ordering product, setting up concession stands, overseeing money for game events, reconciling individual games, etc. <br>• Assist with the management and administration of athletics ticketing including but not limited to understanding athletic ticketing system, overseeing money for game events, reconciling individual games, reporting, etc.<br>• Ideal candidates will have excellent communication skills (both oral and written), work well with a team, assist across all areas of athletics and collaborate with campus and community partners. <br><br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: <br>• Bachelor’s degree <br>• 1-3 years’ experience <br>• Knowledge of event planning, facilities management, budgets and internal processes <br><br>COMMENTS:<br>Sponsorship is not available for this position. <br><br>TO APPLY: <br>Applications must be made online at https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Candidates will need to attach a cover letter, resume and the names/contact information of at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of September 3, 2026 at 11PM mountain time. For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may directed towards Mark Nore, Mark.Nore@bhsu.edu and 605-642-6885.<br><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Intercolleg Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/42294 2025-01-21T07:49:34-06:00 2025-01-21T07:49:35-06:00 Adjunct Instructor <div>The University of South Dakota, the state’s flagship university, is now accepting applications for adjunct clinical instructor positions in the Department of Dental Hygiene. The position is in the School of Health Sciences which houses a Bachelor of Science in Dental Hygiene program.</div><div><br></div><div>As an adjunct clinical instructor for the Department of Dental Hygiene, School of Health Sciences you will oversee the delivery of care to patients in our dental hygiene clinics by teaching and directing dental hygiene students in all aspects of the dental hygiene process of care.</div><div><br></div><div>Responsibilities:</div><ul><li>Oversee and instruct dental hygiene students in the care of patients</li><li>Laboratory, pre-clinical and/or clinical instruction to dental hygiene students</li><li>Assist dental hygiene students as they generate comprehensive treatment and prevention/management plans for their patients; ensure the treatment plans are comprehensively developed, appropriately adapted to the patients needs, and correctly sequenced to manage patient oral health needs</li><li>Work with staff, students and patients to ensure patients receive high-quality care, and students receive a clinical education that meets the standards of the Department of Dental Hygiene</li><li>Support all clinical policies and procedures of the University of South Dakota, School of Health Sciences, Department of Dental Hygiene</li><li>Attend department meetings to stay current with the Department of Dental Hygiene policies, teaching methods, and best practices.</li><li>Additional responsibilities may include committee assignments and service</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Qualifications:</div><div>Required:</div><ul><li>BSDH</li><li>Current South Dakota License, or eligible for licensure</li><li>South Dakota Certification to administer local anesthesia and nitrous oxide/oxygen sedation or eligibility to obtain certification</li><li>Healthcare Provider CPR Certification</li><li>In good standing with the State of South Dakota Board of Dentistry</li></ul><div>Preferred:</div><ul><li>MSDH or related field or current enrollment in a graduate program</li><li>5 or more years of clinical experience</li><li>Experience in preclinical or clinical teaching at accredited Dental Hygiene Program</li></ul> USD-Dental Hygiene https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49350 2026-08-11T08:53:37-05:00 2026-08-11T08:53:38-05:00 Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Veterinary Immunology <div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) Department of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences is seeking applications for a tenure track veterinary immunologist at the Assistant, Associate or Full Professor level. We are seeking an innovative educator and scientist with a research focus on mammalian food-animal infectious disease and immunological responses which will complement and enhance the current departmental research focus. This is a 9-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, SD</strong></a>.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The Department is within the College of Agriculture, Food and Environmental Sciences and the position will report to the Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences Department Head. The Department includes the Animal Disease Research and Diagnostic Laboratory (ADRDL) and the Professional Program in Veterinary Medicine; a 2+2 DVM program in collaboration with the University of Minnesota. The ADRDL is a full service, accredited diagnostic laboratory with testing capabilities spanning molecular diagnostics, food safety, virology, bacteriology, clinical pathology, parasitology, histopathology and serology. The ADRDL is a member of the Food Emergency Response Network (FERN), FDA Genome “Trakr” Program, Veterinary Laboratory Investigation Response Network (VetLIRN) and the USDA National Animal Health Laboratory Network (NAHLN) and works collaboratively with other faculty of other disciplines. There is also an opportunity to become a member of the Governor’s Office of Economic Development Center for Biologics Research and Commercialization, a collaborative center emphasizing probiotic, vaccine and diagnostic assay development. The VBSD offers excellent new or recently renovated facilities along with a highly collaborative work environment.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>The primary responsibility of this position is to develop and lead an active, independent and extramurally funded research program focused on veterinary immunology as related to infectious disease with emphasis on mammalian food animal species. Teaching an immunology course in the Professional Program in Veterinary Medicine is also an expectation, as well as educating and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and post-doctoral scientists and laboratory staff.<br><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><em>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</em></div><ul><li>Earned PhD in Biological Sciences or Veterinary Sciences; or D.V.M., V.M.D or equivalent veterinary degree AND an advanced degree in Biological or Veterinary Sciences or a closely related field with an emphasis in veterinary immunology by start date of appointment.</li><li>Ability to establish an extramurally funded research program that focuses on veterinary immunology and infectious diseases in mammalian food animal species.</li><li>Ability to establish research collaborations and work as a contributing team member.</li><li>Ability to develop curriculum and teach courses at the undergraduate, graduate and/or professional veterinary student level.</li><li>Ability or potential to publish research in peer-reviewed journals</li><li>Knowledge of food animal agriculture and production in the United States.</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><em><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</em></div><ul><li>Postdoctoral training with successful grantsmanship, peer-reviewed publication record and/or graduate student mentorship.</li><li>Experience as a course coordinator and lead instructor for undergraduate, graduate and/or professional veterinary education courses.</li></ul><div><strong><br>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, a research statement (3 page-limit, attached at “other”) and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Veterinary & Biomedical Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49219 2026-07-30T09:25:18-05:00 2026-07-30T09:25:18-05:00 Senior Administrative Assistant <div>University Housing is seeking a qualified candidate for the 12 month Senior Administrative Assistant position. The primary job responsibilities of this position include supervising student staff, processing payroll documents for over 100 department employees, coordinating with campus partners, managing housing email inbox, preparing and processing travel paperwork, and organizing data in Microsoft Excel, StarRez housing database, Banner and Blackboard.<br><br>This position requires a working knowledge of Microsoft Office Products (Word, Excel, &amp; Outlook), a high standard of confidentiality and professionalism, exceptional customer service skills, time management and organizational skills, attention to detail and the ability to work collaboratively as part of a diverse team. Knowledge of StarRez, Banner and USD policies and procedures is highly preferred.<br><br><em>This position is not eligible for sponsorship, applicants must be authorized to work in the United States.&nbsp;</em></div> USD-Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49622 2026-09-01T16:01:20-05:00 2026-09-01T16:01:20-05:00 Instructor of Communication Studies <div><strong>Position Summary: </strong><br>The Department of English, Communication, and Global Languages at Northern State University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Instructor of Communication Studies. This instructor-rank position offers the opportunity to shape the foundational communication and first-year experience of NSU students through engaged teaching and active involvement in departmental and university life. The anticipated start date is August 2027; a January 2027 start may also be considered. <br><br><strong>Minimum Qualifications: </strong><br>• Master’s degree (MA) in Communication Studies or a closely related field, conferred by the position’s start date<br>• Demonstrated university-level teaching experience in introductory communication courses Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach CMST 101: Fundamentals of Communication and FYS 101: First Year Seminar.<br><br>Beyond the classroom, the successful candidate will serve as an active member of the department and university community by:<br>• Directing student learning opportunities, including experiential learning and other applied student experiences<br>• Advising students on communication-related career pathways<br>• Building and sustaining connections with community businesses and organizations to support student learning<br>• Supporting departmental student recruitment and retention efforts<br>• Maintaining a visible, engaged presence within the department and across campus</div> NSU-Arts & Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48681 2026-06-18T10:18:11-05:00 2026-06-18T10:18:12-05:00 Coordinator of Native Student Services <div>The University of South Dakota is seeking to fill the position, Coordinator of Native Student Services. This position will work under the direct supervision of the Director of Native Student Services (NSS) and will support efforts focused on students enrolled or eligible for enrollment with a federally-recognized tribe with a federally recognized Indian tribe or who may be eligible for enrollment, with an emphasis on students from rural and reservation communities. Essential duties will include planning programs and events focused on academic culture and academic success, career readiness, and civic engagement; as well as providing mentorship to enrich the social and cultural university experience. The Coordinator will also help manage the Native American Cultural Center, support assessment and work closely with staff from across campus.</div><div><br>ESSENTIAL DUTIES &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES:</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Lead the administration, implementation and assessment of Native Student Services' programming.</li><li>Assist in managing financing resources for Native Student Services, including tracking expenditures and preparing financial reports.</li><li>Facilitate and coordinate programming that fosters an increasingly engaged, welcoming, and supportive atmosphere that nurtures achievement and success for Native Students.</li><li>Build a sense of belonging and community and assist with recruiting, retaining, and fostering the success of students from rural and reservation communities.</li><li>Serve as a bridge for strategic partnerships that will lead to programs, services, and strategic initiatives that focus on increasing the access, persistence, retention, and success of students. Principle among these are the University Housing Wiyuskinyan Unpi Tipi Living Learning Community, the Opportunity Center and TRIO Student Support Services.</li><li>Work with and support all USD faculty, staff, and students in improving awareness regarding Native Student communities, issues, and experiences.</li><li>Serve as a resource to and work collaboratively and cooperatively with other campus offices and constituencies as needed and able.</li><li>Communicate with campus Marketing to share the talent and success of students, staff, faculty, and alumni.</li><li>Advise one or more student organizations with an emphasis on Native culture and provide advisory support to non-Native student organizations with an emphasis on first generation and rural students.</li><li>Oversee Work-Study employees.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred.</li><li>Demonstrated understanding of college students from varied backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives</li><li>Experience working with students in a post-secondary learning environment, including student programming, student affairs, advising, admissions, etc.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Excellent oral and written communication skills</li><li>Ability to work independently without clear direction</li><li>An experienced collaborator within higher ed and/or departments and organizations across USD’s campus</li><li>Exceptional organizational and administrative abilities</li></ul> USD-Student Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49471 2026-08-20T12:41:24-05:00 2026-08-20T12:41:25-05:00 Assistant Director of Graduate and International Admissions <div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) is looking for a motivated and people-centered individual to help shape the future of enrollment as the Assistant Director of Graduate and International Admissions. This role will be critical in advancing the strategic enrollment management plan of the university as well as continuously helping to build the next generation of Jackrabbits.<strong> </strong>This is a 12-month, full-time ,benefits-eligible position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings SD</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Enrollment Management at SDSU serves as the primary gateway for prospective students by facilitating a smooth and transparent application and enrollment process. The unit engages in active recruitment and outreach efforts while collaborating closely with academic departments, financial aid and other administrative units to ensure a seamless experience for prospective and admitted students.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:<br></strong>The Assistant Director provides key operational support for graduate and international student recruitment through admission processing and enrollment initiatives. This position serves as a key SDSU representative to prospective students and families through recruitment territory management and coordination of recruitment activities. This role will also be responsible for developing and fostering relationships with academic departments as well as external stakeholders to the university. Above all, the Assistant Director will work to ensure that the admissions process is a positive experience from inquiry through enrollment.<br><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:<br></strong><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<br></strong><em>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</em></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree by start date.</li><li>Three or more years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, international education, or a closely related field.</li><li>Experience using CRM systems, student information systems, or related technology platforms.</li><li>Strong project management and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.</li><li>Strong attention to detail, organizational and presentation skills.</li><li>Effective written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills</li><li>Valid driver’s license and Valid US Passport, or ability to obtain both within 30 days of hire, and willingness to travel domestically and internationally and work evenings and weekends as needed.</li></ul><div><em>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</em></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, International Education, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field.</li><li>Ability to analyze data and use information to support enrollment decisions.</li><li>Experience with graduate admissions and/or international student recruitment.</li><li>Experience using Slate CRM.</li><li>Knowledge of SEVIS regulations, F-1 visa processes, and international credential evaluation.</li><li>Experience managing educational agents, international partnerships, or sponsored student programs.</li><li>Experience with mentoring, providing work direction, and/or supervision.</li><li>Experience developing enrollment strategies and recruitment plans.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:<br>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: </strong><a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Grad & International Admissions https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49362 2026-08-12T08:49:24-05:00 2026-08-12T08:49:25-05:00 South Dakota Mesonet Instrumentation Technician <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking two individuals to support the South Dakota Mesonet, South Dakota State University’s statewide network of weather stations. This position travels throughout the state to install and maintain weather stations as well as working in the lab to assemble, calibrate, and test components. Stations are relied on by the National Weather Service for the protection of life and property, so station uptime and data accuracy are critical. The position installs, configures, and troubleshoots analog and digital sensors, IP network cameras, cellular modems, data loggers, and solar power systems. This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>This position provides support to SDSU’s research and outreach program by collaborating with SD Mesonet Operations Manager and devising experimental protocol/design/setup for SD Mesonet data collection platforms, managing SD Mesonet field operations, and also providing critical support, design, programming, troubleshooting, repair, and fieldwork with complex instrumentation used to collect data. Effectively presents a positive image of SDSU in all communication and activities associated with executing the responsibilities of the position.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in science, agriculture, or engineering related field by start date.</li><li>More than 3 years of related experience in a technical field.</li><li>Commercial driver’s license (CDL) or ability to obtain within the first year of employment.</li><li>A valid driver’s license or ability to obtain within 30 days.</li><li>A commercial pesticide applicator license or the ability to obtain within the first year of employment.</li><li>Communication skills to negotiate with multiple constituents including faculty, staff, students, the general public, and farmers who are research cooperators.</li><li>Skills with developing presentations, safety policy forms and manuals, and operation manuals for SD Mesonet equipment using tools such as MS Office.</li><li>Advanced reasoning skills to solve complex instrumentation and data collection challenges with little or no availability of information.</li><li>Advanced math skills to solve complex engineering problems.</li><li>Ability to learn to operate a pickup truck pulling a trailer with a combined gross vehicle weight of over 26,000 pounds.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Ag & Biosystems Engineering https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49681 2026-09-04T17:08:53-05:00 2026-09-04T17:08:54-05:00 Assistant Coach-Softball <div>The University of South Dakota Assistant Softball Coach - Pitching is responsible for assisting the head coach in all aspects of managing a NCAA Division I softball program including but not limited to: recruitment, development and everyday training of all members of a pitching staff; assisting with training and development in other areas of team/players on and off the field; liaison for academics and other departments on campus; assisting with camp and clinics, and administration.<br><br>Qualifications: Bachelor degree required, master’s preferred. Applicants must have knowledge of a collegiate softball program, preference given to those who have D1 experience. Preferred to have knowledge of Rapsodo, Synergy or other technology to assist in development. Candidates must have excellent communication, organizational and leadership skills. Must have the ability to work responsibly with minimal supervision and the flexibility to travel, work weekends and evenings when necessary.</div> USD-Intercollegiate Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49065 2026-07-20T11:54:35-05:00 2026-07-20T11:54:35-05:00 Temporary Teacher Subs <div>USD Head Start has openings for Substitute Center Teachers and Substitute Center Teacher Aides/Food Service workers. These positions are funded by grants/other non-state funds.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Teacher Aide/Food Service Worker Substitutes: Experience working with children is preferred. Supervise children ages 3-5 in a classroom setting to replace a staff who is absent under the direction of a classroom teacher. This may involve assisting with meal preparation and clean-up, eating with children, assisting children with routines (toileting and handwashing), supervision of children during indoor and outdoor activities. Classroom locations include Beresford, Elk Point, Dakota Valley, Canton, Harrisburg, Tea and 3 locations in Vermillion.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Center Teacher Substitutes: Education or related degree and experience working with children is preferred. Substitutes will lead activities and supervise children ages 3-5 in classroom setting to replace a staff who is absent. This may involve leading large and small group activities following a lesson plan, eating with children, assisting children with routines (toileting and hand washing), and supervision of children during indoor and outdoor activities. Classroom locations include Beresford, Elk Point, Dakota Valley, Canton, Harrisburg, Tea and 3 locations in Vermillion.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Applicants must pass background checks and must provide own transportation to sites.</div> USD-Head Start https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49568 2026-08-28T09:24:30-05:00 2026-08-28T09:24:31-05:00 Equipment Technician <div>The South Dakota State University (SDState) Facilities &amp; Services Department is seeking a skilled mechanic to join the team. This position will offer support by maintaining and repairing a variety of construction, off-road, and building equipment. The equipment fleet includes everything from small engines and power equipment to lifts, loaders, generators, and air compressors that help support campus operations. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>.<br><br>Facilities and Services is the internal department overseeing the growth, maintenance, repair and changes of the facilities, infrastructure and grounds of campus and satellite locations. Campus Maintenance staff has technical expertise in electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, welding, mechanics, building repair work, relocation, and grounds. Services include the operation, maintenance, repair and remodeling of university buildings and grounds and the operation and repair of certain types of equipment. <br><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:<br>&nbsp;</em></strong>Perform skilled mechanic work on construction equipment, off road equipment, and building equipment. Routine service work, repair and maintenance of engines, brake systems, hydraulic systems, cooling systems, drive lines, exhaust, heating and air conditioning systems, minor body repairs, generators, air compressors, etc. Equipment ranges from small engines such as chainsaws to large pieces such as JLG lifts and front-end loaders as well as building generators and air compressors.<br><br><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <br><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em> &nbsp;</div><ul><li>Detailed mechanical knowledge of various equipment including diesel, gas, small engines, including electrical, steering, suspension, brake, cooling/heating, powertrain, fuel, air and hydraulic systems.</li><li>Diagnostic techniques for engines and equipment systems</li><li>Equipment maintenance and repair (i.e., automotive, loaders, skid loaders, tractors, telehandlers, UTVs, lawn and grounds care equipment, etc.).</li><li>Math skills including fractions, percentages, and geometry.</li><li>Building equipment maintenance and repair (i.e., standby generators, air compressors, etc.)</li></ul><div><em>&nbsp;</em></div><div><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Analyze mechanical issues by applying problem solving skills.</li><li>Perform routine and in depth repairs to a wide variety of equipment.</li><li>Work safely with a variety of hand and power tools.</li><li>Work in extreme temperatures and various locations including tunnels, rooftops, and agricultural sites.</li><li>Communicate clearly and have good customer service skills.</li><li>Respond to emergency/urgent issues after hours or on weekends.</li><li>Work independently with minimal supervision as well as work as a team player with a positive attitude.</li><li>Lift and carry up to 50 pounds.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Required License: <br></em></strong>Valid driver’s license is required.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Preferred Qualifications: &nbsp;</em></strong></div><ul><li>CDL class B with air brakes endorsement</li><li>Associates degree in Diesel and Automotive Technology (or similar)</li><li>At least 5 years of professional on the job experience performing mechanical repairs and service.</li></ul><div><br><strong><em>Application Procedures:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Bldg Maint https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/45050 2025-08-27T17:00:22-05:00 2025-08-27T17:00:23-05:00 Part-Time Temporary Reference and Instruction Assistance <div>South Dakota State University’s Hilton M. Briggs Library is seeking part-time, temporary reference and instruction assistance for weekend, evening (5–9 p.m.), and/or daytime shifts for up to 16 hours per week. This library faculty position supports the research needs of students, faculty, staff, and community members by providing guidance in locating resources, navigating collections, and using library services. Join a collaborative team dedicated to inspiring academic excellence, creative scholarship, and lifelong curiosity in a welcoming and resource-rich environment. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\">Brookings, South Dakota</a>.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/hilton-m-briggs-library\"><strong>The Hilton M. Briggs Library</strong></a> inspires academic excellence, collaborative endeavor, creative scholarship, student engagement, and lifelong curiosity. Serving all SDSU academic disciplines, the library is a hub for research, learning, preservation, and discovery—empowering the intellectual and creative life of the communities it serves. Its extensive collections include approximately 680,000 bound volumes, over 600,000 government documents, and 66,700 electronic journals. Reference librarians provide expert research assistance, and the library offers a variety of collaborative and individual workspaces, from classrooms and study rooms to quiet areas, couches, and tables.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>Provide in-person, chat, e-mail and phone reference service on weekends and/or evenings. Assist with library instruction and other tasks and projects as needed. Provide guidance for student employees.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>ALA-accredited Master’s Degree in Library and/or Information Science.</li><li>Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills.</li></ul><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Previous reference experience</li><li>Previous academic library experience</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>APPLICATION DEADLINE:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Applications will be accepted through October 10, 2025.&nbsp; Applications will be reviewed upon submission.&nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp; Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp; &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. &nbsp; It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students.&nbsp; This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14. &nbsp;</div> SDSU-Library https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49234 2026-07-31T10:09:58-05:00 2026-07-31T10:09:59-05:00 Controller <div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) is seeking a driven and visionary Controller to join the Accounting Department in a vital leadership role. This position not only offers the opportunity to make a significant impact on the university’s financial strategy but also provides a clear pathway for professional growth and further leadership opportunities within our dynamic team. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>This position plays a central leadership role in all aspects of university financial reporting. The successful candidate will lead and further develop a dedicated team of accounting professionals, overseeing the processing of financial transactions, preparing accurate and timely financial statements, filing tax returns, and updating and guiding finance policies. Additionally, the role involves analyzing financial data to support strategic decision-making and ensure compliance with financial standards.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><br>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</div><ul><li>Bachelors degree in Accounting, Finance, Economics or related area completed by date of application;</li><li>At least 5 years of experience in accounting or financial management;</li><li>Strong knowledge of accounting systems and Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP);</li><li>Ability to analyze financial data to ensure compliance with financial standards.</li><li>Proven ability to lead and manage staff effectively;</li><li>Demonstrated ability to prioritize tasks and manage workload to meet deadlines; and</li><li>Excellent oral and written communication skills.</li></ul><div><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</div><ul><li>CPA certificate or advanced relevant education is highly desirable</li><li>Experience in higher education or public sector accounting</li><li>Proficiency with data analysis, report writing software and advanced Excel skills</li><li>Experience in process improvement methodologies such as Lean</li><li>Demonstrated commitment to building a career within the organization, with a passion for contributing to the university’s sustained success</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Accounting Office-Controller https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49626 2026-09-02T10:01:09-05:00 2026-09-02T10:01:10-05:00 HR Program Assistant II <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is actively seeking a highly dedicated, people-centered Human Resource professional to join our team! Be a part of a dynamic team and provide exceptional customer service to the campus community. We are hiring for four HR Program Assistant II positions. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><strong>Job Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>To provide high level of customer service support for a variety of human resource activities in a Shared Service Center environment, including onboarding, validating I9s, originating EPAFs, enhanced recruitment support, and timekeeping assistance. Analytical, problem-solving, critical-thinking, technology, interpersonal, communication, organizational and customer-service skills are essential.</div><div><strong><br>Benefits</strong><strong><em>:</em></strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong><br>Knowledge of: &nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Human Resource functions</li><li>Computer software applications and systems (Word, Excel, Outlook)</li><li>Customer service practices</li></ul><div><strong><br>Skill &amp; Ability to:&nbsp;</strong></div><ul><li>Recognize discrepancies and potential problems.</li><li>Develop processes to implement program objectives.</li><li>Exercise independent judgement in evaluating situations and making decisions.</li><li>Communicate information concisely and efficiently. &nbsp;</li><li>Handle high volume of work during peak times.</li><li>Multi-task and shift focus without disrupting work production to meet competing demands/deadlines/timelines.</li><li>Understand the impact of work to employees’ access, benefits, leave and pay and to maintain the highest level of confidentiality.</li><li>Demonstrate flexibility and ability to easily adapt to change.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Application Procedures:&nbsp;</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</div> SDSU-Human Resources https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48756 2026-06-25T22:32:32-05:00 2026-06-25T22:32:33-05:00 Assistant Director, Facilities Planning and Management <div>Black Hills State University invites qualified, self-motivated candidates to apply for the position of Assistant Director, Facilities Planning and Management within the Facilities Services Department.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Director of Facilities Planning and Management provides leadership and oversight for campus facilities operations, maintenance, planning, sustainability, and capital projects. This position supports the Associate Vice President for Facilities Services in ensuring that university facilities are safe, efficient, sustainable, and aligned with institutional priorities. The Assistant Director plays a key role in strategic planning, project management, budgeting, and supervision of facilities staff.<br><br></div><div>DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:</div><div>·Assist in the planning, coordination, and implementation of new construction, renovation, and maintenance projects.</div><div>·Provide direct supervision and leadership to a team of 28 custodians, ensuring efficient and effective cleaning operations across campus facilities.</div><div>·Support daily operations of Facilities Services, including building maintenance and grounds operations.</div><div>·Oversee project budgets, schedules, and contractor performance to ensure compliance with university standards, codes, and regulations.</div><div>·Develop and monitor preventive maintenance programs and operational procedures to maximize efficiency and extend facility life cycles.</div><div>·Collaborate with campus departments and external partners to support space planning, sustainability, and accessibility initiatives.</div><div>·Supervise and mentor assigned staff, fostering a culture of safety, accountability, and professional growth.</div><div>·Assist in long-range facilities planning, including capital improvement projects and deferred maintenance strategies.</div><div>·Ensure compliance with state and federal regulations, building codes, and institutional policies. Manage space utilization and reporting, maintaining accurate building data and preparing required Board of Regents reports.</div><div>·Lead sustainability programming and events such as Earth Day, Tree Campus USA, and Go Green Pledge Month.</div><div>·Submit daily NOAA weather data and oversee campus alerts through the Everbridge notification system.</div><div>·Support emergency planning, preparedness, and continuity operations for the university.</div><div>·Assist with annual budget development and monitor departmental budgets to ensure efficient use of resources.</div><div>·Demonstrated experience supervising staff and managing budgets.</div><div>·Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills.</div><div>·Knowledge of facilities planning, safety practices, and sustainability principles in a higher education or similar environment.</div><div>·Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities effectively.<br><br></div><div>QUALIFICATIONS:</div><div>Required:&nbsp;</div><div>·Bachelor’s degree in a related field.</div><div>·Valid driver’s license and ability to travel as required.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Preferred:</div><div>-Master’s degree in a related field.</div><div>-Three years of progressively responsible experience in facilities operations, construction management, or related areas.&nbsp;</div><div>·Experience in higher education or government facilities management.&nbsp;</div><div>·Familiarity with project management software and facilities management systems.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>COMMENTS:</div><div>·This position reports to the Associate Vice President for Facilities Services. Typical work hours are Monday through Friday, 7:30am to 4:30pm, with occasional irregular hours, travel, or weekend work as needed.</div><div>·Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div>TO APPLY:</div><div>Applications must be submitted online at https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Candidates must attach a cover letter, resume, and contact information for at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of June 29, 2026, at 11:00pm Mountain Time. For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605-642-6549. Questions specific to the position may be directed to Kyle Nelsen at 605 642-6157 or <a href=\"mailto:Kyle.Nelsen@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Kyle.Nelsen@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Facility Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49475 2026-08-20T16:50:13-05:00 2026-08-20T16:50:14-05:00 Clinical Instructor of Dental Hygiene <div>The University of South Dakota Department of Dental Hygiene invites applications for a full-time (12-month, 100%) Clinical Faculty position based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. This position is part of an innovative partnership between the University of South Dakota and Falls Community Health Dental Clinic that combines academic instruction, clinical supervision, and direct patient care in a community health setting.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will supervise dental hygiene students during clinical education experiences, and deliver direct patient care during designated clinic sessions. This faculty member will play an integral role in preparing future dental hygienists while advancing access to quality oral healthcare throughout the region.</div><div><strong><br>Essential Responsibilities<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Teaching &amp; Clinical Education</strong></div><ul><li>Supervise dental hygiene students in the clinical setting while ensuring patient safety and high-quality care.</li><li>Provide instruction, mentoring, and evaluation of student clinical performance.</li><li>Facilitate student competency assessments and clinical skill development.</li><li>Participate in faculty calibration, curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation activities.</li><li>Ensure compliance with Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards, South Dakota Board of Dentistry regulations, and University policies.</li><li>Collaborate with Falls Community Health Dental Clinic staff to coordinate student schedules and clinical learning experiences.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Clinical Practice</strong></div><ul><li>Provide direct preventive dental hygiene services within the scope of South Dakota licensure during designated clinical practice periods.</li><li>Maintain accurate clinical documentation utilizing the clinic's electronic health record.</li><li>Collaborate with dentists, dental hygienists, and other healthcare professionals to provide comprehensive patient care.</li><li>Support quality improvement, infection prevention, and patient-centered care initiatives.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Faculty Service &amp; Professional Engagement</strong></div><ul><li>Participate in department, university, and community service activities.</li><li>Maintain professional licensure, certifications, and clinical competency.</li><li>Engage in professional development appropriate to faculty rank.</li><li>Demonstrate a commitment to community engagement and service.</li><li>Displays initiative and willingness to contribute to continuous improvement of clinical education and patient care.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Graduate of a <strong>Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA)</strong> accredited Dental Hygiene program.</li><li>Bachelor of Science in Dental Hygiene (BSDH).</li><li>Current South Dakota dental hygiene license or eligibility for South Dakota licensure.</li><li>South Dakota certification to administer local anesthesia and nitrous oxide/oxygen sedation, or eligibility to obtain certification.</li><li>Current Healthcare Provider CPR certification.</li><li>In good standing with the South Dakota Board of Dentistry.</li><li>Demonstrated commitment to community engagement and service.</li><li>Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills.</li><li>Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, healthcare providers, and community partners.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>Master of Science in Dental Hygiene (MSDH) or a closely related field, or current enrollment in a graduate degree program.</li><li>Three or more years of clinical dental hygiene experience.</li><li>Previous preclinical and/or clinical teaching experience in a CODA-accredited dental hygiene program.</li><li>Experience providing care in public health, federally qualified health center, or other community setting.</li><li>Knowledge of CODA accreditation standards and outcomes assessment.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Work Schedule</strong></div><div>This is a full-time, 12-month faculty position. Clinical education activities are generally scheduled Tuesday through Thursday during the academic year. The faculty member will also provide direct patient care at Falls Community Health Dental Clinic during designated clinic sessions, anticipated to average approximately one and one-half days per week (Mondays, Fridays).</div><div><strong><br></strong>This position offers a unique opportunity to combine teaching, clinical practice, and community service through a partnership between the University of South Dakota and Falls Community Health Dental Clinic. Faculty maintain an active clinical role while educating future dental hygienists, expanding access to care, and strengthening South Dakota's oral health workforce.<br><br></div><div>The University of South Dakota is committed to fostering an environment of academic excellence, collaboration, innovation, and service.<br><br>Candidates must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> USD-Dental Hygiene https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/46885 2026-02-02T15:28:12-06:00 2026-02-02T15:28:12-06:00 Talent Search Advisor <div>TRIO Talent Search at the University of South Dakota has an opening for a full time 10-month position of advisor at the Todd County and White River Schools in the towns of Mission and White River, SD and is located onsite of the schools. This position is off contract mid-June through mid-August. This position assists Talent Search participants in the identification, preparation, and attainment of their educational goals. Talent Search participants will finish high school in the standard four years, graduate, and enroll in postsecondary education the following fall.<br><br>The advisor will:<br>- Maintain a cooperative relationship with the target schools (Todd County and White River) and the communities of Mission and White River, SD through visits with students and collaboration with the schools, staff, and parents.<br>- Working in the community schools 3-4 days out of the week.&nbsp;<br>- Meet with Talent Search participants each week in class and/or small group meetings and/or individual visits.<br>- Plan and carry out activities designed to help students succeed in school, graduate from high school and enroll in postsecondary education.<br>- Provide academic assistance including study skills and goal setting activities and, encourage, conduct, or arrange tutoring as needed.<br>- Collect and disseminate information regarding postsecondary institutions, student financial aid, admissions, housing, and academic assistance programs.<br>- Arrange campus visits to colleges for TRIO Talent Search participants.<br>- Be available to meet with students' parents through letters, personal visits, parent teacher conferences or other activities.<br>- Maintain a record keeping system including student files to document student assistance and counselor activity.<br><br>Qualifications of Advisor:<br>- Education: Bachelor's degree in education, social services, counseling, business administration or related field is required<br>- Experience: Previous work with students from disadvantaged backgrounds.<br>Other Skills and abilities:<br>- Knowledge of Native American and disadvantaged student<br>populations, secondary and postsecondary education requirements,<br>and ability to relate to middle school, secondary, postsecondary students, and adults.<br>- Good communication skills<br>- Valid driver's license (to attend staff meetings and professional<br>development)<br>- Good computer skills<br>- Ability to apply education models and good teaching practices in<br>the classroom.</div> USD-Talent Search https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49383 2026-08-13T08:07:49-05:00 2026-08-13T08:07:50-05:00 Director of Community Relations <div>The Director of Community Relations serves as the University of South Dakota’s primary relationship-builder and institutional ambassador in the Sioux Falls metropolitan area. Based at USD-Sioux Falls, this position advances the university’s visibility, reputation and strategic engagement by cultivating partnerships with businesses, employers, community organizations, professional associations and industry leaders. The director identifies opportunities to strengthen connections between USD and the region, promotes university programs and partnership opportunities, and maintains a consistent presence in the community on behalf of the institution. The position emphasizes employer engagement, strategic partnerships, business relations, and support for workforce and economic development initiatives aligned with USD’s mission.<br><br></div> USD-Presidents Office https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49072 2026-07-20T16:56:30-05:00 2026-07-20T16:56:31-05:00 Athletic Trainer of Clubs Sports <div>The Wellness Center and Natatorium at USD is looking for a professional athletic trainer to assist in providing injury prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation services for our new and expanding Club Sports programs. This will include athletes competing in volleyball, soccer, baseball, powerlifting, rugby, tennis, swimming, and distance sports. This position is instrumental in helping student-athletes perform safely and successfully both in training and competition.<br><br></div><div>Qualifications: Master’s degree in sports medicine or a related field with experience in a similar position required. BOC certification required and South Dakota Athletic Trainers licensure eligible. Familiarity with University of South Dakota events preferred. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered.<br><br></div><div>This position will be appointed on either a 9-month or 12-month basis, depending on operational needs and candidate preference.<br><br></div><div>Authorization to Work: Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> USD-Wellness Center https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49580 2026-08-28T14:29:38-05:00 2026-08-28T14:29:39-05:00 Plumbing Specialist <div>South Dakota State University is seeking a Plumbing Specialist to help keep our campus running strong. We’re looking for someone who takes pride in craftsmanship and problem-solving. In this role, you’ll tackle a wide range of plumbing projects that help maintain safe, reliable facilities. We provide the tools and support to help you do your best work and continue growing in your trade. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings, South Dakota</strong></a>.<br><br>Facilities and Services is the internal department overseeing the growth, maintenance, repair and changes of the facilities, infrastructure and grounds of campus and satellite locations. Campus Maintenance staff has technical expertise in electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, welding, mechanics, building repair work, relocation, and grounds. Services include the operation, maintenance, repair and remodeling of university buildings and grounds and the operation and repair of certain types of equipment.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S.&nbsp; Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br><strong><em>Job Responsibilities:</em></strong> <br>Perform maintenance, repairs, and replacements of plumbing, heating, cooling, water, and sewer systems on campus and the local agricultural research stations. Complete remodel projects and new installations. Perform utility locates. Respond to building plumbing or utility system problems on a rotating on-call basis.<br><br><strong><em>Benefits:</em></strong> <br><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines. &nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Knowledge, Skills &amp; Abilities:&nbsp;</em></strong></div><div><em>Knowledge of:</em> &nbsp;</div><ul><li>Plumbing code</li><li>Commercial plumbing systems, including service, repairs, &amp; maintenance</li><li>New installations and remodel modifications</li><li>Functions of various plumbing, heating and cooling systems</li><li>Basic computer skills</li></ul><div><br><em>Skill &amp; Ability to</em>:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Perform installation or modification of plumbing and heating systems</li><li>Install plumbing, cooling and heating products and equipment</li><li>Repair or replace plumbing, heating and cooling systems or components</li><li>Work in confined areas or from heights</li><li>Lift and carry up to 50 pounds</li><li>Work in extreme temperatures</li><li>Communicate clearly</li><li>Ability to respond to emergency/urgent issues after hours or on weekends</li><li>Work independently with minimal supervision</li><li>Work as a team player with a positive attitude</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong><em>Required License: </em></strong>Valid driver’s license; South Dakota Journeyman’s Plumbing License.<br><br><strong><em>Application Procedures:</em></strong> SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site.&nbsp; To apply, visit:&nbsp; <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.”&nbsp; This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references.&nbsp; Email applications will not be accepted.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check. SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-Facilities & Services-Bldg Maint https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49249 2026-08-03T08:19:30-05:00 2026-08-03T08:19:31-05:00 Precision Livestock Extension Field Specialist I <div>The Agriculture Program with South Dakota State University Extension is seeking a Precision Livestock Extension Field Specialist I to provide strong statewide leadership, within their capstone area of specialization, in delivering research-based information, resources, programming, and support via learning communities while building relationships with stakeholder groups to support the vision of SDSU Extension. This position is located in<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.visitrapidcity.com/\"><strong>Rapid City</strong></a>. This position is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>South Dakota State University (SDSU) Extension is a key outreach arm of the university, delivering research-based information and educational programs that address the needs of South Dakotans. Working in partnership with academic departments and the Agricultural Experiment Station, SDSU Extension focuses its efforts in four core areas: Agriculture and Natural Resources, Food &amp; Families, Community Vitality, and 4-H Youth Development. This position is part of the Agriculture and Natural Resources program area and will collaborate closely with the Department of Agronomy, Horticulture and Plant Science, a varied academic unit with over 40 faculty specializing in areas such as agronomy, plant breeding, precision agriculture, soil science, and more. The department supports leading research initiatives, strong undergraduate and graduate programs, and a robust Extension network, creating rich opportunities for cross-disciplinary work and statewide impact.</div><div><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div><strong><br>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><ul><li>Ability to identify and monitor variables and issues important to learning community vitality.</li><li>Participates in externally funded projects led by Extension State Specialists or Field Specialist colleagues within and/or across capstone areas.</li><li>Uses cutting-edge research-based information and data in programming and collaborates on state emerging issues.</li><li>Develop relationships with all pertinent stakeholders and/or groups and influence decision making of stakeholder groups on state-wide emerging issues. Provides specialized subject matter support.</li><li>Utilizes and adapts technology in program development and delivery</li><li>Recruit and utilize volunteers to enhance educational outreach. Identify potential industry leaders to help accomplish learning community and industry goals.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div><strong><br>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>M.S. degree in animal science or closely related field by start date.</li><li>Demonstrated experience working with precision technology for livestock systems.</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively with varied audiences.</li><li>Excellent oral and written communication skills.</li><li>Demonstrated organizational and time management skills.</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills.</li><li>Experience with computer and information technologies.</li><li>Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire, and willingness to travel.</li></ul><div><strong><br>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Experience with ruminant livestock systems;</li><li>Experience in and/or knowledge of data security;</li><li>The ability to generate grants and other outside funds;</li><li>Experience translating precision technologies and/or precision data to livestock producers.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>SDState accepts applications through an on-line employment site. To apply, visit: <a href=\"https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>, search by the position title, view the job announcement, and click on “apply for this job.” This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, curriculum vitae, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div> SDSU-Agriculture Program-Ext https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49640 2026-09-02T21:11:32-05:00 2026-09-02T21:11:33-05:00 Licensed Provider QE8537 <div>This position may provide training, technical assistance, and clinical services to professionals and families in establishing evidence-based interventions for individuals with developmental disabilities. The position may be responsible for the coordination, information dissemination, and implementation of professional development training opportunities and may also coordinate other training events and participate in diagnostic clinics within the scope of their field. This is a full-time, 12-month position.<br><br>Candidates for this position should have the following qualifications:<br><br>1) Master's degree: i.e., SLP, OT, PT, Psychology, or related profession preferred. Other disciplines will also be considered.<br><br>2) Experience working with children and adolescents with special health care needs and their families, specifically Autism Spectrum Disorder and related neurodevelopmental disorders.<br><br>3) Experience working within an interdisciplinary team in the differential diagnosis of a variety of conditions.<br><br>4) Additional professional experience with clinical training, research, and supervision required.<br><br>5) Candidates with experience working with Native American communities are preferred.<br><br>Position is grant-funded. Continuation within the position is contingent on performance and funding availability.<br><br>This position offers state health insurance and benefits, which includes a retirement plan with 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and 11 paid holidays.<br><br>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div> USD-Center for Disabilities https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48824 2026-07-01T15:35:01-05:00 2026-07-01T15:35:01-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Physics <div>Black Hills State University invites applicants for an adjunct instructor in Physics to teach Introduction to Physics I and II courses online. Successful candidates must possess at least an MS in Physics or related discipline, and teaching experience in higher education is preferred.<br><br></div><div>Applications may be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7CCassie.Maser%40bhsu.edu%7C0c704c36b21747a4fa8808ded6cff90a%7C9bfcf28b3a114fd7a8138f519cdb0db2%7C0%7C0%7C639184385906322247%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=W%2FDKnJwyNve8rtuRkZHGxhynlguB720ti1HxEXuhaWY%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. Interested individuals should complete an online application and also attach a cover letter, c.v., copies of transcripts from graduate institutions, and the names and contact information of three references. For application assistance, contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Inquiries specific to the position and c.v.’s may be sent to <a href=\"mailto:Dan.Asunskis@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Dan.Asunskis@bhsu.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div><div>&nbsp;</div> BHSU-School of Natural Sciences https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49506 2026-08-24T10:47:43-05:00 2026-08-24T10:47:43-05:00 Program Assistant I <div>The University of South Dakota Business Office is seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused professional to join our team. This position plays a key role in supporting the University's financial operations by performing a variety of accounting and transactional duties while ensuring the accuracy, integrity, and timely processing of financial information.<br><br></div><div>In this role, you will primarily support accounts receivable, student accounts, and front-line customer service functions, serving as an important resource for students, faculty, staff, and external customers.</div><div><strong><br>Key Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Process and maintain accounts receivable transactions with a high level of accuracy.</li><li>Assist with student account inquiries and related financial processes.</li><li>Provide professional, responsive customer service to students, faculty, staff, and external customers.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Preferred Qualifications &amp; Skills</strong></div><ul><li>Strong customer service and interpersonal communication skills.</li><li>Knowledge of accounting principles and financial transaction processing.</li><li>Excellent attention to detail and organizational abilities.</li><li>Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining accuracy.</li><li>Experience working with Banner or similar enterprise financial systems preferred.</li></ul><div><br><em>Work Authorization: Employee must be authorized to work in the United State. This position is not eligible for sponsorship.</em></div> USD-Accounting Services https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/47635 2026-04-01T09:24:08-05:00 2026-04-01T09:24:08-05:00 Adjunct Instructor – American Sign Language (ASL) <div>Adjunct Instructor – American Sign Language (ASL)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at the University of South Dakota invites applications for a part‑time Adjunct Instructor to teach American Sign Language (ASL) courses.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Responsibilities:<br>&nbsp;The successful candidate will teach undergraduate ASL courses, which may be offered in an online synchronous format. Instruction emphasizes immersive ASL use and Deaf culture. Additional responsibilities include course preparation, student assessment, and adherence to departmental and university policies.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Required Qualifications:</div><ul><li>Demonstrated fluency in American Sign Language (ASL)</li><li>Ability to teach ASL using an immersive, visually based approach</li><li>Effective communication and organizational skills</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Preferred Qualifications:</div><ul><li>Prior teaching experience in ASL at the secondary or post‑secondary level</li><li>Degree in ASL, Sign Language Education, Deaf Studies, or a related field</li><li>Experience teaching online or hybrid courses</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Appointment Details:<br>&nbsp;This is a temporary, adjunct appointment. Course assignments are made on a semester‑by‑semester basis and are contingent upon enrollment and departmental needs.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Application Process:<br>Applicants should submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae outlining qualifications and teaching experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div><div>&nbsp;</div> USD-Communication Sciences & Disorders https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49428 2026-08-17T13:36:46-05:00 2026-08-17T13:36:47-05:00 IT Engineer <div>USD is seeking an IT Engineer to provide support to install, program, test, and maintain infrastructure systems at the University of South Dakota. The successful candidate will support hardware and software needs for the campus, work with vendors to specify hardware and software solutions and recommend enhancements to campus infrastructure and resources. This position includes on-call responsibilities. <strong>This is a 100% full time position, on campus in Vermillion, SD.</strong></div><div>Duties include working with a variety of network services, security systems, email services, directory services, configuration management products, storage systems, virtualization products, cloud services, load balancing systems, and web systems.</div><div>Responsible for:</div><ul><li>Daily service requests, break/fix work</li><li>Ensuring clear documentation is created and maintained for all infrastructure services</li><li>Monitoring performance and availability of infrastructure systems</li><li>Accurate inventory maintenance</li><li>Documenting test plans and their outcomes</li></ul><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>Networking protocols and operating systems</li><li>Client and server operating systems (Windows, Mac OS, Linux)</li><li>Cloud infrastructure and services (Azure Cloud, Microsoft 365)</li><li>Storage systems and data backup systems</li><li>Systems and Network operating Center monitoring tools</li><li>Security Technologies</li></ul><div>Ability to:</div><ul><li>Troubleshoot and repair IT infrastructure problems</li><li>Identify and implement improvements to IT infrastructure</li><li>Communicate technical concepts to non-technical users</li><li>Communicate effectively both orally and in writing</li><li>Evaluate new hardware and software for usefulness and to determine the best solution to needs</li><li>Establish and maintain effective working relationships with fellow employees, clients, and vendors</li><li>Work effectively as a team member</li></ul><div><br><strong>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position</strong></div> USD-VP for Admin & Technology https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49078 2026-07-21T14:59:21-05:00 2026-07-21T14:59:22-05:00 Assistant Director of Residential Life for Student Success <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an Assistant Director of Residential Life for Student Success in Housing and Residential Life. This position will provide collaborative leadership that advances Housing and Residential Life’s mission by cultivating environments where student communities, academic success, and belonging are central to the residential experience and on campus experience. This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota and is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.<br><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/housing-residential-life\"><strong>Housing &amp; Residential Life</strong></a> creates welcoming, supportive communities where students can thrive. Our team of professional and student staff work together to foster connection, growth, and a positive on-campus living experience.<br><br></div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.<br><br></div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div><br>The Assistant Director of Residential Life for Student Success through intentional partnerships and evidence‑informed approaches will create residential learning environments that promote holistic development, academic support and enrichment, and sustained student success<strong><em>. </em></strong>This is achieved through leading and developing student success initiatives aimed at residential students, supervision of professional live-in Residence Hall Director staff, overseeing the talent management process for the Housing and Residential Life professional and para-professional staff, and serve as the department expert on student success within the residence halls.<br><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.<br><br></div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in Student Personnel Administration, Higher Education, College Student Development, Academic Advising, Counseling, Curriculum and Instruction, or a related field, completed by start date;</li><li>At least three years of relevant work experience connected to student success, advising, leadership, campus housing, outreach, etc.;</li><li>Previous experience working in student support services, academic coaching, on campus housing (K-12 or higher education), advising, student success or outreach, service learning, or student affairs and enrollment management at an institution of higher education;</li><li>Supervision experience;</li><li>Ability to work as a contributing team member;</li><li>Valid driver’s license;</li><li>Effective oral and written communication skills; and</li><li>Effective interpersonal skills.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Demonstrated organizational and time management skills;</li><li>Relevant experiences such as student conduct experience, crisis/emergency experience, student leadership or advising experience, student success work, and/or programming experience;</li><li>Experience leading and implementing student success initiatives;</li><li>Strong leadership skills; and</li><li>Ability to motivate staff members and problem solve within a student-centered developmental model.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.<br><br></div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.<br><br></div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.</div> SDSU-University Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49589 2026-08-31T09:15:39-05:00 2026-08-31T09:15:40-05:00 CBE Research Scientist IV <div>The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at South Dakota Mines is seeking applications for a Research Scientist IV, benefited position at 100% effort. This position will be responsible for designing and executing experimental research, advising student researchers, disseminating research findings through peer-reviewed publications and scientific conference presentations, and contributing to the identification and preparation of funding proposals.<br><br></div><div>The candidate will be developing and managing the new Tissue Engineering and Cell Culture Laboratory (TECCL) as well as the Soft Matter (SoMa) Characterization Facility, overseeing budget, and serving as PI/Co-PI on research grants and contracts. This position will make continued progress in our effort to investigate tissue engineering, cell culture, materials science, microfluidics, vasculature, and soft-matter characterization, including investigations of process-structure-property-performance relations, such as our work on the deleterious effects of radiation in a human microphysiological platform. Other responsibilities will include overseeing growth of the biomedical science and engineering research in the unit, coordinating outreach efforts, and building and disseminating teaching modules.<br><br></div><div><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><div>A PhD in Biomedical Engineering or related field is required, along with at least 5 years of related experience. The applicant should have expertise in mammalian cell culture and tissue engineering, including endocytosis, mechanotransduction, cell viability, viral transfection, cytotoxicity screening, inflammatory screening, cell compatibility, and modified media formulation. Additionally, the applicant should have expertise in advanced materials characterization, advanced manufacturing (e.g., CAD, stereolithography, additive manufacturing, extrusion, or electrospinning) of polymeric materials, thin-film coatings (e.g., dip coating, blade coating), organic polymer synthesis, rheology (e.g., rotational, extensional, intrinsic), particle characterization (e.g., zeta sizing, DLS), microscopy (e.g., fluorescence, DIC, phase contrast, AFM, FLIM-FRET, SEM), and/or polymer processing and characterization (e.g., MTD, MFI, DSC, TGA). Extensive understanding of design and utilization of microphysiological systems is preferred. Experience leading large teams, mentoring at various levels, coordinating outreach efforts, teaching, grant writing, grant management, and dissemination (i.e., oral presenting and manuscript writing) are also preferred.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>To Apply:</strong></div><div>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 31, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, full curriculum vitae, and a list of three professional references (include name and email address for each reference). The cover letter should briefly describe your interest in the position and summarize the qualifications and experience that make you a strong candidate.</div> SDSMT-Karen M. Swindler Chemical and Biological Engineering 1 https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49508 2026-08-24T10:48:54-05:00 2026-08-24T10:48:54-05:00 Nutrition Aide <div>USD Head Start is seeking a Nutrition Aide for the Dakota Valley Head Start classroom. This position is 87% time for 9.5 months (mid-Aug - end of May annually) and provides food service to children ages 3-5 enrolled in the Dakota Valley Head Start program located at the Dakota Valley Elementary School.<br><br>This position serves breakfast and lunch (provided by the district,) and purchases groceries for snack then prepares and serves snack. Works directly with children and other children in classroom. This position is eligible for the full state benefits package, including health insurance, accrual of annual and sick leave and paid state holidays.<br><br>Preferred candidates will have experience working in this Head Start classroom.<br><br><em>Work Authorization: Employee must be authorized to work in the United State. This position is not eligible for sponsorship.</em></div> USD-Head Start https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49263 2026-08-04T08:46:50-05:00 2026-08-04T08:46:50-05:00 Grant Specialist I <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Office of Sponsored Programs</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Starting Hourly Rate: </strong>Minimum of $28.54 per hour, depending upon education and experience, GJ</div><div><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE: </strong>Prepare and submit external invoices, financial reports and document cost share per award terms and conditions. Complete reports and ad-hoc requests from internal and external customers. Reviews expenditures for adherence to Federal regulations, agency requirements and University policies. Provide leadership and training to post-award Grant Specialist for billings, cost share, and financial reporting. Provide Grant Accounting training to departmental administrative staff. SD Mines Financial Point of Contact to Funding agencies regarding Expenditures, Billing, Forecasts and Cost Share. Other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), practices and standards;</li><li>generally accepted auditing standards (GAAS).</li></ul><div>Ability to:</div><ul><li>interpret, comprehend and apply laws, rules and regulations for a variety of funding agencies and the State of SD;</li><li>research, compile and analyze data, providing high level of accuracy with attention to detail;</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner with students, faculty, staff and outside agencies;</li><li>communicate information clearly, concisely and accurately to others both in oral and written form, expressing ideas in a manner that the user can understand, exercising tact, patience and professional demeanor;</li><li>handle multiple tasks, prioritize accordingly and meet strict deadlines;</li><li>use a computer;</li><li>provide outstanding customer service.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>COMMENTS: </strong>Occasional travel, including overnight stays, may be required.</div><div><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin August 4, 2026. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.<br><br></div><div>Please attach a cover letter, resume and list of three professional references (including name, phone number, and email address for each reference).</div> SDSMT-Sponsored Programs https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49643 2026-09-03T08:44:05-05:00 2026-09-03T08:44:06-05:00 Facility Worker <div><strong>LOCATION: </strong>Facilities Management</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Starting Hourly Rate: </strong>$17.10 + per hour, depending upon education and experience, GC</div><div><br></div><div><strong>POSITION PURPOSE:</strong> Performs a variety of cleaning and maintenance procedures to ensure sanitary conditions are met. Duties will include maintaining hard surface floors, including sweeping, mopping, and refinishing; maintaining carpets, including vacuuming and shampooing; cleaning and maintaining buildings, including emptying waste baskets, dusting, upholstery cleaning, making minor repairs, and replacing light bulbs and tubes; cleaning and disinfecting restrooms; ground maintenance, including cleaning windows, trash collection, and snow removal; event set up and moving services; monitoring building safety and property; and other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div><strong>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES</strong></div><div>Knowledge of:</div><ul><li>custodial and grounds maintenance duties</li><li>security procedures</li></ul><div><br>Ability to:</div><ul><li>follow oral and written directions</li><li>work outdoors in all types of weather conditions</li><li>operate required equipment, a variety of motorized vehicles, and hand and power tools</li><li>perform heavy lifting up to 50 lbs. or more, physical labor including pulling and pushing</li><li>establish and maintain effective and cooperative working relationships, interacting in a supportive manner with students, faculty, staff and the public</li><li>provide excellent customer service</li></ul><div><strong><br>COMMENTS:</strong> Work Hours are day shift with some variation. Occasional weekend and holiday work may be required.<br><br></div><div><strong>TO APPLY: </strong><br>Applications must be made online at <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fyourfuture.sdbor.edu%2F&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037528736%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=BdApo8MJEf4YpIgDHYk5SxEdPYl4D1JTxXX6Lh9gb5E%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu</strong></a>. South Dakota Mines is committed to recruiting and retaining a talented workforce and offers an <a href=\"https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sdsmt.edu%2Fabout%2Foffices-and-administration%2Fhuman-resources%2Fbenefits.html&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cnancy.feiler%40sdsmt.edu%7C46c3ab97c8ab4f48dfb908de5552f813%7C867083e60b14435f9b4e8be26f01d84e%7C0%7C0%7C639042012037548093%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=po0g1l9XEBupK1HKAVP6QW5VmnZNs0BxLEiSNonMZu0%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>excellent comprehensive benefits package</strong></a> for employees, spouses and dependents; retirement plans; paid holidays; and a generous vacation and sick day allowance. Human Resources can provide accommodation to the online application process and may be reached at (605) 394-1203 or <a href=\"mailto:hr@sdsmt.edu\"><strong>hr@sdsmt.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Employment is contingent upon completion of a satisfactory background investigation.</div> SDSMT-Facilities Management https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48867 2026-07-07T12:56:21-05:00 2026-07-07T12:56:22-05:00 Custodial Operations Specialist <div>Duties include: Performs routine event set-ups and custodial duties to ensure areas within the Athletic Department are prepared for both athletic and outside events and the facilities are well maintained. Must be able to work in a team environment with different individuals. This is a fast paced environment with a need for proactive attitude and good customer service skills. Must possess knowledge of light custodial and janitorial duties. Regular and reliable attendance is an expectation.<br><br>Duties may include set-up and take-down of equipment for athletic and special events and may be required to move, lift, carry and/or arrange furniture, equipment, and other objects as needed. The duties also include but not limited to; clean and sanitize restrooms, collect and remove refuse from offices and buildings, dusting, mopping, window cleaning, carpet cleaning, waxing, scrubbing, polishing and snow removal from sidewalks and stairs.<br>Qualifications: Ability to work at heights, and include but not limited to bending/stooping, pushing/pulling, balance, climbing, squatting/sitting, twisting, grasping, and crawling. Reach at various levels from floor to overhead. Ability to move/manipulate/carry up to 50 lbs.<br><br></div> USD-Intercollegiate Athletics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48106 2026-05-11T12:56:39-05:00 2026-05-11T12:56:40-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate (Ge-STAR) <div>The Department of Physics at the University of South Dakota is seeking a highly motivated <strong>Postdoctoral Research Associate</strong> to join the <strong>Ge-STAR</strong> (Germanium-Based Science and Technology and Advanced Research) project. This position is funded by the <strong>NSF EPSCoR RII E-RISE</strong> program and focuses on the end-to-end development of high-purity germanium (HPGe) technology. The successful candidate will contribute to a multi-disciplinary team focused on <strong>HPGe crystal growth</strong>, detector fabrication, and applications spanning from fundamental physics to emerging quantum technologies.</div><div><strong><br>Key Research Areas</strong></div><div><br>The selected candidate will lead and support research activities in:</div><ul><li><strong>Detector Development:</strong> Fabricating and characterizing HPGe detectors for <strong>low-mass dark matter searches</strong> and <strong>medical imaging</strong> applications.</li><li><strong>Crystal Growth:</strong> Advancing high-purity germanium crystal growth and zone-refining techniques.</li><li><strong>Quantum Technology:</strong> Developing emerging platforms, specifically <strong>germanium hole-spin qubits</strong> and next-generation <strong>quantum sensors</strong>.</li><li><strong>AI Integration:</strong> Collaborating with AI experts to integrate machine learning and autonomous agents into the crystal growth and device development workflow.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Required Qualifications</strong></div><ul><li>A <strong>Ph.D. in Physics</strong>, Materials Science, or a closely related field.</li><li>Strong background in experimental condensed matter physics, nuclear/particle physics, or cryogenic measurements.</li><li>Experience with semiconductor device fabrication or crystal growth is highly desirable.</li><li>Excellent communication skills and the ability to mentor graduate and undergraduate students within the Ge-STAR consortium.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Appointment Details</strong></div><ul><li><strong>Duration:</strong> The initial appointment is for <strong>one year</strong>, with the possibility of renewal for <strong>two additional years</strong> (up to three years total) based on performance and fund availability.</li><li><strong>Location:</strong> Vermillion, South Dakota.</li><li><strong>Start Date:</strong> Negotiable, but an early start is preferred to align with the summer research cycle.</li></ul><div><strong><br>How to Apply</strong></div><div><br>Interested applicants should submit a CV, a brief statement of research interests, and the contact information for three references.</div> USD-Physics https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49434 2026-08-18T13:03:03-05:00 2026-08-18T13:03:04-05:00 Grounds Keeper <div>Black Hills State University is hiring a full-time Grounds Keeper to maintain the beauty and functionality of our Rapid City campus. This position plays a vital role in supporting a safe, sustainable, and inviting environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors.<br><br>DUTIES:</div><ul><li>Maintain lawns, nurseries, trees, flowers, shrubs, and irrigation systems.</li><li>Care for streets, sidewalks, and related equipment.</li><li>Remove snow during winter months.</li><li>Load, unload, and move furniture, equipment, materials, and supplies.</li></ul><div><br>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES:</div><ul><li>Strong knowledge of gardening and grounds maintenance practices.</li><li>Ability to recognize and address plant diseases and insect damage.</li><li>Capability to work outdoors in all weather conditions.</li><li>Proficiency in following oral and written instructions.</li><li>Physical ability to perform heavy lifting and manual labor.</li><li>Experience operating motorized vehicles, tools, and equipment.</li><li>Professional interaction with co-workers and patrons.</li><li>Reliable and consistent attendance.</li></ul><div><br>REQUIREMENTS:</div><ul><li>Previous and demonstrated landscaping or groundskeeping experience.</li><li>Occasional travel to the Spearfish campus.</li><li>Ability to obtain a pesticide applicator license within the first 12-months of employment.</li></ul><div><br>TO APPLY: <br>Applications for this position must be made online at http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu. Applicants must complete the online application and also attach a cover letter, resume and the names and contact information for three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of August 19, 2026 at 11PM MDT. For application assistance, contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position can be directed to Rhyse Naylor at 605.642.6147.<br><br>Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or <a href=\"mailto:Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu\"><strong>Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu</strong></a>. Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check.</div> BHSU-Buildings & Grounds https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49082 2026-07-21T15:59:07-05:00 2026-07-21T15:59:08-05:00 Assistant Director for Housing Services and Operations <div>South Dakota State University (SDState) is seeking an Assistant Director for Housing Services and Operations in Housing and Residential Life. This position will provide oversight and strategic direction for a broad portfolio for residential operations, including summer camps and conference housing, apartment contracting and occupancy management, residential communications and marketing, front desk and mailroom services and overall residential services systems.&nbsp; This position is located in <a href=\"https://www.liveinbrookings.org/\"><strong>Brookings</strong></a>, South Dakota and is a 12-month, full-time, benefits-eligible position.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/housing-residential-life\"><strong>Housing &amp; Residential Life</strong></a> creates welcoming, supportive communities where students can thrive. Our team of professional and student staff work together to foster connection, growth, and a positive on-campus living experience.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div>The Assistant Director for Housing Services and Operations will lead complex operational cycles such as student move-in/move-out, for summer transitions, guest housing, and contract management while ensuring high-quality service delivery, financial accountability, and compliance with institutional policies. In addition, this position supervises professional staff, graduate assistants, and student employees, providing training, performance management, and leadership development across multiple functional areas. The role requires strong collaboration with campus and community partners, including student services, facilities, dining, admissions, and external organizations, to support a seamless residential experience and successful conference and housing operations. The Assistant Director for Housing Services and Operations develops and executes communication and marketing strategies that enhance student engagement and promote on-campus living. Responsibilities that include on-call crisis response, student conduct support, and participation in senior leadership functions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></div><div><a href=\"https://www.sdstate.edu/human-resources/jackrabbit-way/benefits\"><strong>SDState offers a wide range of excellent benefits</strong></a> including medical, dental, and flexible benefits, retirement plans, compensation packages, paid holidays, and vacation leave. We offer a generous retirement plan that includes 6% matching, 10 hours of annual leave each month, 9.34 hours of sick leave each month, and eleven paid holidays. Employees also have access to internal and state-sponsored training as well as reduced tuition for state-supported courses at all State of South Dakota academic institutions. Relocation benefits are available per university’s guidelines.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Hospitality Management, Operations Management, Communications, Business Administration, Student Affairs Administration, Management, or related field from a regionally accredited institution. Would be willing to consider a bachelor’s level candidate with four years of directly related experience, completed by start date; &nbsp;</li><li>At least three years of progressively responsible professional experience in university housing, residential life, conference services, hospitality management, student affairs, operations management, or a related field;</li><li>Experience supervising professional and/or student staff;</li><li>Experience managing complex operational processes, projects, or programs with multiple stakeholders;</li><li>Experience providing customer service and resolving complex concerns;</li><li>Experience coordinating events, conferences, housing assignments, occupancy management, or residential operations;&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to manage multiple large-scale operational functions simultaneously;</li><li>Demonstrated organizational and project management skills;</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively with a variety of audiences;</li><li>Effective written and verbal communication skills;</li><li>Effective interpersonal and relationship-building skills;</li><li>Valid drivers license&nbsp;</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:</strong></div><ul><li>Training or coursework in project management, marketing, supervision, leadership development, or assessment;&nbsp;</li><li>Experience with summer conference and camp housing programs;&nbsp;</li><li>Experience managing front desk, mailroom, package, or customer service operations;</li><li>Experience with apartment housing or occupancy management;</li><li>Experience developing communication plans, marketing campaigns, or student-facing communications;</li><li>Experience managing budgets, contracts, billing, or revenue-generating programs;</li><li>Experience with conduct processes, crisis response, or on-call responsibilities in higher education;&nbsp;</li><li>Experience using housing management systems such as StarRez or similar enterprise systems.</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>APPLICATION PROCESS:</strong></div><div>This system will guide you through the electronic application form. This employment site will also require the attachment of a cover letter, which should specifically address how the candidate meets the qualifications as outlined in the advertisement, resume, and a reference page with the contact information for three professional references. Email applications will not be accepted. Please contact SDState Human Resources at (605) 688-4128 if you require assistance with this process.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Any offer of employment is contingent on the university’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or university policies, including but not limited to, successful completion of a criminal background check.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>SDState is a tobacco free environment. It is the policy of the University to maintain a drug-free environment and to thereby establish, promote, and maintain a safe and healthy working and learning environment for employees and students. This position is subject to South Dakota State University’s Drug and Alcohol Testing Policy 4:14.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div> SDSU-University Housing https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49601 2026-08-31T14:26:43-05:00 2026-08-31T14:26:44-05:00 Admissions Counselor <div>The University of South Dakota Office of Admissions is seeking an energetic, goal-oriented, self-motivated individual for the position of Admissions Counselor. Responsibilities include, territory management, marketing and recruitment activities on and off campus, assist in financial aid as necessary, database management, counseling prospective students and families, contributing to overall enrollment management goals, evaluating prospective students and participating in the selection of applicants for admission.<br><br>Qualifications: Bachelors degree and valid driver’s license required. Related admissions experience preferred.<br>Knowledge of The University of South Dakota campus, departments, and admission standards desirable. Ideal<br>candidates will have excellent communication skills (both oral and written), be self-starters, and have the ability<br>to be creative in developing recruiting opportunities, and be proficient in Microsoft Office.<br><br><em>This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Applicants must be eligible to work in the United States.</em></div> USD-Admissions"
    },
