l skills; dem... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice President for Research Affairs NFE03134P SDSMT-Research Affairs NFE Position Information:South Dakota Mines invites applications for the Associate Vice President for Research Affairs within the Research Affairs office. This is a regular, full-time, benefited position. This position is responsible for managing technology transfer, intellectual property, and supporting, as needed, faculty and student innovation and entrepreneurship programming. The position overs... View Details Bookmark Department Head - Biology & Microbiology F01913P SDSU-Biology & Microbiology Faculty South Dakota State University (SDState) seeks an innovative and collaborative leader to serve as Department Head of the Department of Biology and Microbiology within the College of Natural Sciences. This is a 12-month, full-time, tenure-track, benefits-eligible appointment with the academic rank of either Associate or Full Professor. This leadership position is located in Brookings, SD, serves ... View Details Bookmark Leadership Giving Officer NFE03148P DSU-Institutional Advancement NFE Dakota State University seeks a passionate relationship builder to serve as its next Leadership Giving Officer. This role is responsible for identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parents, and friends of the university capable of making gifts of $5,000 or more, helping to create philanthropic partnerships that fuel the university’s vision and strengthen its future. Require... View Details Bookmark Program Assistant I CSA02762P SDSMT-Karen M. Swindler Chemical and Biological Engineering CSA LOCATION: Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological EngineeringSTARTING HOURLY RATE: Minimum rate of $21.41 hourly, depending upon education and experience, GGPOSITION PURPOSE: The Karen M. Swindler Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) at South Dakota Mines is seeking applicants for Program Assistant I. This position will provide professional and efficient admin... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Digital Accessibility Specialist CSA02770P DSU-Information Technology Services CSA Dakota State University is seeking a temporary, part-time Digital Accessibility Specialist to support campus-wide accessibility initiatives. This position plays an important role in helping ensure that digital content is accessible to all users while supporting faculty, staff, and students in creating inclusive learning and working environments.Key ResponsibilitiesAssist with training and suppo... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 Next The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
