ng and mopping but could include ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of History F01941P NSU-History Faculty Position Summary: The Department of History and Social Sciences at Northern State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of History. This position offers the opportunity to teach and mentor students in Early American History through the Civil War era while contributing to the department’s research culture and to university life more broadly. The antici... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Researcher, QE9076 NFE03107P Biomedical & Translational Sciences NFE The Chen Lab in the Division of Biomedical and Translational Sciences (BaTS) at the University of South Dakota (USD) Sanford School of Medicine (SSOM) invites applications for a Postdoctoral Fellow position in the field of Cardiovascular Regenerative Engineering, Medicine, and Technology, with a translational research focus. The fellow will work with Dr. William C.W. Chen and his team at USD an... View Details Bookmark Department Assistant (QE9678) CSA02796P Dean of Medical Student Affairs CSA The Office of Medical Student Affairs is a great place to make a difference!This student-centered department is seeking a highly motivated, detail oriented support person to join its close-knit team. The position will assist with managing the MSA office and providing administrative support to the Senior Academic Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, the SSOM financial aid office and play a vital... View Details Bookmark Digital Accessibility Specialist NFE03153P USD-Office of Accessibility NFE The Digital Accessibility Specialist helps ensure that university technology, digital content, and services are accessible to all users. This position provides support and training on assistive technology, evaluates digital content for accessibility compliance, and partners with departments across campus to promote accessibility best practices.Key ResponsibilitiesSupport students, faculty, and ... View Details Bookmark Head Start Teacher Aide CSA02768P USD-Head Start CSA USD Head Start is seeking a caring, energetic Teacher Aide to join our Head Start classroom in the Tea School District.In this role, you’ll support a positive, engaging learning environment for children ages 3–5 and work closely with the Head Start Teacher to help each child reach important developmental milestones.What You’ll DoSupervise children in the classroom and on the playgroundSupport d... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 Next The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
